      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "key = nn.Linear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Model::addernetmatmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: K projection",
        "- **addernetmatmul**: `AdderConvLinear` (Toeplitz\u2013convolution with L1-distance)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "key = AdderConvLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Model::matmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: V projection",
        "- **matmul**: `nn.Linear(emb_dim, head_sz)`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "value = nn.Linear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Model::addernetmatmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: V projection",
        "- **addernetmatmul**: `AdderConvLinear` (Toeplitz\u2013convolution with L1-distance)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "value = AdderConvLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(batch_sz, ctx_len, emb_dim)\n",
        "q = query(x)\n",
        "k = key(x)\n",
        "v = value(x)\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Model::matmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: Attention scores",
        "- **matmul**: `q @ k^T / sqrt(d_k)`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "k_q_sim = q @ k.transpose(2, 1) / np.sqrt(head_sz)\n",
        "print(f\"{k_q_sim.shape=}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Model::addernetmatmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: Attention scores",
        "- **addernetmatmul**: Toeplitz\u2013convolution with L1-distance (`-|q - k| / sqrt(d_k)`)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "k_q_sim = -(q.unsqueeze(2) - k.unsqueeze(1)).abs().sum(-1) / np.sqrt(head_sz)\n",
        "print(f\"{k_q_sim.shape=}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "tril = torch.tril(torch.ones(ctx_len, ctx_len))\n",
        "k_q_sim = k_q_sim.masked_fill(tril == 0, float(\"-inf\"))\n",
        "attn_weights = F.softmax(k_q_sim, dim=2)\n",
        "print(f\"{attn_weights.shape=}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Model::matmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: Attention output",
        "- **matmul**: `attn_weights @ v`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "attn_out = attn_weights @ v\n",
        "print(f\"{attn_out.shape=}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Model::addernetmatmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: Attention output",
        "- **addernetmatmul**: Toeplitz\u2013convolution with L1-distance (`-|attn_weights - v|`)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "attn_out = -(attn_weights.unsqueeze(-1) - v.unsqueeze(2)).abs().sum(dim=2)\n",
        "print(f\"{attn_out.shape=}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Head \u2013 Single Self-Attention Head",
        "Each head implements its own Q, K, V projections, attention scores, and output."
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Attn::vanillaatten{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Standard self-attention",
        "Scaled dot-product attention with a causal mask: each position attends to itself and earlier positions."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Attn::mqa{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Multi-Query Attention (Shazeer 2019)",
        "All query heads share a single key/value head, so the KV cache shrinks by the number of heads.",
        "Each head below accepts an optional shared `kv`; the sharing itself is wired up in `MultiHead`."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Attn::gqa{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Grouped-Query Attention (Ainslie et al. 2023)",
        "Query heads are split into groups that share key/value heads: fewer KVs than full multi-head attention,",
        "more than single-query attention. Group routing is wired up in `MultiHead`."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Attn::mla{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Multi-head Latent Attention (DeepSeek-AI 2024)",
        "Keys and values are low-rank: inputs are compressed to a small latent vector that is cached,",
        "then projected back up per head. Queries stay full-rank."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Attn::dsa{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Sparse attention (DeepSeek NSA-inspired)",
        "On top of the causal mask, each query keeps a local window plus strided distant positions,",
        "then filters to the top-k scores before the softmax. Near-dense on tiny contexts; pays off at long ones."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Attn::tokenformer{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Token-parameter attention (TokenFormer, Wang et al. 2025)",
        "Linear projections are replaced by attention over learnable parameter tokens: input tokens act as queries",
        "while parameters serve as keys and values. Capacity grows by adding new key-value parameter pairs,",
        "so the model scales without retraining from scratch."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Attn::tpa{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Tensor Product Attention (Zhang et al. 2026)",
        "Each projection is factorized as a sum of R rank-1 tensor products: a compact mixing factor times",
        "token features. Only the small factors need caching, and the factorization composes with rotary",
        "position embeddings, unlike KV-compression approaches."
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Projection and score functions",
        "Defined once here and reused by every attention module below."
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Model::matmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"Standard projections and dot-product scores.\"\"\"\n",
        "QKVLinear = nn.Linear\n",
        "def attn_scores(q, k):\n",
        "    return q @ k.transpose(-2, -1)\n",
        "def attn_combine(wei, v):\n",
        "    return wei @ v\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Model::addernetmatmul{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"AdderNet projections and L1 scores (no multiplies).\"\"\"\n",
        "QKVLinear = AdderConvLinear\n",
        "def attn_scores(q, k):\n",
        "    return -(q.unsqueeze(-1) - k.unsqueeze(-2)).abs().sum(-1)\n",
        "def attn_combine(wei, v):\n",
        "    return -(wei.unsqueeze(-1) - v.unsqueeze(-2)).abs().sum(-2)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"Single self-attention head.\"\"\"\n",
        "class Head(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, head_sz, emb_dim):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.head_sz, self.emb_dim = head_sz, emb_dim\n",
        "        self.key = QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.query = QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.value = QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n",
@Impl::Attn::mla{
        "        # MLA latent projections (used instead of key/value)\n",
        "        self.kv_down = QKVLinear(emb_dim, max(16, head_sz // 2), bias=False)\n",
        "        self.k_up = QKVLinear(max(16, head_sz // 2), head_sz, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.v_up = QKVLinear(max(16, head_sz // 2), head_sz, bias=False)\n",
}@}
@Impl::Attn::tokenformer{
        "        # Token-parameter tokens: p_keys (n', d_model), p_values (n', d_head) (Tseng et al. Eq.4)\n",
        "        self.p_keys = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(64, emb_dim) * 0.02)\n",
        "        self.p_values = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(64, head_sz) * 0.02)\n",
}@}
@Impl::Attn::tpa{
        "        # TPA: each projection is a sum of R rank-1 tensor products (Zhang et al. 2026)\n",
        "        self.tpa_rank = 2\n",
        "        self.a_q = QKVLinear(emb_dim, self.tpa_rank, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.b_q = nn.ModuleList([QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False) for _ in range(self.tpa_rank)])\n",
        "        self.a_k = QKVLinear(emb_dim, self.tpa_rank, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.b_k = nn.ModuleList([QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False) for _ in range(self.tpa_rank)])\n",
        "        self.a_v = QKVLinear(emb_dim, self.tpa_rank, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.b_v = nn.ModuleList([QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False) for _ in range(self.tpa_rank)])\n",
}@}
        "        self.register_buffer(\"tril\", torch.tril(torch.ones(ctx_len, ctx_len)))\n",
@Impl::Attn::slidingwindow{
        "        # Sliding window (Beltagy et al. 2020): self-attention only within W previous positions\n",
        "        self.window = 32\n",
}@}
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x, kv=None):\n",
        "        B, T, C = x.shape\n",
        "        q = self.query(x)\n",
        "        k = self.key(x)\n",
        "        v = self.value(x)\n",
@Impl::Attn::mla{
        "        c = self.kv_down(x)\n",
        "        k = self.k_up(c)\n",
        "        v = self.v_up(c)\n",
}@}
@Impl::Attn::tpa{
        "        # TPA: rebuild q/k/v from rank-R factors (mean over R outer products)\n",
        "        aq = self.a_q(x)\n",
        "        bq = torch.stack([l(x) for l in self.b_q], dim=-1)\n",
        "        q = (aq.unsqueeze(-2) * bq).sum(-1) / self.tpa_rank\n",
        "        ak = self.a_k(x)\n",
        "        bk = torch.stack([l(x) for l in self.b_k], dim=-1)\n",
        "        k = (ak.unsqueeze(-2) * bk).sum(-1) / self.tpa_rank\n",
        "        av = self.a_v(x)\n",
        "        bv = torch.stack([l(x) for l in self.b_v], dim=-1)\n",
        "        v = (av.unsqueeze(-2) * bv).sum(-1) / self.tpa_rank\n",
}@}
        "        if kv is not None:\n",
        "            k, v = kv\n",
        "        wei = attn_scores(q, k) * (self.head_sz ** -0.5)\n",
        "        wei = wei.masked_fill(self.tril[:T, :T] == 0, float(\"-inf\"))\n",
@Impl::Attn::slidingwindow{
        "        # restrict attention to the last W positions (Beltagy et al. Eq.2)\n",
        "        idx_w = torch.arange(T, device=x.device)\n",
        "        band = (idx_w.unsqueeze(1) - idx_w.unsqueeze(0) >= 0) & (idx_w.unsqueeze(1) - idx_w.unsqueeze(0) < self.window)\n",
        "        wei = wei.masked_fill(~band, float(\"-inf\"))\n",
}@}
@Impl::Attn::dsa{
        "        idx = torch.arange(T, device=x.device)\n",
        "        local = (idx.unsqueeze(1) - idx.unsqueeze(0) < 32)\n",
        "        strided = ((idx.unsqueeze(0) - idx.unsqueeze(1)) % 8 == 0)\n",
        "        wei = wei.masked_fill(~((self.tril[:T, :T] > 0) & (local | strided)), float(\"-inf\"))\n",
        "        k_top = min(32, T)\n",
        "        topv, _ = wei.topk(k_top, dim=-1)\n",
        "        wei = wei.masked_fill(wei < topv[..., -1].unsqueeze(-1), float(\"-inf\"))\n",
}@}
        "        wei = F.softmax(wei, dim=-1)\n",
        "        out = attn_combine(wei, v)\n",
@Impl::Attn::tokenformer{
        "        # Token-parameter attention (Tseng et al. Eq.4): out = GeLU(L2norm(x) @ p_keys^T) @ p_values overrides v\n",
        "        p_k = self.p_keys.unsqueeze(0).expand(B, -1, -1)\n",
        "        p_v = self.p_values.unsqueeze(0).expand(B, -1, -1)\n",
        "        theta = F.gelu(F.normalize(x, dim=-1) @ p_k.transpose(1, 2))\n",
        "        out = theta @ p_v\n",
}@}
        "        return out\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Attn::vanillaatten{
    @Impl::Attn::linearatten{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "\"\"\"Linear-attention Head (Katharopoulos et al., arXiv:2006.16236; survey \u00a73.4/Table 5).\n",
        "\n",
        "Subclass of the existing Head: reuses key/query/value projections (ONLY the\n",
        "scoring changes). Forward is the kernel recurrence quoted in \u00a73.4:\n",
        "V'_i = (phi(Q_i)^T S_i)/(phi(Q_i)^T Z_i), S_i = sum_j phi(K_j) V_j^T,\n",
        "Z_i = sum_j phi(K_j); phi = elu+1 applied elementwise. Causal by\n",
        "construction (cumulative sums); per-step O(d^2), total O(T) (Table 5).\"\"\"\n",
        "class LinearAttnHead(Head):\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        q = self.query(x)\n",
        "        k = self.key(x)\n",
        "        v = self.value(x)\n",
        "        qf = _t27.nn.functional.elu(q) + 1.0\n",
        "        kf = _t27.nn.functional.elu(k) + 1.0\n",
        "        B, T, D = q.shape\n",
        "        S = _t27.zeros(B, D, D, device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)\n",
        "        z = _t27.zeros(B, D, 1, device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)\n",
        "        outs = []\n",
        "        for t in range(T):\n",
        "            kt = kf[:, t:t + 1, :]\n",
        "            vt = v[:, t:t + 1, :]\n",
        "            S = S + kt.transpose(1, 2) @ vt\n",
        "            z = z + kt.transpose(1, 2)\n",
        "            qt = qf[:, t:t + 1, :]\n",
        "            outs.append((qt @ S) / (qt @ z).clamp_min(1e-6))\n",
        "        return _t27.cat(outs, dim=1)\n"
      ]
    }
    }@},
    @Impl::Attn::loglinearatten{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "\"\"\"Log-linear-attention Head (Guo et al., arXiv:2506.04761; survey \u00a73.4/Fig.12/Table 5).\n",
        "\n",
        "Subclass of the existing Head: reuses projections; past tokens accumulate in\n",
        "a streaming Fenwick structure (power-of-two buckets that merge on insert, so\n",
        "the prefix [0..t] is always covered by O(log t) buckets). Per-survey output:\n",
        "o_t = sum_l lam^(l) q_t^T S_t^(l); lam by bucket size = 1/bitlen(size) is a\n",
        "recency stand-in (documented: the paper learns bucket weights). Per-step\n",
        "working set O(log T); total O(T log T) (Table 5).\"\"\"\n",
        "class LogLinearAttnHead(Head):\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        q = self.query(x)\n",
        "        k = self.key(x)\n",
        "        v = self.value(x)\n",
        "        B, T, D = q.shape\n",
        "        buckets = []\n",
        "        outs = []\n",
        "        for t in range(T):\n",
        "            kt = k[:, t:t + 1, :]\n",
        "            vt = v[:, t:t + 1, :]\n",
        "            buckets.append([1, kt.transpose(1, 2) @ vt])\n",
        "            while len(buckets) >= 2 and buckets[-1][0] == buckets[-2][0]:\n",
        "                s2, S2 = buckets.pop()\n",
        "                s1, S1 = buckets.pop()\n",
        "                buckets.append([s1 + s2, S1 + S2])\n",
        "            qt = q[:, t:t + 1, :]\n",
        "            num = 0\n",
        "            for s, S in buckets:\n",
        "                lam = 1.0 / int(s).bit_length()\n",
        "                num = num + lam * (qt @ S)\n",
        "            outs.append(num)\n",
        "        return _t27.cat(outs, dim=1)\n"
      ]
    }
    }@},
    @Impl::Attn::locallinearatten{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "\"\"\"Local-linear-attention Head (Zuo et al., arXiv:2510.01450 Eq.6-8, 13-16).\n",
        "\n",
        "Subclass of the existing Head: reuses projections. Per query q_i, a\n",
        "query-centered ridge regression (Eq.6) is fit on the CAUSAL history with\n",
        "query-dependent kernel weights w_ij = exp(q_i.k_j / h), h = sqrt(d)\n",
        "(softmax-analog bandwidth; fully causal range - the paper's sliding\n",
        "windows are future work, its Sec.5). Implementation follows the matrix\n",
        "form Eq.14-16 with the matrix-free CG solve of Eq.13 (small scale,\n",
        "dense-prototype intend): W = tril(exp(QK^T/h)); M = WK - brsum(W).Q (mu);\n",
        "R = CGSolve(M, Q, K, lambda) (rho); delta = omega - rsum(M.R);\n",
        "O = ((1 - relmm(R,Q,K)) / bcast(delta) . W) V with relmm = RK^T - brsum(R.Q).\n",
        "Cost: expected - heavier than softmax per head (no FLOP claim).\"\"\"\n",
        "class LocalLinearAttnHead(Head):\n",
        "    def _cgsolve(self, W, M, Q, K, lam, iters=12):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Matrix-free CG on Sigma_i p (Eq.13), batched over (B, T).\"\"\"\n",
        "        omega = W.sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        def Aop(p):\n",
        "            Kp = p @ K.transpose(-2, -1)\n",
        "            t1 = (W * Kp) @ K\n",
        "            qp = (p * Q).sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "            Mp = (M * p).sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
            "            return (t1 - qp * M - Mp * Q\n",
            "                    - (qp * omega) * Q + lam * p)\n",
        "        x = _t27.zeros_like(M)\n",
        "        r = M - Aop(x)\n",
        "        p = r\n",
        "        rs = (r * r).sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        for _ in range(iters):\n",
        "            Ap = Aop(p)\n",
        "            alpha = rs / (Ap * p).sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "            x = x + alpha * p\n",
        "            r = r - alpha * Ap\n",
        "            rs_new = (r * r).sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "            p = r + (rs_new / rs.clamp_min(1e-12)) * p\n",
        "            rs = rs_new\n",
        "        return x\n",
        "    def forward(self, x, ridge=1e-3):\n",
        "        q = self.query(x)\n",
        "        k = self.key(x)\n",
        "        v = self.value(x)\n",
        "        B, T, D = q.shape\n",
        "        lam = ridge\n",
        "        h = float(D) ** 0.5\n",
        "        tril = self.tril[:T, :T]\n",
        "        W = (q @ k.transpose(-2, -1) / h).masked_fill(tril == 0, float(\"-inf\"))\n",
        "        W = W.exp() * tril\n",
        "        omega = W.sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        M = W @ k - omega * q\n",
        "        R = self._cgsolve(W, M, q, k, lam)\n",
        "        delta = (omega - (M * R).sum(-1, keepdim=True)).clamp_min(1e-6)\n",
        "        zk = R @ k.transpose(-2, -1) - (R * q).sum(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        S = (1.0 - zk) / delta * W\n",
        "        return S @ v\n"
      ]
    }
    }@},
    @Impl::Attn::kimilinear{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "\"\"\"KIMI-linear KDA Head (Kimi Team, arXiv:2510.26692; survey \u00a73.4/Table 5).\n",
        "\n",
        "Subclass of the existing Head: reuses key/query/value projections and adds\n",
        "ONLY the two small gating nets (forget gate alpha, update rate beta). Memory:\n",
        "S_t = (I - b_t k_t k_t^T) Diag(a_t) S_{t-1} + b_t k_t v_t^T; o_t = S_t^T q_t.\n",
        "Gates are untrained at small scale (the paper trains them) - documented;\n",
        "the recurrence, chunking note, and 3:1 KDA/full hybrid ratio are recorded in\n",
        "\u00a727 reasoning. Per-step O(d^2), O(1) state (Table 5).\"\"\"\n",
        "class KimiLinearHead(Head):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, head_sz, emb_dim):\n",
        "        super().__init__(head_sz, emb_dim)\n",
        "        self.kda_a = QKVLinear(emb_dim, head_sz, bias=False)\n",
        "        self.kda_b = QKVLinear(emb_dim, 1, bias=False)\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        q = self.query(x)\n",
        "        k = self.key(x)\n",
        "        v = self.value(x)\n",
        "        B, T, D = q.shape\n",
        "        al = _t27.sigmoid(self.kda_a(x))\n",
        "        be = _t27.sigmoid(self.kda_b(x)).squeeze(-1)\n",
        "        S = _t27.zeros(B, D, D, device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)\n",
        "        I = _t27.eye(D, device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)\n",
        "        outs = []\n",
        "        for t in range(T):\n",
        "            a = al[:, t, :]\n",
        "            b = be[:, t].view(B, 1, 1)\n",
        "            kt = k[:, t, :]\n",
        "            vt = v[:, t, :]\n",
        "            qt = q[:, t, :]\n",
        "            DaS = a.unsqueeze(-1) * S\n",
        "            kk = kt.unsqueeze(-1) * kt.unsqueeze(-2)\n",
        "            S = (I - b * kk) @ DaS + b * kt.unsqueeze(-1) * vt.unsqueeze(-2)\n",
        "            outs.append(((S.transpose(1, 2) @ qt.unsqueeze(-1)).squeeze(-1)).unsqueeze(1))\n",
        "        return _t27.cat(outs, dim=1)\n"
      ]
    }
    }@},
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Multi-Head Self-Attention Demo"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Attn::vanillaatten{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"Multi-head self-attention demo.\"\"\"\n",
        "n_heads = 2\n",
        "heads = nn.ModuleList([Head(head_sz, emb_dim) for _ in range(n_heads)])\n",
        "attn_outs = [head(x) for head in heads]\n",
        "attn_out = torch.cat(attn_outs, dim=2)\n"
      ]
    },
