        "### Backprop: TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21) x the first paper (arXiv:1706.03762, foundation; no prior line touched)",
        "",
        "- **Refines the Relations verdict `vs Attention: NONE` - mechanism-wise none, substrate-wise total.** TASCO computes entirely on the first paper's primitive trio: scaled dot-product attention under the causal tril mask (`attn_scores`/`attn_combine`), `QKVLinear` projections, and the position table. Teacher log-likelihood is a gather over the same log_softmax head; every RP/SAP prefix steer acts through the k/v inputs to untouched attention math. From the first paper's perspective: the last paper is a weight-frozen consumer of its forward - the connection is real but lives below the mechanism layer, which is why the mechanism-level NONE stays true.",
        "- **What can be changed considering both (levers; additive, none claimed as run):** (1) the rho/sigma estimator (`tasco_rp_loss`, s21) perturbs `prefix.V` by `.data.add_` plus K noisy re-decodes; the first paper's autograd through the same softmax path can replace it with one exact d loglik/dV backward - fewer evals, lower variance, no sigma tuning. (2) every KV compress/evict/place @Impl re-shapes exactly what TASCO perturbs: measuring rho under each policy selects prefixes that keep teacher stability under compressed KV (a joint knob neither paper had alone). (3) the mmlu-suite MC scorer (s28) is a cheap on-path prefix-quality gauge, so prefix work gains an accuracy readout with no extra downloads.",
        "- **Future directions to make them more compatible:** expose `prefix.V` as a differentiable buffer so RP/SAP and every KV @Impl share one gradient path; persist optimized prefixes next to checkpoints so cross-path transfer (tiny64/124m/any-ctx) re-uses the same prefix objects; generalize decoding from greedy argmax to the foundation's sampling/temperature softmax so prefix quality is measured off-path too. Boundary kept: prefixes steer the forward, never the weights (NEVER-SAME-PATH).",
