      "source": [
        "## 23. Shared Circuits \\u2013 Shared circuits predict whether LLMs generalize across formats in arithmetic reasoning (de Varda, Pandey, Han, Andreas, Fedorenko 2026, arXiv:2609.04463v1)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** LLMs solve numeric arithmetic (44 + 22 =) far better than verbal renditions of the same problems (forty-four plus twenty-two equals / cuarenta y cuatro m\\u00e1s veintid\\u00f3s es igual a / quarantaquattro pi\\u00f9 ventidue fa). Using attribution patching (Eq.1 preference from the model's OWN greedy answers, Eq.2 rescaling to 1 on x and 0 on the sign-flipped x', Eq.3 attrib=(a(x)-a(x')) grad M at the last prompt token), the paper localizes each model's numeric circuit S_m (top 1% of MLP units) and shows overlap with it predicts generalization at three levels: format difficulty (Jaccard .145/.078/.069 vs accuracy 36.4/17.9/6.8%), best-generalizing models (r=.75/.58/.47), and item correctness (point-biserial medians .38/.32/.29), matching supervised probes with no labels. App C confirms causality by clean-over-corrupted patching; App D shows loading adds unique R2 beyond probes and entropy (LMG); App E shows S_incorrect predicts nothing; App F shows any accuracy-balanced anchor works.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** no public code for this paper exists anywhere (0 issues reviewable) - text-faithful. The paper reuses Han et al. 2026 = github.com/Pengrui-Han/LLM_Modularity (0 issues, 0 PRs): our Eq.3 reduction `g*(clean-corr)` at the last prompt token and the `down_proj.input` hook site match `src/attribution.py::run_neuron_attribution` verbatim; the six divergences (top-1% not 0.1%, Jaccard not intersection/k, own answers not gold, keep-all-items filter, clean-over-corrupted patching not ablation, 4 formats of 1 task) are all implemented the paper's way (graded 11_RepoAudit).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): no new Technique.** Everything here is readout-side analysis on frozen states (hooks on `blocks[l].ffwd.net[2]`, the post-activation MLP hidden units = the paper's scored units) plus a training corpus that feeds the UNCHANGED NanoGPT class. The anchor format is looped, not pathed; exposure mixes are experimental configs, not compiled-artifact differences. Plain ALWAYS-PRESENT codeblocks by design, valid on every Model/State/Arch/Attn combo (the hook site exists in matmul and addernet FeedForwards alike).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) char65 has no digits except '3' and no '+/=' (audit: `sorted(set(open('data/tiny_shakespeare.txt').read()))`), so the numeric renderer remaps digits 0-9 to a-j, '+' to 'P', '=' to 'Q' ('-' and space are native) - same positional arithmetic, vocab-safe alphabet; verbal renderers use native lowercase + hyphen. Accents are ASCII-folded (mas/ventidos/piu). (2) The paper's asymmetry comes from pretraining exposure; ours comes from training exposure (numeric-majority + English-minority, Spanish/Italian unseen) - the controlled analogue, stated in the runner. (3) Answers are sign-aware fixed-width (`P0066`/`-0022`, width 5) so the answer span sits at a deterministic offset like s16. (4) s16 lesson applied: `token_to_int.get(c, 0)` silently collapses out-of-vocab chars to newline, which destroys s16's digit/operator information (only '3' survives; '+/=/*\/|' all become newline) - s23 asserts zero unknown chars instead of inheriting the collapse (s16 fix proposed, not applied here).\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT shared-circuits alphabet + renderers + item generator | Paper s2.1 (four renderings, 2-3 digit operands, 2-3 terms, 50/50, half carry, sign-flip partner) + App B (own answers, length filter) | graded 11_Setup/11_Fig1_Pipeline | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Vocab-safe numeric alphabet (char65 audit: only '3' of 0-9, no '+/='): digits \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"0-9 -> a-j, '+' -> 'P', '=' -> 'Q'; '-' and ' ' are native. Verbal formats \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"use native lowercase + hyphen; accents ASCII-folded (mas/piu).\"\"\"\n",
        "SC_DIG = {str(d): chr(ord(\"a\") + d) for d in range(10)}\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_sym_num(s):\n",
        "    out = []\n",
        "    for c in s:\n",
        "        if c in SC_DIG:\n",
        "            out.append(SC_DIG[c])\n",
        "        elif c == \"+\":\n",
        "            out.append(\"P\")\n",
        "        elif c == \"=\":\n",
        "            out.append(\"Q\")\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            out.append(c)\n",
        "    return \"\".join(out)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_words_en():\n",
        "    ones = [\"zero\", \"one\", \"two\", \"three\", \"four\", \"five\", \"six\", \"seven\", \"eight\",\n",
        "            \"nine\", \"ten\", \"eleven\", \"twelve\", \"thirteen\", \"fourteen\", \"fifteen\",\n",
        "            \"sixteen\", \"seventeen\", \"eighteen\", \"nineteen\"]\n",
        "    tens = {20: \"twenty\", 30: \"thirty\", 40: \"forty\", 50: \"fifty\", 60: \"sixty\",\n",
        "            70: \"seventy\", 80: \"eighty\", 90: \"ninety\"}\n",
        "    out = {n: ones[n] for n in range(20)}\n",
        "    for d, b in tens.items():\n",
        "        out[d] = b\n",
        "        for n in range(1, 10):\n",
        "            out[d + n] = b + \"-\" + ones[n]\n",
        "    for h in range(1, 10):\n",
        "        out[100 * h] = ones[h] + \" hundred\"\n",
        "        for r in range(1, 100):\n",
        "            out[100 * h + r] = ones[h] + \" hundred \" + out[r]\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_words_es():\n",
        "    ones = [\"cero\", \"uno\", \"dos\", \"tres\", \"cuatro\", \"cinco\", \"seis\", \"siete\",\n",
        "            \"ocho\", \"nueve\", \"diez\", \"once\", \"doce\", \"trece\", \"catorce\", \"quince\",\n",
        "            \"dieciseis\", \"diecisiete\", \"dieciocho\", \"diecinueve\"]\n",
        "    tens = {20: \"veinte\", 30: \"treinta\", 40: \"cuarenta\", 50: \"cincuenta\",\n",
        "            60: \"sesenta\", 70: \"setenta\", 80: \"ochenta\", 90: \"noventa\"}\n",
        "    out = {n: ones[n] for n in range(20)}\n",
        "    for d, b in tens.items():\n",
        "        out[d] = b\n",
        "        for n in range(1, 10):\n",
        "            out[d + n] = b + \" y \" + ones[n]\n",
        "    hund = {1: \"ciento\", 2: \"doscientos\", 3: \"trescientos\",\n",
        "            4: \"cuatrocientos\", 5: \"quinientos\", 6: \"seiscientos\",\n",
        "            7: \"setecientos\", 8: \"ochocientos\", 9: \"novecientos\"}\n",
        "    out[100] = \"cien\"\n",
        "    for h in range(2, 10):\n",
        "        out[100 * h] = hund[h]\n",
        "    for h in range(1, 10):\n",
        "        for r in range(1, 100):\n",
        "            out[100 * h + r] = hund[h] + \" \" + out[r]\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_words_it():\n",
        "    ones = [\"\", \"uno\", \"due\", \"tre\", \"quattro\", \"cinque\", \"sei\", \"sette\", \"otto\",\n",
        "            \"nove\", \"dieci\", \"undici\", \"dodici\", \"tredici\", \"quattordici\",\n",
        "            \"quindici\", \"sedici\", \"diciassette\", \"diciotto\", \"diciannove\"]\n",
        "    tens = {20: \"venti\", 30: \"trenta\", 40: \"quaranta\", 50: \"cinquanta\",\n",
        "            60: \"sessanta\", 70: \"settanta\", 80: \"ottanta\", 90: \"novanta\"}\n",
        "    out = {n: ones[n] for n in range(20)}\n",
        "    for d, b in tens.items():\n",
        "        out[d] = b\n",
        "        for n in range(1, 10):\n",
        "            stem = b[:-1] if n in (1, 3, 8) else b\n",
        "            out[d + n] = stem + ones[n]\n",
        "    hund = {1: \"cento\", 2: \"duecento\", 3: \"trecento\",\n",
        "            4: \"quattrocento\", 5: \"cinquecento\", 6: \"seicento\",\n",
        "            7: \"settecento\", 8: \"ottocento\", 9: \"novecento\"}\n",
        "    for h in range(1, 10):\n",
        "        out[100 * h] = hund[h]\n",
        "        for r in range(1, 100):\n",
        "            w = out[r]\n",
        "            stem = hund[h][:-1] if w[0] in \"aeiou\" else hund[h]\n",
        "            out[100 * h + r] = stem + w\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "SC_FMT = (\"numeric\", \"english\", \"spanish\", \"italian\")\n",
        "SC_OPW = {\"english\": (\"plus\", \"minus\"), \"spanish\": (\"mas\", \"menos\"),\n",
        "          \"italian\": (\"piu\", \"meno\")}\n",
        "SC_TAIL = {\"english\": \"equals\", \"spanish\": \"es igual a\", \"italian\": \"fa\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_render(operands, ops, fmt):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Paper s2.1 renderings: '44 + 22 =' / 'forty-four plus twenty-two equals' / \"\"\"\n",
        "    \"\"\"'cuarenta y cuatro mas veintidos es igual a' / 'quarantaquattro piu ventidue fa'.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if fmt == \"numeric\":\n",
        "        s = str(operands[0])\n",
        "        for op, v in zip(ops, operands[1:]):\n",
        "            s += \" %s %d\" % (op, v)\n",
        "        return sc_sym_num(s + \" =\")\n",
        "    W = {\"english\": sc_words_en(), \"spanish\": sc_words_es(),\n",
        "         \"italian\": sc_words_it()}[fmt]\n",
        "    parts = [W[operands[0]]]\n",
        "    for op, v in zip(ops, operands[1:]):\n",
        "        parts += [SC_OPW[fmt][0] if op == \"+\" else SC_OPW[fmt][1], W[v]]\n",
        "    parts.append(SC_TAIL[fmt])\n",
        "    return \" \".join(parts)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_eval(operands, ops):\n",
        "    r = operands[0]\n",
        "    for op, v in zip(ops, operands[1:]):\n",
        "        r = r + v if op == \"+\" else r - v\n",
        "    return r\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_carry(operands, ops):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Any decimal carry/borrow evaluating left to right (paper: half the items).\"\"\"\n",
        "    r, hit = operands[0], False\n",
        "    for op, v in zip(ops, operands[1:]):\n",
        "        if op == \"+\":\n",
        "            if any(((r // 10 ** k) % 10 + (v // 10 ** k) % 10) >= 10 for k in range(5)):\n",
        "                hit = True\n",
        "            r += v\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            if any(((r // 10 ** k) % 10) < ((v // 10 ** k) % 10) for k in range(5)):\n",
        "                hit = True\n",
        "            r -= v\n",
        "    return hit\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_flip(ops):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Sign-flipped partner x' (paper s2.1: every + becomes - and vice versa).\"\"\"\n",
        "    return [\"-\" if o == \"+\" else \"+\" for o in ops]\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_fmt_ans(a):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Sign-aware fixed-width answer (width 5): '+0066' -> 'Paagg'. Deterministic span.\"\"\"\n",
        "    s = (\"P%04d\" % abs(a)) if a >= 0 else (\"-%04d\" % abs(a))\n",
        "    return \"\".join(SC_DIG.get(c, c) for c in s)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_gen_items(n, seed=0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Paper s2.1: 2-3 digit operands, 2-3 terms, both 50/50, half with carry.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import random as _r\n",
        "    rng = _r.Random(seed)\n",
        "    items, have_carry, guard = [], 0, 0\n",
        "    need_carry = n // 2\n",
        "    while len(items) < n and guard < n * 500:\n",
        "        guard += 1\n",
        "        nd = 2 if rng.random() < 0.5 else 3\n",
        "        nt = 2 if rng.random() < 0.5 else 3\n",
        "        operands = [rng.randrange(10, 100) if nd == 2 else rng.randrange(100, 1000)\n",
        "                    for _ in range(nt)]\n",
        "        ops = [rng.choice([\"+\", \"-\"]) for _ in range(nt - 1)]\n",
        "        c = sc_carry(operands, ops)\n",
        "        if c and have_carry >= need_carry:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        if (not c) and (len(items) - have_carry) >= (n - need_carry):\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        have_carry += 1 if c else 0\n",
        "        items.append({\"operands\": operands, \"ops\": ops,\n",
        "                      \"ans\": sc_eval(operands, ops), \"carry\": c})\n",
        "    return items\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT shared-circuits encoding + exposure training | Paper s2.2 (1-shot exemplar in target format, greedy decode) + s2.3 (equal-length x/x' filter) | graded 11_Setup | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"One-shot prompts (exemplar with answer, then problem); causal loss on the answer \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"span only; greedy exact-match with the CAUSAL shift (logits[p-1] predict token \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"p). Length handling mirrors paper s2.3: overflow prompts are skipped; the shorter \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"of x/x' is right-padded with spaces so tokenized lengths match (verbal op-words \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"differ in length: plus/minus, mas/menos, piu/meno - at subword level both are \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"usually one token, at char level padding is the documented stand-in).\"\"\"\n",
        "SC_AW = 5\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_build_rows(items, fmt, ex_item, ctx_len):\n",
        "    ex_text = (sc_render(ex_item[\"operands\"], ex_item[\"ops\"], fmt) + \" \" +\n",
        "               sc_fmt_ans(ex_item[\"ans\"]) + \"\\n\")\n",
        "    rows, n_skip, n_unk, n_padded = [], 0, 0, 0\n",
        "    for it in items:\n",
        "        p = ex_text + sc_render(it[\"operands\"], it[\"ops\"], fmt)\n",
        "        a = sc_fmt_ans(it[\"ans\"])\n",
        "        pf = ex_text + sc_render(it[\"operands\"], sc_flip(it[\"ops\"]), fmt)\n",
        "        af = sc_fmt_ans(sc_eval(it[\"operands\"], sc_flip(it[\"ops\"])))\n",
        "        if len(p) != len(pf):\n",
        "            m = max(len(p), len(pf))\n",
        "            p = p + \" \" * (m - len(p))\n",
        "            pf = pf + \" \" * (m - len(pf))\n",
        "            n_padded += 1\n",
        "        if len(p) + len(a) > ctx_len or len(pf) + len(af) > ctx_len:\n",
        "            n_skip += 1\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        x_ids = [token_to_int.get(c, 0) for c in p]\n",
        "        xp_ids = [token_to_int.get(c, 0) for c in pf]\n",
        "        a_ids = [token_to_int.get(c, 0) for c in a]\n",
        "        af_ids = [token_to_int.get(c, 0) for c in af]\n",
        "        n_unk += sum(1 for c in (p + a + pf + af) if c not in token_to_int)\n",
        "        rows.append({\"x_ids\": x_ids, \"xp_ids\": xp_ids, \"a_ids\": a_ids,\n",
        "                     \"af_ids\": af_ids, \"P\": len(x_ids), \"ans\": it[\"ans\"],\n",
        "                     \"item\": it})\n",
        "    return {\"rows\": rows, \"n_skip\": n_skip, \"n_unknown_chars\": n_unk,\n",
        "            \"n_padded\": n_padded, \"fmt\": fmt}\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_greedy(model, prompt_ids, steps):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Greedy decode (paper s2.2: decoded greedily), argmax, deterministic.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    ids = list(prompt_ids)\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        for _ in range(steps):\n",
        "            xb = _t.tensor([ids[-model.ctx_len:]], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "            nxt = int(model(xb)[0, -1, :].argmax().item())\n",
        "            ids.append(nxt)\n",
        "    return ids[len(prompt_ids):]\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_answer_em(model, rows, use_flipped=False):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Greedy exact-match over the fixed-width answer span (causal-shifted).\"\"\"\n",
        "    hits = 0\n",
        "    for r in rows:\n",
        "        pred = sc_greedy(model, r[\"x_ids\"] if not use_flipped else r[\"xp_ids\"], SC_AW)\n",
        "        gold = r[\"a_ids\"] if not use_flipped else r[\"af_ids\"]\n",
        "        hits += 1 if pred == gold else 0\n",
        "    return hits / max(1, len(rows))\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_train_exposure(model, pool, steps=1200, batch=64, eta=3e-3, seed=0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Train the UNCHANGED model on prompt+answer strings; loss ONLY on answer tokens.\"\"\"\n",
        "    \"\"\"pool: list of (seq_ids, a0) with a0 = answer start. The paper's pretraining-\"\"\"\n",
        "    \"\"\"exposure asymmetry is reproduced as a training-exposure mix (documented).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    _t.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    opt = _t.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=eta)\n",
        "    loss_fn = _t.nn.CrossEntropyLoss(reduction=\"none\")\n",
        "    hist = []\n",
        "    for s in range(steps):\n",
        "        model.train()\n",
        "        ix = _t.randint(len(pool), (batch,))\n",
        "        seqs = [pool[int(i)][0] for i in ix]\n",
        "        a0s = [pool[int(i)][1] for i in ix]\n",
        "        L = max(len(q) for q in seqs)\n",
        "        xb = _t.tensor([q + [0] * (L - len(q)) for q in seqs], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "        opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "        logits = model(xb)\n",
        "        tot, n = 0.0, 0\n",
        "        for b in range(batch):\n",
        "            a0, a1 = a0s[b], a0s[b] + SC_AW\n",
        "            ce = loss_fn(logits[b, a0 - 1:a1 - 1, :], xb[b, a0:a1])\n",
        "            tot = tot + ce.sum()\n",
        "            n += SC_AW\n",
        "        (tot / max(1, n)).backward()\n",
        "        opt.step()\n",
        "        if (s + 1) % 200 == 0 or s == steps - 1:\n",
        "            hist.append(float(tot.detach().item()) / max(1, n))\n",
        "    return {\"loss_hist\": hist, \"steps\": steps}\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_pool_from_built(built_list, weights):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Merge per-format built rows into one exposure pool: [(seq, a0)].\"\"\"\n",
        "    pool = []\n",
        "    for b, w in zip(built_list, weights):\n",
        "        rep = max(1, int(round(w * 4)))\n",
        "        for r in b[\"rows\"]:\n",
        "            pool += [((r[\"x_ids\"] + r[\"a_ids\"]), r[\"P\"])] * rep\n",
        "    return pool\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT shared-circuits attribution patching (live Eq.1-3) | Paper App B (m/M/attrib, last prompt token, MLP units, 2 fwd + 1 bwd) + s2.3 (S_m top 1%, Jaccard, loading) | graded 11_Equations | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Hook site = blocks[l].ffwd.net[2] input (post-activation hidden units), the live \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"equivalent of the base repo's layer.mlp.down_proj.input. Jaccard is the paper's \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"top-1% Jaccard, NOT the base repo's asymmetric intersection/k (divergence #2).\"\"\"\n",
        "def sc_logp_span(model, seq_ids, a0, ans_ids):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Teacher-forced sum log P(ans|prompt) over the answer span (App B).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    xb = _t.tensor([seq_ids], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    logits = model(xb)[0]\n",
        "    lp = _t.log_softmax(logits[a0 - 1:a0 - 1 + len(ans_ids), :], dim=-1)\n",
        "    tb = _t.tensor(ans_ids, dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    return lp[_t.arange(len(ans_ids)), tb].sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_attrib_item(model, row):\n",
        "    \"\"\"One item: own greedy answers (App B), Eq.1 m, Eq.2 M, Eq.3 attrib per layer.\"\"\"\n",
        "    \"\"\"Drops identical-output items (paper filter). Returns None when dropped.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    P = row[\"P\"]\n",
        "    yhat = sc_greedy(model, row[\"x_ids\"], SC_AW)\n",
        "    yhatp = sc_greedy(model, row[\"xp_ids\"], SC_AW)\n",
        "    if yhat == yhatp:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        m_x = float(sc_logp_span(model, row[\"x_ids\"] + yhat, P, yhat))\n",
        "        m_xp = float(sc_logp_span(model, row[\"xp_ids\"] + yhatp, P, yhatp))\n",
        "    denom = m_x - m_xp\n",
        "    if abs(denom) < 1e-9:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    saved = []\n",
        "    handles = []\n",
        "    for blk in model.blocks:\n",
        "        handles.append(blk.ffwd.net[2].register_forward_hook(\n",
        "            lambda mod, inp, out, s=saved: s.append(inp[0])))\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "            saved.clear()\n",
        "            model(_t.tensor([row[\"x_ids\"] + yhat], dtype=_t.long).to(\n",
        "                next(model.parameters()).device))\n",
        "            clean = [_t.tensor(s[0, P - 1, :].detach().cpu().numpy()) for s in saved]\n",
        "        saved.clear()\n",
        "        dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "        seqp = _t.tensor([row[\"xp_ids\"] + yhatp], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "        logits = model(seqp)\n",
        "        for s in saved:\n",
        "            s.retain_grad()\n",
        "        lp = _t.log_softmax(logits[0, P - 1:P - 1 + SC_AW, :], dim=-1)\n",
        "        tb = _t.tensor(yhat, dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "        tp = _t.tensor(yhatp, dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "        m = lp[_t.arange(SC_AW), tb].sum() - lp[_t.arange(SC_AW), tp].sum()\n",
        "        model.zero_grad()\n",
        "        m.backward()\n",
        "        grads = [s.grad[0, P - 1, :].detach().cpu() for s in saved]\n",
        "        corr = [s[0, P - 1, :].detach().cpu() for s in saved]\n",
        "    finally:\n",
        "        for h in handles:\n",
        "            h.remove()\n",
        "    attr = _np.stack([((clean[l] - corr[l]) * grads[l]).numpy() / denom\n",
        "                      for l in range(len(clean))])\n",
        "    return {\"attrib\": attr, \"m_x\": m_x, \"m_xp\": m_xp,\n",
        "            \"yhat\": yhat, \"yhatp\": yhatp}\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_aggregate(attribs):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Format-level score A_{m,f}: mean item attribution (paper s2.3), L x H.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    return _np.stack(attribs).mean(axis=0)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_topk(A, pct=1.0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Top-pct unit set (paper: pct=1.0 defines S_m on A_numeric).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    k = max(1, int(A.size * pct / 100.0))\n",
        "    idx = _np.argsort(-A.ravel())[:k]\n",
        "    return set(map(tuple, _np.stack(_np.unravel_index(idx, A.shape), -1).tolist())), k\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_jaccard(Af, Anum, pct=1.0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Top-1% Jaccard |A cap B|/|A cup B| (paper s2.3; base repo uses inter/k).\"\"\"\n",
        "    Sf, _ = sc_topk(Af, pct)\n",
        "    Sn, _ = sc_topk(Anum, pct)\n",
        "    return len(Sf & Sn) / max(1, len(Sf | Sn))\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_loading(attrib, S):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Item loading on the numeric circuit (paper s2.3/Fig.1).\"\"\"\n",
        "    return float(sum(attrib[l, u] for (l, u) in S))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT shared-circuits main results (live Fig.2/Fig.3 analogs) | Paper s3.1 (per-format accuracy, ordering) + s3.2 (Jaccard means .145/.078/.069, model-level r) + s3.3 (point-biserial, >=30-correct rule, accuracy/entropy vs loading) | graded 11_Fig2_Accuracy/11_Fig3_Loading | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Per-format greedy accuracy, numeric-circuit Jaccard, item loadings, point-biserial \"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"r with t-test p, and live loading-vs-accuracy/entropy binned curves.\"\"\"\n",
        "def sc_point_biserial(loads, correct):\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    x = _np.array(loads, dtype=float)\n",
        "    y = _np.array(correct, dtype=float)\n",
        "    n = len(y)\n",
        "    if n < 8 or y.std() == 0 or x.std() == 0:\n",
        "        return 0.0, 1.0, n\n",
        "    r = float(_np.corrcoef(x, y)[0, 1])\n",
        "    t = r * ((n - 2) / max(1e-12, 1 - r * r)) ** 0.5\n",
        "    from math import erf as _erf, sqrt as _sqrt\n",
        "    p = float(1 - _erf(abs(t) / _sqrt(2)))\n",
        "    return r, max(p, 1e-300), n\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_run_format(model, built, S, max_items=None):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Accuracy + loadings + point-biserial for one format's rows.\"\"\"\n",
        "    rows = built[\"rows\"][:max_items] if max_items else built[\"rows\"]\n",
        "    loads, correct, kept = [], [], 0\n",
        "    for r in rows:\n",
        "        a = sc_attrib_item(model, r)\n",
        "        pred = sc_greedy(model, r[\"x_ids\"], SC_AW)\n",
        "        ok = 1 if pred == r[\"a_ids\"] else 0\n",
        "        if a is None:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        kept += 1\n",
        "        loads.append(sc_loading(a[\"attrib\"], S))\n",
        "        correct.append(ok)\n",
        "    r_pb, p, n = sc_point_biserial(loads, correct)\n",
        "    acc = sum(correct) / max(1, len(correct))\n",
        "    return {\"fmt\": built[\"fmt\"], \"acc\": acc, \"r\": r_pb, \"p\": p, \"n\": n,\n",
        "            \"n_correct\": int(sum(correct)), \"loads\": loads, \"correct\": correct,\n",
        "            \"n_skip\": built[\"n_skip\"], \"n_unknown\": built[\"n_unknown_chars\"]}\n",
        "\n",
        "def sc_plot_main(per_fmt, out_prefix=\"sc_live\"):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Live Fig.2 (accuracy bars) + Fig.3B/C (binned accuracy/entropy vs loading).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import matplotlib.pyplot as _plt\n",
        "    import numpy as _np\n",
        "    _plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.facecolor\": \"white\", \"axes.grid\": True,\n",
        "                          \"grid.alpha\": 0.25, \"font.size\": 10})\n",
        "    fmts = [d[\"fmt\"] for d in per_fmt]\n",
        "    fig, axes = _plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(13.5, 4))\n",
        "    bars = axes[0].bar(fmts, [d[\"acc\"] for d in per_fmt],\n",
        "                       color=[\"#4c72b0\", \"#dd8452\", \"#55a868\", \"#c44e52\"])\n",
        "    for b, d in zip(bars, per_fmt):\n",
        "        axes[0].text(b.get_x() + b.get_width() / 2, b.get_height() + 0.015,\n",
        "                     f\"{d['acc']:.2f}\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=9)\n",
        "    axes[0].set_ylim(0, 1.05)\n",
        "    axes[0].set_ylabel(\"greedy exact-match\")\n",
        "    axes[0].set_title(\"live per-format accuracy (Fig.2 analog)\")\n",
        "    for ax, key, ttl in ((axes[1], \"acc\", \"B accuracy vs loading\"),\n",
        "                         (axes[2], \"ent\", \"C entropy vs loading\")):\n",
        "        for d in per_fmt:\n",
        "            if d[\"n\"] < 8:\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "            lo = _np.array(d[\"loads\"], dtype=float)\n",
        "            span = lo.max() - lo.min()\n",
        "            xn = (lo - lo.min()) / span if span > 0 else lo * 0\n",
        "            order = _np.argsort(xn)\n",
        "            xs, ys = xn[order], _np.array(d[\"correct\"], dtype=float)[order]\n",
        "            k = max(8, len(xs) // 6)\n",
        "            bx = [xs[i:i + k].mean() for i in range(0, len(xs), k)]\n",
        "            if key == \"acc\":\n",
        "                by = [ys[i:i + k].mean() for i in range(0, len(ys), k)]\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                import math as _m\n",
        "                by = []\n",
        "                for i in range(0, len(ys), k):\n",
        "                    q = ys[i:i + k].mean()\n",
        "                    q = min(max(q, 1e-6), 1 - 1e-6)\n",
        "                    by.append(-(q * _m.log2(q) + (1 - q) * _m.log2(1 - q)))\n",
        "            ax.plot(bx, by, \"o-\", ms=4, label=d[\"fmt\"])\n",
        "        ax.set_xlabel(\"loading (normalised bins)\")\n",
        "        ax.set_title(ttl)\n",
        "        ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
        "    fig.tight_layout()\n",
        "    fig.savefig(out_prefix + \"_main.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
        "    _plt.close(fig)\n",
        "    return out_prefix + \"_main.png\"\n"
      ]
    },
