        "## 25. Implicit Weight Patches \\u2013 Equivalence of Context and Parameter Updates in Modern Transformer Blocks (Goldwaser, Munn, Gonzalvo, Dherin 2025/2026, arXiv:2511.17864v1, ICML 2026 Oral)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** A prompt's effect can be compiled into weights: for a Gemma-style block the full-context output T(C,x) is exactly reproduced without the context by rank-1 patches dWgate/dWup (Eq.2-3, input controllability) plus an output-scale patch dm (Eq.4, output controllability); induction extends this to L layers (Thm 2) via a record-targets-then-patch-sequentially procedure (Alg.1, lines 2-19); the controllability framework (Thm 5, Table 1: input MLP/pre-norm, outer bias/weight/elementwise/MoE/parallel) covers Gemma/Llama/Mistral/MoE/GPT-J; Gemma 3 validation matches logits/tokens (Fig.3-5: float32 ~exact, bfloat16 87.5% -> stable 98%) with TVD = 0.5*||p-q||_1; the dm division is bfloat16-unstable, fixed by RMSNorm inversion (App B). Descriptive lens, token-dependent recompute, no global reusable update (s6).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** no official code exists anywhere (0 issues reviewable; only third-party replications of the vanilla foundation paper, which cover nothing in paper 12) - text-faithful. All identities below are verified live in graded 12 (Thm 1 linf ~9e-16 with rank exactly 1; Table 1 all rows ~1e-15; Thm 5; App B bisection).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): no new Technique.** Patch computation reads frozen weights/states and writes a patched CLONE (original never touched, frozen-by-design like TASCO); the anchor (full vs reduced context) is looped, never pathed. Plain ALWAYS-PRESENT codeblocks by design, valid wherever `blocks[l].ffwd.net[0/2]` exist (matmul and addernet alike).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) nanoGPT's MLP keeps its output bias, so the single-block patch takes the Theorem-8 outer-bias path dB = dv - exact with NO division, sidestepping the paper's dm bfloat16 instability by construction (the runner's precision measurement sets test exactly this consequence); under the addernet variant net[2].bias is None, so there the output patch takes the paper's own Theorem-9 outer-weight form on net[2].weight (the Llama row) - same claim, different site, recorded per run. (2) Reduced context = pad prefix at equal length (position-aligned): the query sits at identical absolute positions in both passes, so the patch absorbs attention differences only, mirroring the paper's same-x setup; pads are a legitimate reduced context C\\\\Y, and the machinery is identical for any. (3) Identities are weight-agnostic (exact for random weights too), so the runner needs no training - frozen analysis throughout.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
