        "### Compatibility: Equivalence of Context and Parameter Updates in Modern Transformer Blocks (Goldwaser, Munn, Gonzalvo, Dherin 2025/2026, arXiv:2511.17864)\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** frozen-weight patch computation on any live path (matmul/addernet via the bias/Theorem-9 fork, layernorm/regularisedbn via the same hook sites, decoder/encdec blocks, all Attn impls - attention is never patched, only read); patched clone as a LayerMix probe substrate (do probe geometries survive context absorption?); SABER RSS/CS read on patched runs as a behavioral check beyond logits; Tmem/Tgrok checkpoints as patch substrates across training stages; WRP-pruned checkpoints as patch substrates (recovery-free + patch, both frozen, no training); TASCO optimized prefixes as the Y to absorb (compile the prefix into weights instead of prepending it); lam read on patched vs unpatched runs; s23 exemplar absorbed then AP re-run (does the numeric circuit persist without the exemplar in context?).\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** output-patch site per block (out-bias on matmul paths vs Theorem-9 down-weight on bias-free paths - recorded per layer, never mixed within one comparison); full vs pad-reduced vs query-only reduced context per equivalence run (position consequences documented each way); float32 vs float64 leg per claim.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** patched-clone logits presented as original-model logits (always label which); patch numbers compared across different anchors (full-vs-pad vs full-vs-empty are different equivalences); token-dependent per-position patches presented as a global reusable update (the paper's s6 scope limit - Mazzawi thought-patch direction is cited, not claimed); bfloat16 instability conclusions transferred from the paper's dm path to our bias path (ours divides only by ||z||^2 - different stability profile, tested not assumed).\n",
        "\n",
        "### Relations: ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (kept).** s25 runs the patch to equate two contexts, then s10 probes test whether hallucination geometry survives the equivalence BECAUSE both operate on frozen states without training - the probe panel ports unchanged, and preservation-vs-collapse across absorption is a new probe question neither paper asks alone.\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (kept).** s25 takes SABER's RSS/CS as the behavioral check beyond logits BECAUSE the paper's claim is functional equivalence - stability under the exit lens tests more than logit matching, and a patched run that matches logits but breaks stability would bound the claim.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (kept).** s25 takes s16's Tmem/Tgrok checkpoints as patch substrates across training stages BECAUSE the identities are weight-agnostic in theory - stage-invariance of the equivalence (memorization vs generalized weights) is the empirical check that earns the generality claim.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): NONE (kept).** No joint analysis BECAUSE long-context scaffolding and weight-patch equivalence share no mechanism - the negative is recorded, not forced.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (kept).** s25 re-runs the patch under geodesicflat with documented heads BECAUSE the patch touches MLP weights while the head owns the readout - head-swap orthogonality (does absorption survive the geometry change?) is untestable inside either paper alone.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (kept).** s25 takes WRP's pruned checkpoints as patch substrates BECAUSE both methods are frozen-weight with no training - does the equivalence survive block removal is the cheapest mechanism check in the file after s20's own eval.\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (kept, high value).** s25 takes TASCO's optimized prefixes as the Y to absorb BECAUSE a prefix IS context - compiling V into MLP weights replaces per-token prepend cost with per-token recompute, mirroring the paper's own token-dependence limit and the cited thought-patch direction without claiming reusability.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (kept).** s25 reads lam on patched vs unpatched runs BECAUSE absorption moves context from activations into weights - whether prior loading survives that move is a new readout question, with lam as the existing instrument.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept, highest value).** s23's one-shot exemplar IS a context Y, so s25 absorbs it into weights and s23 re-runs AP/loading on the patched model BECAUSE that directly tests circuit-vs-prompt dependence - does the numeric circuit persist with no exemplar in context? Both papers' activation-surgery machineries (App C patching, implicit patches) meet on this experiment.\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): NONE.** Attention is read, never patched; the vanilla construction is the cited foundation, not a runtime surface.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
