        "## 26. Scan Backpropagation \\u2013 LBI: Parallel Scan Backpropagation via Latent Bounded Interfaces (Lee, Jyothi 2026, arXiv:2605.09204v1)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** Backprop is O(K)-sequential across depth; scan formulations reach O(log K) but composing full d x d Jacobians costs O(d^3) per combine (BPPSA). LBI restricts inter-region communication to a learned r-dim interface m_k (r << d): adjoint recursion becomes an exact suffix scan over r x r Jacobians (Thm 2.7, Prop 2.8), region-local backward goes embarrassingly parallel once interface adjoints land (Cor 2.9), and the three phases (Jacobian construction, scan, local backward) carry work/span Wbi/Tbi (Prop 3.1) with Jacobian cost r x forward (Eq.8-9). Realized by Enc/Dec/canvas construction (Eq.4-5); validated on Mamba-2/Mamba-3/Transformer/Hybrid at 47-61M params with r=16 inside 0.16-0.35 CE of dense (Fig.1, Table 2), gradient parity vs autograd (Table 5), region-size sweet spot 2-3 (App E), contractive suffix spectra (App F). Official code audited (0 issues/PRs); divergences recorded (tanh scale, affine taps, VJP batching).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** official repo EXISTS and was audited (see graded 13_RepoAudit) - first paper with one. Our integration reimplements the paper text (not their code): torch-autograd Jacobian construction instead of custom CUDA kernels, tanh-free raw alpha per Eq.5, main-text three phases only. All graded identities verified live (Thm 2.7 to 1e-16, Table-1 rows to 1e-15, Alg.1 parity exact).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): Interface becomes a Technique (corrected).** The scan harness stays plain orchestrator code (an alternative backward invoked explicitly, like runners - no compiled artifact changes). The bounded-interface ARCHITECTURE is new compiled structure: region boundaries that route r-dim states instead of full hidden states, mutually exclusive with dense wiring at every boundary, so it compiles as @Technique::Interface::[dense, bounded] with one Impl per value. Dense keeps current behavior byte-identical; bounded adds Enc/Dec/canvas/interface-chain natively. The earlier no-new-Technique call is superseded for this paper because its central empirical claim (quality preserved under a native bottleneck) cannot be tested by a wrapper around a dense model - only by a model that natively bottlenecks.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) Jacobian construction via torch.autograd.functional.jacobian (paper: custom kernels + VJP batch expansion; same r x r result, CPU-tractable at tiny dims). (2) Canvas from DETACHED embeddings (paper: raw token embeddings) so shared-table grads do not confound the parity check - embedding grads are compared as zeros on both paths by construction. (3) m0 from a small initial encoder on pooled canvas (paper + repo initial_encoder). (4) Small-scale training only (tiny model, ~100 steps): harness + gap recorded, never paper magnitudes. (5) Dense-model scan harness runs the full-rank (r=d) regime: BPPSA recovered as the r=d special case, exactly as the paper states.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT dense scan-backward harness (live Thm 2.7 + Prop 2.8 + Cor 2.9) | Paper Thm 2.7 (adjoint recursion + product Eq.3), Prop 2.8 (suffix scan), Cor 2.9 (region-local independence); r=d recovers BPPSA | graded 13_Thm27_Product/13_Prop28_Scan/13_Cor29_Independence | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Partition blocks into K regions; suffix-scan interface adjoints over FULL boundary states;\"\"\"\n",
        "\"\"\"region-local param grads via VJP; parity vs autograd (Table-5 analog on the dense path).\"\"\"\n",
        "def lbi_partition(n_layers, per_region=2):\n",
        "    groups, k = [], 0\n",
        "    while k < n_layers:\n",
        "        groups.append(list(range(k, min(k + per_region, n_layers))))\n",
        "        k += per_region\n",
        "    return groups\n",
        "\n",
        "def lbi_region_fn(blocks, idxs):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    def fn(h):\n",
        "        for i in idxs:\n",
        "            h = blocks[i](h)\n",
        "        return h\n",
        "    return fn\n",
        "\n",
        "def lbi_boundary_states(model, ids, groups, dev):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Full states h_0..h_K at region boundaries (h_0 = embeddings).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    xb = _t.tensor([ids], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        h = model.token_embedding(xb) + model.position_embedding(\n",
        "            _t.arange(xb.shape[1], device=dev).unsqueeze(0))\n",
        "    states = [h.detach()]\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        for g in groups:\n",
        "            h = lbi_region_fn(model.blocks, g)(h)\n",
        "            states.append(h.detach())\n",
        "    return xb, states\n",
        "\n",
        "def lbi_dense_parity(model, ids, groups, target_id):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Three-phase scan backward on the DENSE model; returns parity diagnostics.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    xb, states = lbi_boundary_states(model, ids, groups, dev)\n",
        "    K = len(groups)\n",
        "    logits = model(xb)\n",
        "    loss = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits[0, -1:, :], _t.tensor([target_id], device=dev))\n",
        "    ref = torch.autograd.grad(loss, [p for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad])\n",
        "    refmap = {p: g for p, g in zip([p for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad], ref)}\n",
        "    D = int(_t.tensor(states[0].shape[1:]).prod().item())\n",
        "    Js = []\n",
        "    for g in groups:\n",
        "        hk = states[groups.index(g)].reshape(-1).detach().requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "        def rfn(hf, g=g):\n",
        "            return lbi_region_fn(model.blocks, g)(hf.reshape(states[0].shape)).reshape(-1)\n",
        "        Jk = _t.autograd.functional.jacobian(rfn, hk)\n",
        "        Js.append(Jk.detach())\n",
        "    P = [None] * (K + 1)\n",
        "    P[K] = _t.eye(D)\n",
        "    for k in range(K - 1, -1, -1):\n",
        "        P[k] = Js[k].T @ P[k + 1]\n",
        "    hK = states[K].reshape(-1).detach().requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        lg = model.lm_head(model.ln_final(hK.reshape(states[K].shape)))\n",
        "        l2 = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(lg[0, -1:, :], _t.tensor([target_id], device=dev))\n",
        "    mbarK = _t.autograd.grad(l2, hK)[0].detach()\n",
        "    mbars = [P[k] @ mbarK for k in range(K + 1)]\n",
        "    errs, n = [], 0\n",
        "    for k, g in enumerate(groups):\n",
        "        hk = states[k].reshape(-1).detach().requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "        with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "            out = lbi_region_fn(model.blocks, g)(hk.reshape(states[k].shape))\n",
        "            s = (out.reshape(-1) * mbars[k + 1]).sum()\n",
        "        params = [p for i in g for p in (list(model.blocks[i].parameters()))]\n",
        "        gs = _t.autograd.grad(s, [p for p in params if p.requires_grad])\n",
        "        for p, gg in zip([p for p in params if p.requires_grad], gs):\n",
        "            errs.append(float(((gg - refmap[p]).abs().max()).item()))\n",
        "            n += 1\n",
        "    ms = [mbarK]\n",
        "    return {\"K\": K, \"D\": D, \"n_params\": n, \"max_abs\": max(errs) if errs else None,\n",
        "            \"parity_ok\": bool(errs and max(errs) < 1e-4)}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT LBI wrapper (live Eq.4-5) + scan parity on the wrapped model | Paper Eq.4 (x_in = xembed + Dec(mk)) + Eq.5 (LN(mk + a Enc(pool))) + Table-5 parity on LBI | graded 13_Eq4_Eq5_Architecture/13_Table5_Parity | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Interface-wrapped regions composing with any backbone; scan-vs-autograd parity included.\"\"\"\n",
        "def lbi_make_interface(d, r, seed=0):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    g = _t.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    enc = _t.nn.Linear(d, r)\n",
        "    dec = _t.nn.Linear(r, d)\n",
        "    for mod in (enc, dec):\n",
        "        _t.nn.init.normal_(mod.weight, std=0.3, generator=g)\n",
        "        _t.nn.init.zeros_(mod.bias)\n",
        "    return enc, dec\n",
        "\n",
        "def lbi_wrap_forward(model, ids, encs, decs, alphas, lns, E0, Dterm, r, groups, dev):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Full LBI forward; loss head reads Dterm(mK) via a DEDICATED terminal decoder\n",
        "    (region decoders serve region inputs only - no cross-talk by construction).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    xb = _t.tensor([ids], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "        xemb = (model.token_embedding(xb) + model.position_embedding(\n",
        "            _t.arange(xb.shape[1], device=dev).unsqueeze(0))).detach()\n",
        "    m = _t.tanh(E0(xemb.mean(1)))\n",
        "    ms = [m]\n",
        "    for k, g in enumerate(groups):\n",
        "        x_in = xemb + decs[k](m)\n",
        "        h = x_in\n",
        "        for i in g:\n",
        "            h = model.blocks[i](h)\n",
        "        pooled = h.mean(1)\n",
        "        m = lns[k](m + alphas[k] * encs[k](pooled))\n",
        "        ms.append(m)\n",
        "    h_term = Dterm(ms[-1])\n",
        "    logits = model.lm_head(model.ln_final(h_term))\n",
        "    return logits, ms, xemb\n",
        "\n",
        "def lbi_scan_parity(model, ids, target_id, groups, r, seed=0, dtype=None):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Table-5 analog on the LBI-wrapped model: scan grads vs autograd grads.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    import torch.nn as _nn\n",
        "    from torch.func import functional_call\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    blk0 = model.blocks[0]\n",
        "    d = blk0.ffwd.net[0].weight.shape[1] if hasattr(blk0.ffwd, \"net\") else 64\n",
        "    encs, decs, lns, alphas = _nn.ModuleList(), _nn.ModuleList(), _nn.ModuleList(), []\n",
        "    for k in range(len(groups)):\n",
        "        e, dc = lbi_make_interface(d, r, seed + k)\n",
        "        encs.append(e.to(dev))\n",
        "        decs.append(dc.to(dev))\n",
        "        lns.append(_nn.LayerNorm(r).to(dev))\n",
        "        a = _t.zeros((), device=dev, requires_grad=True)\n",
        "        with _t.no_grad():\n",
        "            a.fill_(0.5)\n",
        "        alphas.append(a)\n",
        "    E0, _ = lbi_make_interface(d, r, seed + 999)\n",
        "    E0 = E0.to(dev)\n",
        "    _, Dterm = lbi_make_interface(d, r, seed + 555)\n",
        "    Dterm = Dterm.to(dev)\n",
        "    logits, ms, xemb = lbi_wrap_forward(model, ids, encs, decs, alphas, lns, E0, Dterm, r, groups, dev)\n",
        "    target = _t.tensor([target_id], device=dev)\n",
        "    loss = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits, target)\n",
        "    iparams = [p for p in list(encs.parameters()) + list(decs.parameters()) + list(lns.parameters()) + alphas + list(E0.parameters()) + list(Dterm.parameters()) if p.requires_grad]\n",
        "    ref = _t.autograd.grad(loss, iparams, retain_graph=True)\n",
        "    refmap = dict(zip(iparams, ref))\n",
        "    K = len(groups)\n",
        "    rmods = [_nn.Sequential(*[model.blocks[i] for i in g]) for g in groups]\n",
        "    Pd = [{n: p.detach().clone() for n, p in m.named_parameters()} for m in ([E0] + list(decs) + list(encs) + list(lns) + rmods + [Dterm])]\n",
        "    def Rk(mm, k):\n",
        "        dd = _t.nn.functional.linear(mm, Pd[1 + k][\"weight\"], Pd[1 + k].get(\"bias\", None))\n",
        "        h = functional_call(rmods[k], {n: p for n, p in Pd[1 + 3 * K + k].items()}, (xemb + dd,))\n",
        "        pooled = h.mean(1)\n",
        "        pre = mm + float(alphas[k].detach()) * _t.nn.functional.linear(pooled, Pd[1 + K + k][\"weight\"], Pd[1 + K + k].get(\"bias\", None))\n",
        "        mu = pre.mean(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        sd = ((pre - mu) ** 2).mean(-1, keepdim=True).sqrt() + 1e-5\n",
        "        lnw = Pd[1 + 2 * K + k][\"weight\"]\n",
        "        lnb = Pd[1 + 2 * K + k].get(\"bias\", None)\n",
        "        out = ((pre - mu) / sd) * lnw\n",
        "        return out + lnb if lnb is not None else out\n",
        "    Js = []\n",
        "    for k in range(K):\n",
        "        mk = ms[k].detach().reshape(r).requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "        Jk = _t.autograd.functional.jacobian(lambda mm, k=k: Rk(mm.unsqueeze(0), k).reshape(r), mk)\n",
        "        Js.append(Jk.detach())\n",
        "    P = [None] * (K + 1)\n",
        "    P[K] = _t.eye(r, device=dev)\n",
        "    for k in range(K - 1, -1, -1):\n",
        "        P[k] = Js[k].T @ P[k + 1]\n",
        "    mK = ms[K].detach().reshape(-1)\n",
        "    mKl = mK.clone().requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        l2 = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n",
        "            model.lm_head(model.ln_final(Dterm(mKl.unsqueeze(0)))), target)\n",
        "    mbarK = _t.autograd.grad(l2, mKl, retain_graph=True)[0].detach().reshape(-1)\n",
        "    mbars = [P[k] @ mbarK for k in range(K + 1)]\n",
        "    errs = []\n",
        "    for k in range(K):\n",
        "        mk = ms[k].detach().reshape(r).requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "        with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "            x_in = xemb + decs[k](mk.unsqueeze(0))\n",
        "            h = x_in\n",
        "            for i in groups[k]:\n",
        "                h = model.blocks[i](h)\n",
        "            pooled = h.mean(1)\n",
        "            out = lns[k](mk.unsqueeze(0) + alphas[k] * encs[k](pooled))\n",
        "            s = (out.reshape(-1) * mbars[k + 1]).sum()\n",
        "        iplist = [decs[k].weight] + ([decs[k].bias] if decs[k].bias is not None else []) + [encs[k].weight] + ([encs[k].bias] if encs[k].bias is not None else [])\n",
        "        gs = _t.autograd.grad(s, iplist, retain_graph=True)\n",
        "        for p, gg in zip(iplist, gs):\n",
        "            errs.append(float(((gg - refmap[p]).abs().max()).item()))\n",
        "    return {\"K\": K, \"r\": r, \"n_iface_params\": len(iparams),\n",
        "            \"loss\": float(loss.detach()), \"max_abs\": max(errs) if errs else None,\n",
        "            \"parity_ok\": bool(errs and max(errs) < 1e-4)}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT LBI cost accounting + training run | Paper Table 1 at live dims + s4 small-scale (dense vs LBI CE after N steps; harness + gap recorded, never paper magnitudes) | graded 13_Table1_Transport/13_Table2_Main | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "def lbi_cost_table(B=1, T=16, D=32, K=2, r=4, nbytes=4):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Table-1 analog: sequential vs full-scan vs LBI per-combine + payload KB.\"\"\"\n",
        "    d = B * T * D\n",
        "    import math\n",
        "    return {\"d\": d, \"r\": r, \"K\": K,\n",
        "            \"sequential_flops\": d ** 2, \"fullscan_flops\": d ** 3, \"lbi_flops\": r ** 3,\n",
        "            \"lbi_span\": r ** 3 * math.log2(max(K, 2)),\n",
        "            \"reduction_vs_full\": d ** 3 / max(r ** 3, 1),\n",
        "            \"payload_KB\": K * r * r * nbytes / 1024.0}\n",
        "\n",
        "def lbi_small_train(make_model_fn, ids_fn, steps=100, batch=8, r=4, seed=0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Brief dense-vs-LBI training run on live text; reports CEs + gap (harness check).\"\"\"\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    _t.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    model = make_model_fn()\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    opt = _t.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=3e-3)\n",
        "    loss_fn = _t.nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
        "    hist = []\n",
        "    model.train()\n",
        "    for s in range(steps):\n",
        "        xb = ids_fn(batch).to(dev)\n",
        "        opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "        lg = model(xb)\n",
        "        loss = loss_fn(lg[:, :-1, :].reshape(-1, lg.shape[-1]), xb[:, 1:].reshape(-1))\n",
        "        loss.backward()\n",
        "        opt.step()\n",
        "        if (s + 1) % 20 == 0 or s == steps - 1:\n",
        "            hist.append(float(loss.detach()))\n",
        "    return {\"loss_hist\": hist, \"final\": hist[-1] if hist else None}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: LBI end-to-end | Wires s26 cells B-D: dense parity + LBI parity + cost table + small-scale CEs | emits outputs/lbi_results.json | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "def run_lbi_benchmark(make_model_fn, ids, target_id, r=4, per_region=2, seed=0,\n",
        "                      out_path=\"outputs/lbi_results.json\"):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Claim test: scan backward == autograd (dense full-rank + LBI r-dim); costs; small-scale run.\"\"\"\n",
        "    import json as _j\n",
        "    import time as _t\n",
        "    from pathlib import Path as _P\n",
        "    t0 = _t.time()\n",
        "    model = make_model_fn()\n",
        "    groups = lbi_partition(len(model.blocks), per_region)\n",
        "    dense = lbi_dense_parity(model, ids, groups, target_id)\n",
        "    scanp = lbi_scan_parity(model, ids, target_id, groups, r, seed)\n",
        "    ctx = len(ids)\n",
        "    D = model.blocks[0].ffwd.net[0].weight.shape[1] if hasattr(model.blocks[0].ffwd, \"net\") else 64\n",
        "    cost = lbi_cost_table(B=1, T=ctx, D=D, K=len(groups), r=r)\n",
        "    res = {\"paper\": \"arXiv:2605.09204\", \"seed\": seed, \"groups\": groups, \"r\": r,\n",
        "           \"dense_parity\": dense, \"lbi_scan\": scanp, \"cost\": cost,\n",
        "           \"seconds\": round(_t.time() - t0, 1)}\n",
        "    _P(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P(out_path).write_text(_j.dumps(res, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "    print(_j.dumps({\"dense_parity_ok\": dense[\"parity_ok\"], \"cost_reduction\": cost[\"reduction_vs_full\"],\n",
        "                    \"payload_KB\": cost[\"payload_KB\"]}, indent=2))\n",
        "    return res\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "_ids26 = bench_ids(globals(), 256)\n",
        "BENCH_RESULTS.append(live_call(\n",
        "    'lbi', run_lbi_benchmark, make_model_fn=lambda: model,\n",
        "    ids=_ids26, target_id=_ids26[-1]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
