      "source": [
        "### Compatibility: LBI: Parallel Scan Backpropagation via Latent Bounded Interfaces (Lee, Jyothi 2026, arXiv:2605.09204)\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** scan harness on any live path (matmul/addernet, layernorm/regularisedbn, decoder/encdec, all Attn impls - regions are block groups, Jacobians read whatever backbone computes); parity harness as a gradient auditor for every training loop in the file (grokking s16, exposure s23, LBI s26 - same comparison, different loop); interface Jacobians as tracked diagnostics beside norm trackers (s14/s16); region partition as the unit WRP prunes (block groups) and ConvMem windows (channels); scan payload accounting beside SABER overhead tables.\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** dense full-rank scan (BPPSA regime, exact, O(d^3)) vs LBI r-dim scan per parity run (looped configs, never pathed); region size (layers per region) per sweep; interface width r per small-scale leg; fused vs chunked Jacobian construction (Eq.12 vs Eq.13 trade, documented per run).\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** scan-path grads presented as autograd grads without the parity check (parity-gated reporting: numbers ship only beside their max-abs/cosine); LBI small-scale CEs cited as paper-magnitude evidence (small-scale only - harness + gap recorded); canvas treated as an inter-region channel (it depends on inputs only - the paper's own no-bypass argument, enforced by detaching it); wall-clock speedup claims from algorithmic span alone (kernels/fusion outstanding - paper s6 limit, inherited here).\n",
        "\n",
        "### Relations: LBI (arXiv:2605.09204) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (kept).** Probes read frozen states; the parity harness audits the gradients that trained those states - same frozen truism from opposite ends (forward readout vs backward audit). No shared math beyond the 5-fold CV discipline both reuse.\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** SABER exits online during generation; LBI parallelizes offline during training - complementary axes (depth-parallel backward vs early-exit forward), same accounting style (payload KB beside probe-token tables).\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (kept, high value).** s25 takes Tmem/Tgrok checkpoints as patch substrates; s26 takes the same s16 training loop as its parity-audit subject BECAUSE the loop that produces grokking is exactly what a gradient auditor must verify - s16 trains, s26 checks, neither retrains the other.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** Channels and regions are both partitionings of depth/work; ConvMem windows the forward context while LBI scan parallelizes the backward depth - same divide-and-conquer taste, different objects (context vs gradients), never merged.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** GeodesicHead changes the readout; the parity harness is head-agnostic (it differentiates whatever forward exists) - re-running parity under geodesicflat tests auditor robustness the same way s23 re-runs circuits.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (kept).** Pruned checkpoints are smaller region graphs; parity re-run on pruned models asks whether absorption... [see backprop: pruning meets scan-parallel regions] - both frozen-weight, no training.\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Prefixes steer the forward pass; the parity harness audits whatever backward trained it - frozen steering and exact scan-backward compose (steer first, verify the training that made the steered model).\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam reads priors off frozen states; interface Jacobians expose gradient-transport spectra off the same states - readout geometry meets transport geometry, two columns, never fused.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP localizes circuits with gradients; the parity harness verifies the gradients AP itself consumes BECAUSE attribution patching is only as exact as the backward pass beneath it - s26 audits s23's instrument.\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): STACK (kept, highest value).** Both compile context/history into cheaper forms - s25 compiles prompts into weights (rank-1 patches), s26 compiles depth-sequential backward into scan-parallel backward (r x r Jacobians); the shared theme is exactness-preserving compression, tested by logit-match and gradient-parity respectively.\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** Regions are block groups on any backbone; Vaswani 2017 is cited by the paper itself (foundation, not a runtime surface).\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** Interface axis mechanics - dense wiring ships byte-identical behavior (selectable default); bounded wiring compiles Enc/Dec/canvas/interface-chain natively with the same Block/attention/norm impls underneath, so every existing combo keeps composing and the axis multiplies nothing it cannot run with.\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** dense inter-block wiring vs bounded interface wiring (mutually exclusive at every boundary - the axis exists exactly because of this); encoder-decoder Arch crossed with bounded has no Impl provided and is out of scope here.\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::Interface::dense{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Impl: dense inter-block wiring\n",
        "- **dense** names the current behavior so the compiler can select it: every block boundary carries the FULL hidden state; regions are pure index groupings (`lbi_partition`, plain s26 Cell B) with zero wiring changes.\n",
        "- The scan-backward harness runs the full-rank (BPPSA) regime on dense paths; parity vs autograd is the dense-path acceptance check (Table-5 analog, exact).\n",
        "- Dense keeps all existing combos byte-identical; bounded is the opt-in alternative (next cells).\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Interface::bounded{
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "### Impl: bounded interface wiring (folded into the one NanoGPT class)\n",
        "- The interface chain (Enc/Dec/canvas/LN/alpha/E0/terminal tap), the r-dim region grouping, and the region-wired forward are spliced INTO `NanoGPT` itself under this selection (no sibling class; the one-model rule). Embeddings/blocks/head/generate stay the base class.\n",
        "- Native parity reads `model._iface` + the same interface modules from the one class (next cell).\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::Interface::bounded{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT native parity on compiled bounded models | Reads model._iface stash + own interface modules; region VJPs vs autograd ref (Table-5 analog on the native path) | graded 13_Table5_Parity | plain codeblock structure, Impl-tagged path.\n",
        "\"\"\"Phase-3 VJPs cover interface params (Enc/Dec/LN/alpha/E0/Dterm); backbone params use standard autograd within regions (dense harness already verifies region-local exactness on backbone params).\"\"\"\n",
        "def lbi_native_parity(model, ids, target_id):\n",
        "    import torch as _t\n",
        "    import torch.nn as _nn\n",
        "    from torch.func import functional_call\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    groups = model.region_groups\n",
        "    K = len(groups)\n",
        "    r = model.iface_width\n",
        "    xb = _t.tensor([ids], dtype=_t.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    logits = model(xb)\n",
        "    target = _t.tensor([target_id], device=dev)\n",
        "    loss = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits[:, -1, :], target)\n",
        "    iparams = [p for p in list(model.iface_encs.parameters()) + list(model.iface_decs.parameters()) + list(model.iface_lns.parameters()) + [model.iface_alphas] + list(model.iface_E0.parameters()) + list(model.iface_Dterm.parameters()) if p.requires_grad]\n",
        "    ref = _t.autograd.grad(loss, iparams, retain_graph=True)\n",
        "    refmap = dict(zip(iparams, ref))\n",
        "    xemb = model._iface[\"xemb\"]\n",
        "    msvals = model._iface[\"ms\"]\n",
        "    rmods = [_nn.Sequential(*[model.blocks[i] for i in g]) for g in groups]\n",
        "    Pd = [{n: p.detach().clone() for n, p in m.named_parameters()} for m in (list(model.iface_decs) + list(model.iface_encs) + list(model.iface_lns) + rmods)]\n",
        "    def Rk(mm, k):\n",
        "        dd = _t.nn.functional.linear(mm, Pd[k][\"weight\"], Pd[k].get(\"bias\", None))\n",
        "        h = functional_call(rmods[k], {n: p for n, p in Pd[3 * K + k].items()}, (xemb + dd.unsqueeze(1),))\n",
        "        pooled = h.mean(1)\n",
        "        pre = mm + float(model.iface_alphas[k].detach()) * _t.nn.functional.linear(pooled, Pd[K + k][\"weight\"], Pd[K + k].get(\"bias\", None))\n",
        "        mu = pre.mean(-1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        sd = ((pre - mu) ** 2).mean(-1, keepdim=True).sqrt() + 1e-5\n",
        "        lnw = Pd[2 * K + k][\"weight\"]\n",
        "        lnb = Pd[2 * K + k].get(\"bias\", None)\n",
        "        out = ((pre - mu) / sd) * lnw\n",
        "        return out + lnb if lnb is not None else out\n",
        "    Js = []\n",
        "    for k in range(K):\n",
        "        mk = msvals[k].detach().reshape(-1).requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "        Jk = _t.autograd.functional.jacobian(lambda mm, k=k: Rk(mm.unsqueeze(0), k).reshape(-1), mk)\n",
        "        Js.append(Jk.detach())\n",
        "    P = [None] * (K + 1)\n",
        "    P[K] = _t.eye(r, device=dev)\n",
        "    for k in range(K - 1, -1, -1):\n",
        "        P[k] = Js[k].T @ P[k + 1]\n",
        "    mK = msvals[K].detach().reshape(-1)\n",
        "    mKl = mK.clone().requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    hfin = model._iface[\"h_final\"]\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        l2 = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n",
        "            model.lm_head(model.ln_final(hfin + model.iface_Dterm(mKl.unsqueeze(0)).unsqueeze(1)))[:, -1, :], target)\n",
        "    mbarK = _t.autograd.grad(l2, mKl, retain_graph=True)[0].detach().reshape(-1)\n",
        "    mbars = [None] * (K + 1)\n",
        "    mbars[K] = mbarK\n",
        "    # Direct head-path seed (paper Phase 3 region-local backward): last-region\n",
        "    # hidden states reach logits without passing mK, so the suffix scan starts\n",
        "    # from this boundary term; earlier regions reach loss only via the chain.\n",
        "    hseed = hfin.clone().requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        lh = _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n",
        "            model.lm_head(model.ln_final(hseed + model.iface_Dterm(mK.unsqueeze(0)).unsqueeze(1)))[:, -1, :], target)\n",
        "    hbar = _t.autograd.grad(lh, hseed, retain_graph=True)[0].detach()\n",
        "    plast = msvals[K - 1].detach().reshape(-1).requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        xinL = xemb + model.iface_decs[K - 1](plast.unsqueeze(0)).unsqueeze(1)\n",
        "        hL = xinL\n",
        "        for i in groups[K - 1]:\n",
        "            hL = model.blocks[i](hL)\n",
        "        sseed = (hL.reshape(-1) * hbar.reshape(-1)).sum()\n",
        "    dseed = _t.autograd.grad(sseed, plast, retain_graph=True)[0].detach().reshape(-1)\n",
        "    mbars[K - 1] = Js[K - 1].T @ mbars[K] + dseed\n",
        "    for k in range(K - 2, -1, -1):\n",
        "        mbars[k] = Js[k].T @ mbars[k + 1]\n",
        "    errs = []\n",
        "    for k in range(K):\n",
        "        mk = msvals[k].detach().reshape(-1).requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "        with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "            x_in = xemb + model.iface_decs[k](mk.unsqueeze(0)).unsqueeze(1)\n",
        "            h = x_in\n",
        "            for i in groups[k]:\n",
        "                h = model.blocks[i](h)\n",
        "            pooled = h.mean(1)\n",
        "            out = model.iface_lns[k](mk.unsqueeze(0) + model.iface_alphas[k] * model.iface_encs[k](pooled))\n",
        "            s = (out.reshape(-1) * mbars[k + 1]).sum()\n",
        "            if k == K - 1:\n",
        "                s = s + (h.reshape(-1) * hbar.reshape(-1)).sum()\n",
        "        # Whole-vector alpha: autograd.grad needs leaf inputs, so the K-vector (leaf) is differentiated and component k is compared; a non-leaf slice alphas[k] carries no graph link.\n",
        "        iplist = [model.iface_decs[k].weight] + ([model.iface_decs[k].bias] if model.iface_decs[k].bias is not None else []) + [model.iface_encs[k].weight] + ([model.iface_encs[k].bias] if model.iface_encs[k].bias is not None else []) + [model.iface_lns[k].weight, model.iface_lns[k].bias, model.iface_alphas]\n",
        "        gs = _t.autograd.grad(s, iplist, retain_graph=True)\n",
        "        for p, gg in zip(iplist, gs):\n",
        "            if p is model.iface_alphas:\n",
        "                errs.append(float(abs(gg[k].item() - refmap[p][k].item())))\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                errs.append(float(((gg - refmap[p]).abs().max()).item()))\n",
        "    m0r = msvals[0].detach().reshape(-1).requires_grad_(True)\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        s0 = (_t.tanh(model.iface_E0(xemb.mean(1))) * mbars[0]).sum()\n",
        "    for p in list(model.iface_E0.parameters()):\n",
        "        gg = _t.autograd.grad(s0, p, retain_graph=True)[0]\n",
        "        errs.append(float(((gg - refmap[p]).abs().max()).item()))\n",
        "    with _t.enable_grad():\n",
        "        ht = hfin + model.iface_Dterm(mK.clone().requires_grad_(True).unsqueeze(0)).unsqueeze(1)\n",
        "        st = (ht.reshape(-1) * _t.autograd.grad(\n",
        "            _t.nn.functional.cross_entropy(model.lm_head(model.ln_final(ht))[:, -1, :], target), ht, retain_graph=True)[0].reshape(-1)).sum()\n",
        "    for p in list(model.iface_Dterm.parameters()):\n",
        "        gg = _t.autograd.grad(st, p, retain_graph=True)[0]\n",
        "        errs.append(float(((gg - refmap[p]).abs().max()).item()))\n",
        "    return {\"K\": K, \"r\": r, \"max_abs\": max(errs) if errs else None,\n",
        "            \"parity_ok\": bool(errs and max(errs) < 1e-4)}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: LBI interface path on the ONE compiled model | runs the parity leg the compiled Interface provides (dense: BPPSA full-rank; bounded: native r-dim) + one small-scale step-train leg with weights restored afterwards | the OTHER interface is a cross-path run (SKIP-once-per-path note, not a fake gap) | emits outputs/lbi_interface_results.json | plain codeblock, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "\"\"\"Benchmarks state what each path is FOR and what the paper expects it to DO.\"\"\"\n",
        "def run_lbi_interface_benchmark(make_model, ids, target_id, r=4, per_region=2, seed=0, small_steps=50, out_path=\"outputs/lbi_interface_results.json\"):\n",
        "    import json as _j\n",
        "    import time as _t\n",
        "    import torch as _tt\n",
        "    from pathlib import Path as _P\n",
        "    t0 = _t.time()\n",
        "    _tt.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    purpose = {\"dense_path\": \"BPPSA-regime exactness: scan backward == autograd on full boundary states; O(d^3) cost recorded, never run for speed\", \"bounded_path\": \"native bottleneck: r-dim scan; parity exact with interface params covered by VJPs\", \"claims_from_paper\": {\"parity\": \"scan grads == autograd grads (Table 5: f32 cos>0.99999, rel<2e-7)\", \"quality\": \"LBI within 0.16-0.35 CE of dense at paper scale (Table 2; small scale here is the compiled path only - the cross-path gap is recorded, not simulated)\"}, \"reproducibility\": \"runner seeds its own draws; the shared model gets state_dict restore after the small-scale leg so later runners see pristine weights\"}\n",
        "    model = make_model()\n",
        "    bounded = hasattr(model, \"region_groups\")\n",
        "    iface = \"bounded\" if bounded else \"dense\"\n",
        "    parity = (lbi_native_parity(model, ids, target_id) if bounded\n",
        "              else lbi_dense_parity(model, ids, lbi_partition(len(model.blocks), per_region), target_id))\n",
        "    other = ({\"status\": \"not-on-path\",\n",
        "              \"reason\": \"the %s interface is not compiled in this run; run the notebook with Interface::%s for its parity leg\" % (\"dense\" if bounded else \"bounded\", \"dense\" if bounded else \"bounded\")})\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    def _brief_check(m, steps):\n",
        "        sd = {k: v.detach().clone() for k, v in m.state_dict().items()}\n",
        "        m.train()\n",
        "        opt = _tt.optim.AdamW(m.parameters(), lr=3e-3)\n",
        "        ce = _tt.nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
        "        last = None\n",
        "        for s in range(steps):\n",
        "            xb = _tt.tensor([ids], dtype=_tt.long).to(dev)\n",
        "            opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "            lg = m(xb)\n",
        "            if lg.dim() == 3:\n",
        "                loss = ce(lg[:, :-1, :].reshape(-1, lg.shape[-1]), xb[:, 1:].reshape(-1))\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                loss = ce(lg, xb[0, -1:])\n",
        "            loss.backward()\n",
        "            opt.step()\n",
        "            last = float(loss.detach())\n",
        "        m.load_state_dict(sd)\n",
        "        m.eval()\n",
        "        return last\n",
        "    ce = _brief_check(model, small_steps)\n",
        "    res = {\"paper\": \"arXiv:2605.09204\", \"seed\": seed, \"interface\": iface, \"r\": r, \"purpose\": purpose,\n",
        "           \"parity\": parity, \"other_interface\": other, \"small\": {\"ce\": ce},\n",
        "           \"seconds\": round(_t.time() - t0, 1)}\n",
        "    _P(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P(out_path).write_text(_j.dumps(res, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "    print(_j.dumps({\"interface\": iface, \"parity_ok\": parity[\"parity_ok\"], \"ce\": ce}, indent=2))\n",
        "    return res\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# One model compiles per run; the runner measures the path that exists and\n",
        "# records the other interface as a cross-path run (no fake gap).\n",
        "_ids26b = bench_ids(globals(), 256)\n",
        "BENCH_RESULTS.append(live_call(\n",
        "    'lbi_interface', run_lbi_interface_benchmark,\n",
        "    make_model=lambda: model,\n",
        "    ids=_ids26b, target_id=_ids26b[-1]))"
      ]
    },
