      "source": [
        "## 27. KV Cache Optimization - arXiv:2603.20397 (Xu, Khaira, Singh, Dell 2026, survey, 20 Mar 2026)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** A 28-technique survey of KV-cache optimization in 5 categories (Tables 1-6; there is no Table 7): cache eviction (9), cache compression (4), hybrid memory (7), new attention calculation (4, Table 5), combination methods (4, \u00a73.5). Background fixes notation: keys/values append per token (Fig.2, O(T) per head per layer), KV_per_token = 2*H*D*B*L and cache size = per_token * context (Eq.1-2), attention scores/weights/output (Eq.3-5, \u00a72.3). Fig.4 (causal matrix for 'The apple tastes sweet', sweet->apple 0.65) shows the non-uniform importance that motivates selective eviction; Fig.6 is the H2O framework (heavy-hitter + recent balance, greedy lowest-score eviction). Table 6 records per-technique memory/speed/accuracy claims; \u00a75 maps 8 deployment scenarios to techniques.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** the survey itself has NO public code (searched, see graded 14_RepoAudit); 25 of 28 techniques have official repos (verified pages: shadowpa0327/Palu, ydyhello/TailorKV, CommediaJW/CLO). No-public-code: InfiniPot, HashEvict, LayerKV. Discrepancies recorded in graded audit and kept here: ref [4] miscitation, KIVI cited without arXiv ID (actual 2402.02750), INF2 released as HILOS, CLO also circulated as LiteCache, Q-Hitter without arXiv (MLSys 2024), MiniCache absent from \u00a73.2 prose, RocketKV HAS/HSA naming, Kimi 6.3x vs 6x, Table-6 baselines without references.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): three stackable axes + one Attn extension.** Eviction, compression, and placement are mutually exclusive WITHIN each axis (one policy per run: pick 1 evictor, 1 compressor, 1 placer) and freely stackable ACROSS axes (evict-then-compress-then-place, the survey's own pipeline order), so they compile as the KVCacheEvict (10 values), KVCacheCompress (5 values), and KVCachePlace (8 values) axes declared in the file header, with one Impl per value; each Impl is the policy delta only (a selector/transform/planner class, never a model copy). The 4 attention mechanisms extend the existing Attn axis (they are mutually exclusive attention kernels at the same Head site) as subclasses of the existing Head that reuse its projections and change ONLY the scoring. Combination methods (FlexGen, Q-Hitter, ShadowKV, TailorKV) are NOT axes: they are plain always-present compositions of axis values plus their unique glue (zigzag schedule, unified score, landmarks, layer regimes). Hardware-bound methods (INF2, Oneiros, CLO, LayerKV, KVPR, InfiniGen, PagedAttention) are faithful POLICY SIMULATORS (declared): tier schedules, transfer volumes, and overlap feasibility are computed exactly; wall-clock/hardware constants are labeled stand-ins, never measured claims. The shared cache substrate (prefill capture, Eq.1-2 accounting, mass/error metrics) is plain orchestrator code.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Technique -> Impl -> original paper -> repo map\n",
        "\n",
        "| Survey technique | Survey table | Original paper | Impl value | Official repo |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| H2O | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2306.14048 | KVCacheEvict::h2o | FMInference/H2O |\n",
        "| SnapKV | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2404.14469 | KVCacheEvict::snapkv | FasterDecoding/SnapKV |\n",
        "| Ada-KV | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2407.11550 | KVCacheEvict::adakv | FFY0/AdaKV |\n",
        "| NACL | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2408.03675 | KVCacheEvict::nacl | PaddlePaddle/Research (subdir) |\n",
        "| InfiniPot | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2410.01518 | KVCacheEvict::infinipot | none (no public code) |\n",
        "| HashEvict | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2412.16187 | KVCacheEvict::hashevict | none (no public code) |\n",
        "| MorphKV | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2503.00979 | KVCacheEvict::morphkv | ghadiaravi13/MorphKV |\n",
        "| RocketKV | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2502.14051 | KVCacheEvict::rocketkv | NVlabs/RocketKV |\n",
        "| KVzip | Table 2 (evict) | arXiv:2505.23416 | KVCacheEvict::kvzip | snu-mllab/KVzip |\n",
        "| KIVI | Table 3 (compress) | arXiv:2402.02750 | KVCacheCompress::kivi | jy-yuan/KIVI |\n",
        "| KVQuant | Table 3 (compress) | arXiv:2401.18079 | KVCacheCompress::kvquant | SqueezeAILab/KVQuant |\n",
        "| MiniCache | Table 3 (compress) | arXiv:2405.14366 | KVCacheCompress::minicache | AkideLiu/MiniCache |\n",
        "| PALU | Table 3 (compress) | arXiv:2407.21118 | KVCacheCompress::palu | shadowpa0327/Palu |\n",
        "| PagedAttention | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2309.06180 | KVCachePlace::paged | vllm-project/vllm |\n",
        "| InfiniGen | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2406.19707 | KVCachePlace::infinigen | snu-comparch/InfiniGen |\n",
        "| LayerKV | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2410.00428 | KVCachePlace::layerkv | none (no public code) |\n",
        "| INF2 | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2502.09921 | KVCachePlace::inf2 | hongsunjang/HILOS |\n",
        "| KVPR | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2411.17089 | KVCachePlace::kvpr | chaoyij/KVPR |\n",
        "| Oneiros | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2507.11507 | KVCachePlace::oneiros | UT-SysML/Oneiros |\n",
        "| CLO | Table 4 (hybrid) | arXiv:2511.14510 | KVCachePlace::clo | CommediaJW/CLO |\n",
        "| Linear attention | Table 5 (attn) | arXiv:2006.16236 | Attn::linearatten | idiap/fast-transformers |\n",
        "| Log-linear attention | Table 5 (attn) | arXiv:2506.04761 | Attn::loglinearatten | HanGuo97/log-linear-attention |\n",
        "| Local linear attention | Table 5 (attn) | arXiv:2510.01450 | Attn::locallinearatten | Yifei-Zuo/Flash-LLA |\n",
        "| KIMI linear (KDA) | Table 5 (attn) | arXiv:2510.26692 | Attn::kimilinear | MoonshotAI/Kimi-Linear |\n",
        "| FlexGen | \u00a73.5 (combo) | arXiv:2303.06865 | plain preset (no axis) | FlexGen/FlexGen |\n",
        "| Q-Hitter | \u00a73.5 (combo) | MLSys 2024 | plain preset (no axis) | VITA-Group/Q-Hitter |\n",
        "| ShadowKV | \u00a73.5 (combo) | arXiv:2410.21465 | plain preset (no axis) | ByteDance-Seed/ShadowKV |\n",
        "| TailorKV | \u00a73.5 (combo) | arXiv:2505.19586 | plain preset (no axis) | ydyhello/TailorKV |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Scenario picks carried over (\u00a75):** long-context single requests -> eviction/compression + KIMI; minimal modification -> Ada-KV/SnapKV/KIVI; high throughput -> PagedAttention/Oneiros/ShadowKV/FlexGen/Q-Hitter; edge -> InfiniPot/TailorKV; multi-turn -> RocketKV-MT/KVzip/ShadowKV (NOT H2O/FlexGen); prefill-heavy -> NACL/HashEvict/LayerKV/MiniCache/CLO; accuracy-critical -> hybrid memory (lossless); hardware-specific -> Oneiros/CLO (GH200 PCIe), INF2 (CSD), FlexGen (GPU+CPU+disk).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) harness captures Head.key/Head.value projection outputs; for Attn values whose final k/v diverge from those projections (mla, tpa, tokenformer) the captures are projection-level and the runner records that fidelity note; default-path (vanillaatten-class) captures are exact; (2) recent-window protection in H2O realizes the survey's stated recent+H2 balance; (3) InfiniPot CCD is keep-top-K by CaP+NuC at enforcement; (4) PALU weight factorization is modeled at cache level via SVD; (5) KVQuant NUQ levels are data quantiles; (6) LLA regression is the centered ridge form; the survey prints no LLA equations; (7) KIMI gates are untrained at small scale (paper trains them); the 3:1 hybrid and chunking are recorded, not run; (8) placer timing/rate constants are stand-ins; (9) harness has no RoPE: ShadowKV landmarks and KVQuant pre-RoPE notes use captured keys directly.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT \u00a727 KV-cache substrate (survey \u00a72.2 Eq.1-2, Fig.1-2) | Explicit per-layer per-head cache over the model's OWN Head projections (captured by forward hooks on Head.key/Head.value/Head.query: zero QKV duplication) | Evict/Compress/Place policies plug in below; metrics are the survey metric families: Eq.1-2 exact bytes, retained attention mass, attention-output relative error | Harness is head-layout based (vanillaatten-class MultiHead.heads); runner uses the default path.\n",
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "import math as _m27\n",
        "_attn27 = attn_scores  # compiled-path scores (matmul default; runner uses the default path)\n",
        "class KVCacheHarness:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Explicit KV cache for cache-policy benchmarking.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Prefill runs the compiled model once; hooks capture each Head's actual\n",
        "    Q/K/V projections. Scores are causal softmax of attn_scores(q, k)/sqrt(d)\n",
        "    (survey \u00a72.3 Eqs.3-5). apply() runs evict -> compress -> place in order.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, model, budget=None, bytes_per_elem=4):\n",
        "        self.model = model\n",
        "        self.budget = budget\n",
        "        self.bpe = bytes_per_elem\n",
        "        self.caps = {}\n",
        "        self._hooks = []\n",
        "        self.stats = {}\n",
        "    def _hook(self, mod, key):\n",
        "        def fn(m, inp, out):\n",
        "            self.caps.setdefault(key, []).append(out.detach())\n",
        "        self._hooks.append(mod.register_forward_hook(fn))\n",
        "    def prefill(self, ids):\n",
        "        self.caps, self._hooks, self.stats = {}, [], {}\n",
        "        mh = [b.self_attn for b in self.model.blocks]\n",
        "        self.layers = []\n",
        "        for li, m in enumerate(mh):\n",
        "            hs = [h for h in m.heads]\n",
        "            self.layers.append(hs)\n",
        "            for hi, h in enumerate(hs):\n",
        "                self._hook(h.key, (li, hi, \"k\"))\n",
        "                self._hook(h.value, (li, hi, \"v\"))\n",
        "                self._hook(h.query, (li, hi, \"q\"))\n",
        "        dev = next(self.model.parameters()).device\n",
        "        xb = _t27.tensor([ids], dtype=_t27.long).to(dev)\n",
        "        self.model.eval()\n",
        "        with _t27.no_grad():\n",
        "            self.model(xb)\n",
        "        for h in self._hooks:\n",
        "            h.remove()\n",
        "        self._hooks = []\n",
        "        self.cache = {}\n",
        "        for li, hs in enumerate(self.layers):\n",
        "            for hi in range(len(hs)):\n",
        "                K = self.caps[(li, hi, \"k\")][0].squeeze(0)\n",
        "                V = self.caps[(li, hi, \"v\")][0].squeeze(0)\n",
        "                Q = self.caps[(li, hi, \"q\")][0].squeeze(0)\n",
        "                d = K.shape[-1]\n",
        "                logits = _attn27(Q, K) / _m27.sqrt(d)\n",
        "                T = K.shape[0]\n",
        "                causal = _t27.tril(_t27.ones(T, T, device=K.device)) == 0\n",
        "                logits = logits.masked_fill(causal, float(\"-inf\"))\n",
        "                S = _t27.softmax(logits, dim=-1)\n",
        "                self.cache[(li, hi)] = {\"K\": K, \"V\": V, \"Q\": Q, \"S\": S,\n",
        "                                       \"qlast\": Q[-1], \"head_dim\": d}\n",
        "        self.T = T\n",
        "        self.n_heads_total = sum(len(hs) for hs in self.layers)\n",
        "        self.n_layers = len(self.layers)\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def eq12_bytes(self, kept_per_head=None):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Survey Eq.1-2: KV_per_token = 2*H*D*B*L; size = per_token * ctx.\n",
        "        kept_per_head maps (l,h) -> kept count; None means full cache.\"\"\"\n",
        "        H = len(self.layers[0])\n",
        "        D = self.cache[(0, 0)][\"head_dim\"]\n",
        "        L = self.n_layers\n",
        "        per_token = 2 * H * D * self.bpe * L\n",
        "        full = per_token * self.T\n",
        "        if kept_per_head is None:\n",
        "            return {\"per_token\": per_token, \"full\": full, \"kept\": full, \"ratio\": 1.0}\n",
        "        kept = sum(int(kept_per_head[k]) for k in kept_per_head)\n",
        "        avg_ctx = kept / max(1, self.n_heads_total)\n",
        "        return {\"per_token\": per_token, \"full\": full,\n",
        "                \"kept\": int(per_token * avg_ctx), \"ratio\": kept / max(1, self.n_heads_total * self.T)}\n",
        "    def retained_mass(self, kept, rows_last=8):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Mean retained attention mass over the last rows_last query rows.\"\"\"\n",
        "        out = {}\n",
        "        for key, c in self.cache.items():\n",
        "            S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "            rows = S[max(0, self.T - rows_last):]\n",
        "            k = _t27.as_tensor(sorted(int(i) for i in kept[key]), dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "            out[key] = float(rows[:, k].sum() / rows.sum())\n",
        "        return out\n",
        "    def attn_output_error(self, kept):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Relative error of next-token attention output: full vs kept subset.\"\"\"\n",
        "        out = {}\n",
        "        for key, c in self.cache.items():\n",
        "            K, V, S = c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"], c[\"S\"]\n",
        "            full = S[-1] @ V\n",
        "            k = _t27.as_tensor(sorted(int(i) for i in kept[key]), dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "            lk = (_attn27(c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0), K[k]) / _m27.sqrt(c[\"head_dim\"]))\n",
        "            w = _t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1)\n",
        "            approx = (w @ V[k]).squeeze(0)\n",
        "            out[key] = float((full - approx).norm() / (full.norm() + 1e-12))\n",
        "        return out\n",
        "def kvc_sym_quant(x, bits, red_dim):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Symmetric integer quantization with scales along red_dim; returns (x_hat, meta).\"\"\"\n",
        "    qmax = float(2 ** (bits - 1) - 1)\n",
        "    scale = x.abs().amax(dim=red_dim, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-12) / qmax\n",
        "    q = (x / scale).round().clamp(-qmax - 1, qmax)\n",
        "    return q * scale, {\"bits\": bits, \"elems\": int(x.numel())}\n",
        "def kvc_slerp(u, v, alpha=0.5):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Spherical interpolation of two vectors (MiniCache cross-layer merge).\"\"\"\n",
        "    un = u / (u.norm() + 1e-12)\n",
        "    vn = v / (v.norm() + 1e-12)\n",
        "    th = (un * vn).sum().clamp(-1.0, 1.0).acos()\n",
        "    s = th.sin().clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "    w0 = ((1.0 - alpha) * th).sin() / s\n",
        "    w1 = (alpha * th).sin() / s\n",
        "    mag = 0.5 * (u.norm() + v.norm())\n",
        "    return mag * (w0 * un + w1 * vn), float(th)\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::none{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"No eviction baseline (full cache; survey \u00a73 policies compare against full attention).\"\"\"\n",
        "class NoneEvictor:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Keep every token: lossless reference for memory/quality deltas.\"\"\"\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        return _t27.arange(T)  # no eviction: the full-cache baseline\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::h2o{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"H2O heavy-hitter eviction (Zhang et al., arXiv:2306.14048; survey \u00a73.1/Fig.6/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Survey prose: greedy budget management - append while space remains; once full,\n",
        "score every cached token INCLUDING the new one by accumulated attention and\n",
        "discard the lowest score; the policy balances recent tokens with heavy-hitter\n",
        "(H2) tokens. Recent-window protection below realizes that stated balance.\"\"\"\n",
        "class H2OEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, recent_w=6, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        recent = _t27.arange(max(0, T - recent_w), T)\n",
        "        mask = _t27.ones(T, dtype=_t27.bool)\n",
        "        mask[recent] = False\n",
        "        pool = _t27.nonzero(mask, as_tuple=True)[0]\n",
        "        n_h2 = min(int(budget - recent.numel()), int(pool.numel()))\n",
        "        top = _t27.topk(scores[pool], n_h2).indices if n_h2 > 0 else pool[:0]\n",
        "        keep = _t27.cat([pool[top], recent])\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(keep).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::snapkv{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"SnapKV observation-window eviction (Li et al., arXiv:2404.14469; survey \u00a73.1/Fig.7/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: \"Retain critical tokens and their context\", applied after prefill:\n",
        "the observation window votes on prefix tokens; 1D pooling clusters neighbors\n",
        "of the selected tokens; the window itself is always retained.\"\"\"\n",
        "class SnapKVEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, win=None, window=8, pool=2, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        W = min(window, T)\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        votes = win.sum(0) if win is not None else scores\n",
        "        prefix = T - W\n",
        "        n_prefix = max(0, min(int(budget - W), prefix))\n",
        "        top = _t27.topk(votes[:prefix], n_prefix).indices if n_prefix > 0 else votes[:0]\n",
        "        keep = set(int(i) for i in top.tolist())\n",
        "        for i in list(keep):\n",
        "            for d in range(1, pool + 1):\n",
        "                if i - d >= 0:\n",
        "                    keep.add(i - d)\n",
        "                if i + d < prefix:\n",
        "                    keep.add(i + d)\n",
        "        keep.update(range(prefix, T))\n",
        "        ranked = sorted(keep, key=lambda i: (-float(votes[i]), i))\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(_t27.tensor(ranked[:budget], dtype=_t27.long)).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::nacl{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"NACL hybrid proxy+random eviction (Chen et al., arXiv:2408.03675; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: \"Hybrid Proxy and Random Eviction\" in a single global shot during\n",
        "prefill (O(1) single-shot per Table 6): proxy tokens score the prefix once;\n",
        "top scorers are kept and the remainder of the budget is filled by sampling\n",
        "from the proxy-score distribution. Fix to paper (2408.03675): the random\n",
        "component is UNIFORM random over the evicted remainder, not importance-sampled.\"\"\"\n",
        "class NACLEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, prox=None, proxy_n=4, rand_frac=0.25, seed=0, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        P = prox[:proxy_n].sum(0) if prox is not None else scores\n",
        "        n_top = max(1, int(round(budget * (1.0 - rand_frac))))\n",
        "        top = _t27.topk(P, min(n_top, T)).indices\n",
        "        rest = _t27.tensor([i for i in range(T) if i not in set(top.tolist())], dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "        n_rand = min(int(budget - top.numel()), rest.numel())\n",
        "        g = _t27.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "        pick = rest[_t27.randperm(rest.numel(), generator=g)[:n_rand]] if n_rand > 0 else rest[:0]\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(_t27.cat([top, pick])).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::infinipot{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"InfiniPot continual context distillation (Kim et al., arXiv:2410.01518; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: fixed-size \"pot\" with continual distillation (CaP = catalyst-prompt\n",
        "attention, NuC = key novelty). Distillation here is keep-top-K by the combined\n",
        "score at each budget enforcement (documented harness realization of CCD).\"\"\"\n",
        "class InfiniPotEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, K=None, cap_lambda=0.5, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        nov = _t27.zeros(T)\n",
        "        if K is not None and T > 1:\n",
        "            nov[1:] = (K[1:] - K[:-1]).norm(dim=-1)\n",
        "            nov = (nov - nov.mean()) / (nov.std() + 1e-12)\n",
        "        acc = (scores - scores.mean()) / (scores.std() + 1e-12)\n",
        "        comb = acc + cap_lambda * nov\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(_t27.topk(comb, budget).indices).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::hashevict{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"HashEvict pre-attention LSH eviction (Liu et al., arXiv:2412.16187; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: attention-free ranking via locality-sensitive hashing; token\n",
        "importance estimated by the SUMMED Hamming distance between SimHash codes\n",
        "of each key and the current query over k parallel receivers (bits=16,\n",
        "n_recv=4 default) - no full attention is ever materialized.\"\"\"\n",
        "class HashEvictEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, K=None, qlast=None, bits=16, seed=1, n_recv=4, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        ham = 0\n",
        "        for k in range(n_recv):\n",
        "            g = _t27.Generator().manual_seed(seed + k)\n",
        "            G = _t27.randn(int(K.shape[-1]), bits, generator=g)\n",
        "            Hk = (K @ G) > 0\n",
        "            Hq = (qlast.unsqueeze(0) @ G) > 0\n",
        "            ham = ham + (Hk != Hq).sum(-1)\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(_t27.topk(-ham.to(_t27.float), budget).indices).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::morphkv{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"MorphKV correlation-aware selection (Ghadia et al., arXiv:2503.00979; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: constant-sized cache for long responses, removing early-token bias:\n",
        "a fixed recent window plus old tokens ranked by fused recent-query attention\n",
        "(SumFusion default; MaxFusion available), deliberately not by whole-history mass.\"\"\"\n",
        "class MorphKVEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, win=None, window=8, fusion=\"sum\", **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        W = min(window, T)\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        agg = win.sum(0) if fusion == \"sum\" else win.max(0).values\n",
        "        old = agg[: T - W]\n",
        "        n_old = max(0, min(int(budget - W), old.numel()))\n",
        "        top = _t27.topk(old, n_old).indices if n_old > 0 else old[:0]\n",
        "        keep = _t27.cat([top, _t27.arange(T - W, T)])\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(keep).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::rocketkv{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"RocketKV two-stage compression (Behnam et al., arXiv:2502.14051; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: permanent coarse eviction as in SnapKV (stage 1), then fine-grain\n",
        "dynamic selection with hybrid sparse attention (stage 2): surviving tokens\n",
        "are grouped into pages carrying per-page max/min keys; pages are ranked by\n",
        "the current query against page representatives and fetched until the budget\n",
        "fills. (Table 6 claims up to 400x compression at decode.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class RocketKVEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, win=None, K=None, qlast=None, window=8, page=4, coarse_mult=2, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        W = min(window, T)\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        votes = win.sum(0) if win is not None else scores\n",
        "        K1 = min(T, max(budget, coarse_mult * budget))\n",
        "        cand = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(votes, K1).indices.tolist())\n",
        "        cand.update(range(T - W, T))\n",
        "        pages = {}\n",
        "        for i in sorted(cand):\n",
        "            pages.setdefault(i // page, []).append(i)\n",
        "        reps = []\n",
        "        for v in pages.values():\n",
        "            sub = K[_t27.tensor(v)]\n",
        "            reps.append(_t27.cat([sub.max(0).values, sub.min(0).values], dim=-1))\n",
        "        rep = _t27.stack(reps)\n",
        "        ps = _t27.softmax((rep @ _t27.cat([qlast, qlast], dim=-1)), dim=0)\n",
        "        order = _t27.argsort(ps, descending=True)\n",
        "        keys = list(pages.keys())\n",
        "        keep = []\n",
        "        for o in order.tolist():\n",
        "            keep.extend(pages[keys[o]])\n",
        "            if len(keep) >= budget:\n",
        "                break\n",
        "        keep = keep[:budget]\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(_t27.tensor(keep, dtype=_t27.long)).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::kvzip{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"KVzip query-agnostic compression (Kim et al., arXiv:2505.23416; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: context-reconstruction importance = maximum cross-attention any\n",
        "prefill query gives a token; future queries are unknown, so the score uses\n",
        "only past queries (max over rows, not columns) - genuinely query-agnostic.\n",
        "(Table 6: up to 70% eviction, negligible loss; overhead amortized over queries.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class KVzipEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, Smat=None, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        if budget >= T:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        imp = Smat.max(0).values if Smat is not None else scores\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(_t27.topk(imp, budget).indices).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::adakv{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"AdaKV adaptive budget allocation (Feng et al., arXiv:2407.11550; survey \u00a73.1/Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 2: budget is allocated ACROSS attention heads instead of fixed per-head:\n",
        "layer-scope allocator; per-head importance here is score dispersion (concentrated\n",
        "heads receive more budget); each head then keeps its own top scorers.\n",
        "(Table 6: 4x cache reduction, ~5% quality improvement; allocation within layers only.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class AdaKVEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"layer\"\n",
        "    def select_layer(self, acc_list, budget_total, temp=1.0, **kw):\n",
        "        H = len(acc_list)\n",
        "        T = int(acc_list[0].numel())\n",
        "        per = max(1, budget_total // H)\n",
        "        if per >= T:\n",
        "            return [_t27.arange(T) for _ in acc_list]\n",
        "        disp = _t27.stack([a.std() for a in acc_list])\n",
        "        w = _t27.softmax(disp / temp, dim=0)\n",
        "        raw = (w * budget_total).floor().long()\n",
        "        raw = _t27.clamp(raw, 1, T)\n",
        "        left = int(budget_total - int(raw.sum()))\n",
        "        order = _t27.argsort(w, descending=True)\n",
        "        i = 0\n",
        "        while left != 0 and i < 4 * H:\n",
        "            h = int(order[i % H])\n",
        "            if left > 0 and raw[h] < T:\n",
        "                raw[h] += 1\n",
        "                left -= 1\n",
        "            elif left < 0 and raw[h] > 1:\n",
        "                raw[h] -= 1\n",
        "                left += 1\n",
        "            i += 1\n",
        "        return [_t27.sort(_t27.topk(a, int(raw[h])).indices).values for h, a in enumerate(acc_list)]\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, **kw):\n",
        "        return self.select_layer([scores], budget, **kw)[0]\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::none{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"No compression baseline (fp32 resident; survey \u00a73 methods compare quality against full precision).\"\"\"\n",
        "class NoneCompressor:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Identity storage: lossless reference for memory/quality deltas.\"\"\"\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def compress(self, K, V, **kw):\n",
        "        n = int(K.numel() + V.numel())\n",
        "        return K, V, {\"bytes\": n * 4, \"bits_per_elem\": 32, \"recon_k\": 0.0, \"recon_v\": 0.0}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::kivi{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"KIVI asymmetric quantization (Liu et al., arXiv:2402.02750; survey \u00a73.2/Fig.8/Table 3).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 3: keys per-channel, values per-token; the most recent tokens (a\n",
        "sliding window of W) stay fp16 while the rest are 2-bit (paper's residual\n",
        "window). Paper: tuning-free 2-bit (survey \u00a75.2 minimal-modification pick).\n",
        "(Table 6 claims: 2.6x peak memory, 2.35-3.47x throughput, <2% accuracy drop.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class KIVICompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def compress(self, K, V, bits=2, window=16, **kw):\n",
        "        T = K.shape[0]\n",
        "        W = max(0, min(int(window), T))\n",
        "        if W >= T:\n",
        "            Kh, Vh = K, V\n",
        "            nb = int((K.numel() + V.numel()) * 2)\n",
        "            return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": nb, \"bits_per_elem\": 16, \"residual_frac\": 1.0,\n",
        "                            \"recon_k\": 0.0, \"recon_v\": 0.0}\n",
        "        main_k, resid_k = K[:T - W], K[T - W:]\n",
        "        main_v, resid_v = V[:T - W], V[T - W:]\n",
        "        Kq, mk = kvc_sym_quant(main_k, bits, red_dim=0)\n",
        "        Vq, mv = kvc_sym_quant(main_v, bits, red_dim=1)\n",
        "        Kh = _t27.cat([Kq, resid_k], 0)\n",
        "        Vh = _t27.cat([Vq, resid_v], 0)\n",
        "        nb = int((mk[\"elems\"] + mv[\"elems\"]) * bits / 8 + (resid_k.numel() + resid_v.numel()) * 2)\n",
        "        rk = float((K - Kh).norm() / (K.norm() + 1e-12))\n",
        "        rv = float((V - Vh).norm() / (V.norm() + 1e-12))\n",
        "        return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": nb, \"bits_per_elem\": bits, \"residual_frac\": W / max(1, T),\n",
        "                        \"recon_k\": rk, \"recon_v\": rv}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::kvquant{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"KVQuant non-uniform quantization (Hooper et al., arXiv:2401.18079; survey \u00a73.2/Table 3).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 3: NUQ levels on pre-RoPE keys per-channel and values per-token; top 1%\n",
        "outliers isolated into a sparse fp16 store; the attention sink (first token)\n",
        "kept fp16. Levels below are data quantiles (documented stand-in for the\n",
        "paper's sensitivity-weighted NUQ tables). Harness has no RoPE, so keys are\n",
        "taken as captured (noted, not hidden).\"\"\"\n",
        "class KVQuantCompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def _nuq(self, x, bits, red_dim):\n",
        "        L = 2 ** bits\n",
        "        probs = _t27.linspace(0.0, 1.0, L)\n",
        "        lv = _t27.quantile(x, probs, dim=red_dim)\n",
        "        if red_dim == 1:  # torch.quantile fronts the quantile dim: (L,T)->(T,L)\n",
        "            lv = lv.T\n",
        "        if red_dim == 0:\n",
        "            idx = _t27.argmin((x.unsqueeze(0) - lv.unsqueeze(1)).abs(), dim=0)\n",
        "            col = _t27.arange(x.shape[-1], device=x.device)\n",
        "            return lv[idx, col], int(x.numel())\n",
        "        idx = _t27.argmin((x.unsqueeze(-1) - lv.unsqueeze(1)).abs(), dim=-1)\n",
        "        row = _t27.arange(x.shape[0], device=x.device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
        "        return lv[row, idx], int(x.numel())\n",
        "    def compress(self, K, V, bits=3, outlier_frac=0.01, **kw):\n",
        "        Kh, _ = self._nuq(K, bits, 0)\n",
        "        Vh, _ = self._nuq(V, bits, 1)\n",
        "        sparse, sink = 0, 0\n",
        "        for X, Xh in ((K, Kh), (V, Vh)):\n",
        "            thr = _t27.quantile(X.abs(), 1.0 - outlier_frac)\n",
        "            m = X.abs() > thr\n",
        "            Xh[m] = X[m]\n",
        "            sparse += int(m.sum())\n",
        "            Xh[0] = X[0]\n",
        "            sink += int(X.shape[-1])\n",
        "        main = int((K.numel() + V.numel()) * bits / 8)\n",
        "        nb = main + (sparse + sink) * 2\n",
        "        return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": nb, \"bits_per_elem\": bits, \"sparse_elems\": sparse,\n",
        "                        \"sink_elems\": sink, \"recon_k\": float((K - Kh).norm() / (K.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                        \"recon_v\": float((V - Vh).norm() / (V.norm() + 1e-12))}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::minicache{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"MiniCache cross-layer KV merge (Liu et al., arXiv:2405.14366; survey Tables 3/6).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 3: adjacent layers' KV merged when similar; highly distinct pairs stay\n",
        "full precision. Merge here is SLERP at alpha=0.5 on tokens whose key AND value\n",
        "cosine exceed tau; each merged token stores one shared vector + the two\n",
        "original angles (documented storage model of the paper's direction/magnitude\n",
        "retention). Note: the method is never cited in \u00a73.2 prose (Tables 3/6 only).\"\"\"\n",
        "class MiniCacheCompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"layerpair\"\n",
        "    def compress_pair(self, KV1, KV2, tau=0.9, **kw):\n",
        "        K1, V1 = KV1\n",
        "        K2, V2 = KV2\n",
        "        T, d = K1.shape\n",
        "        ck = (K1 * K2).sum(-1) / (K1.norm(dim=-1) * K2.norm(dim=-1) + 1e-12)\n",
        "        cv = (V1 * V2).sum(-1) / (V1.norm(dim=-1) * V2.norm(dim=-1) + 1e-12)\n",
        "        merge = (ck > tau) & (cv > tau)\n",
        "        K1h, V1h, K2h, V2h = K1.clone(), V1.clone(), K2.clone(), V2.clone()\n",
        "        thetas = []\n",
        "        for t in _t27.nonzero(merge, as_tuple=True)[0].tolist():\n",
        "            m, thk = kvc_slerp(K1[t], K2[t])\n",
        "            K1h[t] = m\n",
        "            K2h[t] = m\n",
        "            thetas.append(thk)\n",
        "            m, thv = kvc_slerp(V1[t], V2[t])\n",
        "            V1h[t] = m\n",
        "            V2h[t] = m\n",
        "            thetas.append(thv)\n",
        "        n_merge = int(merge.sum())\n",
        "        shared = n_merge * 2 * d * 4\n",
        "        angles = len(thetas) * 4\n",
        "        separate = (T - n_merge) * 2 * d * 4 * 2\n",
        "        nb = shared + angles + separate\n",
        "        rk = float(((K1 - K1h).norm() + (K2 - K2h).norm()) / (K1.norm() + K2.norm() + 1e-12))\n",
        "        rv = float(((V1 - V1h).norm() + (V2 - V2h).norm()) / (V1.norm() + V2.norm() + 1e-12))\n",
        "        return (K1h, V1h), (K2h, V2h), {\"bytes\": nb, \"merged_tokens\": n_merge,\n",
        "                \"merge_frac\": n_merge / max(1, T), \"recon_k\": rk, \"recon_v\": rv}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::palu{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"PALU low-rank projection (Chang et al., arXiv:2407.21118; survey \u00a73.2/Fig.9/Table 3).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 3: hidden-dimension compression via low-rank projection + reconstruction,\n",
        "per-token per-head-group latent, higher ranks for critical layers. The paper\n",
        "factorizes projection weights (W ~= A B, Fig.9); the harness realizes the same\n",
        "storage model at cache level via SVD of the captured K/V (documented).\"\"\"\n",
        "class PALUCompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def _lr(self, X, r):\n",
        "        U, S, Vh = _t27.linalg.svd(X, full_matrices=False)\n",
        "        lat = U[:, :r] * S[:r].unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "        return lat @ Vh[:r, :], int(X.shape[0] * r + r * X.shape[1])\n",
        "    def compress(self, K, V, rank=None, rank_ratio=0.5, **kw):\n",
        "        d = K.shape[-1]\n",
        "        r = rank or max(1, int(d * rank_ratio))\n",
        "        Kh, ek = self._lr(K, r)\n",
        "        Vh, ev = self._lr(V, r)\n",
        "        return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": (ek + ev) * 4, \"rank\": r,\n",
        "                        \"recon_k\": float((K - Kh).norm() / (K.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                        \"recon_v\": float((V - Vh).norm() / (V.norm() + 1e-12))}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::resident{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"Resident placement baseline: whole KV cache lives on the accelerator (survey \u00a72.2/Eq.2).\n",
        "\n",
        "Offload-based rows in Table 4 report \"no reduction\" against this baseline;\n",
        "it anchors every placer comparison.\"\"\"\n",
        "class ResidentPlacer:\n",
        "    \"\"\"All-GPU bytes, zero transfers, TTFT factor 1.0 by definition.\"\"\"\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, **kw):\n",
        "        full = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        return {\"gpu_bytes\": full, \"cpu_bytes\": 0, \"xfer_bytes\": 0, \"ttft_factor\": 1.0}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::paged{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"PagedAttention block paging (Kwon et al., arXiv:2309.06180; survey \u00a73.3/Fig.10/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: KV paged into fixed blocks (virtual-memory style), cutting\n",
        "fragmentation and enabling cache sharing. Plan: block count, allocated vs\n",
        "used bytes, internal-fragmentation ratio, block-table bytes. (Table 6 claims:\n",
        "lossless, 2-4x throughput at same latency.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class PagedPlacer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, block=16, table_entry=8, **kw):\n",
        "        per = spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        nb = (spec[\"T\"] + block - 1) // block\n",
        "        alloc = nb * block\n",
        "        frag = alloc - spec[\"T\"]\n",
        "        used = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        return {\"block\": block, \"blocks_per_seq\": nb, \"total_blocks\": nb * per,\n",
        "                \"alloc_tokens\": alloc * per, \"frag_tokens\": frag * per,\n",
        "                \"frag_ratio\": frag / max(1, alloc), \"table_bytes\": nb * per * table_entry,\n",
        "                \"gpu_bytes\": used, \"sharing\": \"copy-on-write block sharing enabled (policy flag)\"}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::infinigen{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"InfiniGen dynamic prefetch (Lee et al., arXiv:2406.19707; survey \u00a73.3/Fig.11/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: CPU residency + attention speculation/prefetch of essential chunks\n",
        "only. Plan: chunk the cache, rank chunks by partial-query mass, prefetch\n",
        "top-m; report transfer ratio, savings, and oracle recall of the selection.\n",
        "(Table 6: comparable accuracy above 15% relative KV size.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class InfiniGenPlacer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, chunk=32, keep_frac=0.15, **kw):\n",
        "        T = spec[\"T\"]\n",
        "        full = 2 * T * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        n_chunks = max(1, (T + chunk - 1) // chunk)\n",
        "        m = max(1, int(n_chunks * keep_frac))\n",
        "        rec, mass = 0.0, 0.0\n",
        "        if scores:\n",
        "            agg = _t27.stack([s for s in scores.values()]).mean(0)\n",
        "            cm = _t27.stack([agg[i * chunk:(i + 1) * chunk].max() for i in range(n_chunks)])\n",
        "            top = _t27.topk(cm, min(m, n_chunks)).indices\n",
        "            oracle = _t27.topk(agg, max(1, int(T * keep_frac))).indices\n",
        "            inc = _t27.zeros(T, dtype=_t27.bool)\n",
        "            for c in top.tolist():\n",
        "                inc[c * chunk:(c + 1) * chunk] = True\n",
        "            rec = float(inc[oracle].float().mean())\n",
        "            mass = float(agg[inc].sum() / agg.sum())\n",
        "        return {\"chunk\": chunk, \"n_chunks\": n_chunks, \"prefetch_chunks\": m,\n",
        "                \"xfer_ratio\": m / max(1, n_chunks), \"saving\": 1.0 - m / max(1, n_chunks),\n",
        "                \"oracle_recall\": rec, \"prefetched_mass\": mass,\n",
        "                \"gpu_bytes\": 0, \"cpu_bytes\": full}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::layerkv{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LayerKV layer-wise residency (Xiong et al., arXiv:2410.00428; survey \u00a73.3/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: SLO-aware scheduler balancing GPU/CPU residency per layer to cut\n",
        "queuing. Plan: keep k hot layers resident; the offload of the remaining L-k\n",
        "overlaps prefill; report the overlap-feasible k, TTFT vs no-overlap baseline,\n",
        "and resident bytes. Timing constants are documented stand-ins (policy-level).\"\"\"\n",
        "class LayerKVPlacer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, t_prefill=1.0, t_offload=0.35, **kw):\n",
        "        L = spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        layer_bytes = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"]\n",
        "        base = L * t_prefill + L * t_offload\n",
        "        best = None\n",
        "        for k in range(L, -1, -1):\n",
        "            stall = max(0.0, (L - k) * t_offload - L * t_prefill)\n",
        "            ttft = L * t_prefill + stall\n",
        "            if best is None or ttft <= best[1]:\n",
        "                best = (k, ttft)\n",
        "        k, ttft = best\n",
        "        return {\"gpu_layers\": k, \"cpu_layers\": L - k, \"gpu_bytes\": k * layer_bytes,\n",
        "                \"cpu_bytes\": (L - k) * layer_bytes, \"ttft\": ttft,\n",
        "                \"ttft_factor\": base / max(ttft, 1e-12), \"xfer_bytes\": (L - k) * layer_bytes}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::inf2{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"INF2 attention-near-storage (Jang et al., arXiv:2502.09921; survey \u00a73.3/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: attention computed at the storage tier (CSDs), so KV never crosses\n",
        "PCIe; only queries and new KV move. Plan: baseline fetch-all bytes vs\n",
        "query+append bytes; report KV I/O reduction (Table 6 claims >80%, lossless,\n",
        "3.46x throughput; requires CSD hardware - declared policy simulation).\"\"\"\n",
        "class INF2Placer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, **kw):\n",
        "        kv = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        q = spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        new = 2 * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        moved = q + new\n",
        "        return {\"kv_bytes\": kv, \"xfer_bytes\": moved, \"gpu_bytes\": moved,\n",
        "                \"kv_io_reduction\": 1.0 - moved / max(1, kv), \"storage\": \"CSD-resident KV (simulated)\"}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::kvpr{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"KVPR I/O-aware partial recomputation (Jiang et al., arXiv:2411.17089; survey \u00a73.3/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: partial cache recompute on GPU overlaps async transfer of the rest.\n",
        "Plan: split fraction b recomputed / (1-b) transferred; balance point where\n",
        "the two measurement sets meet; report the balanced split and stall reduction vs\n",
        "transfer-only baseline. Rate constants are documented stand-ins (policy-level).\n",
        "(Table 6: up to 35.8% lower latency, 46.2% higher throughput vs DeepSpeed/HF.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class KVPRPlacer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, c_recomp=1.0, c_xfer=0.6, **kw):\n",
        "        kv = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        b = c_xfer / (c_xfer + c_recomp)\n",
        "        leg = b * c_recomp\n",
        "        base = c_xfer\n",
        "        return {\"recompute_frac\": b, \"transfer_frac\": 1.0 - b, \"overlap_leg\": leg,\n",
        "                \"stall_reduction\": 1.0 - leg / max(base, 1e-12),\n",
        "                \"gpu_bytes\": int(kv * (1.0 - b)), \"recomputed_bytes\": int(kv * b)}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::oneiros{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"Oneiros parameter remapping (Li et al., arXiv:2507.11507; survey \u00a73.3/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: idle models' parameter memory repurposed as KV space for\n",
        "multi-tenant serving. Plan: extra KV budget from remapped idle parameters;\n",
        "report capacity gain over the resident budget. Tenant/idle fractions are\n",
        "documented stand-ins (policy-level simulation, declared).\"\"\"\n",
        "class OneirosPlacer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, idle_frac=0.5, remap_frac=0.9, **kw):\n",
        "        kv = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        extra = spec.get(\"param_bytes\", kv * 4) * idle_frac * remap_frac\n",
        "        return {\"gpu_bytes\": kv, \"remapped_bytes\": int(extra),\n",
        "                \"capacity_gain\": extra / max(1, kv), \"effective_budget_mult\": 1.0 + extra / max(1, kv)}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCachePlace::clo{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"CLO CPU-light offloading (Yi et al., arXiv:2511.14510; survey \u00a73.3/Table 4).\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 4: algorithm-system co-design with head-wise approximate caching and a\n",
        "zero-copy transfer engine; full parallel prefill plus speculative sparse\n",
        "prefetch. Plan: low-entropy heads approximated (1 byte/elem sketch budget),\n",
        "the rest exact; report approximated heads, byte savings, and the engine\n",
        "model factor. Entropy threshold is a documented stand-in (policy-level).\n",
        "(Table 6: 9.3-66.6% throughput over RetroInfer/InfiniGen; near-lossless.)\"\"\"\n",
        "class CLOPlacer:\n",
        "    def plan(self, spec, scores=None, entropy_tau=3.0, sketch_bpe=1, pcie_eff=0.9, **kw):\n",
        "        full = 2 * spec[\"T\"] * spec[\"H\"] * spec[\"hs\"] * spec[\"bpe\"] * spec[\"L\"]\n",
        "        approx, total = 0, 0\n",
        "        if scores:\n",
        "            for s in scores.values():\n",
        "                total += 1\n",
        "                p = (s / (s.sum() + 1e-12)).clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "                ent = float(-(p * p.log()).sum())\n",
        "                if ent < entropy_tau:\n",
        "                    approx += 1\n",
        "            exact_frac = 1.0 - approx / max(1, total)\n",
        "            kept = full * exact_frac + full * (approx / max(1, total)) * sketch_bpe / spec[\"bpe\"]\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            kept, exact_frac = full, 1.0\n",
        "        return {\"approx_heads\": approx, \"exact_frac\": exact_frac, \"gpu_bytes\": int(kept),\n",
        "                \"saving\": 1.0 - kept / max(1, full), \"xfer_bytes\": int(full - kept),\n",
        "                \"engine\": \"zero-copy (simulated, pcie_eff=%.2f)\" % pcie_eff}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT \u00a727 combination presets (survey \u00a73.5) | Plain compositions of the KVCache axes plus each combo's unique glue - NOT new axes | FlexGen = 4-bit groupwise compression + tiered offload + zigzag schedule; Q-Hitter = unified attention\u00d7robustness score + sparse-quantized top-K; ShadowKV = low-rank keys on GPU + values offloaded + landmarks/outliers + sparse fetch; TailorKV = per-layer concentration regimes (quant-friendly vs sparsity-friendly) + double buffering. Each takes a prefilled harness; Impl classes are resolved lazily so every compiled path stays runnable.\n",
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "def kvcache_flexgen_preset(harness, bits=4, group=32, n_batches=4):\n",
        "    \"\"\"FlexGen (Sheng et al., arXiv:2303.06865; survey \u00a73.5): 4-bit groupwise\n",
        "    min/max compression of weights+KV (paper) realized on harness K/V, tiered\n",
        "    residency flags, and zig-zag block scheduling (batches loop inside each\n",
        "    layer): weight loads L instead of L*n_batches. High-throughput design,\n",
        "    not low-latency single-request (survey caveat, kept).\"\"\"\n",
        "    ratios, recs = [], []\n",
        "    for key, c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        for X in (c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"]):\n",
        "            g = X.reshape(-1, group)\n",
        "            qmax = float(2 ** (bits - 1) - 1)\n",
        "            sc = g.abs().amax(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-12) / qmax\n",
        "            Xh = ((g / sc).round().clamp(-qmax - 1, qmax) * sc).reshape(X.shape)\n",
        "            ratios.append(X.numel() * bits / 8 / (X.numel() * 4))\n",
        "            recs.append(float((X - Xh).norm() / (X.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "    L = harness.n_layers\n",
        "    return {\"recipe\": {\"compress\": \"groupwise-%dbit\" % bits, \"place\": \"gpu+cpu+disk tiers\",\n",
        "                       \"schedule\": \"zigzag (batches-inside-layer)\"},\n",
        "            \"compression_ratio\": float(sum(ratios) / max(1, len(ratios))),\n",
        "            \"mean_recon\": float(sum(recs) / max(1, len(recs))),\n",
        "            \"weight_loads_zigzag\": L, \"weight_loads_naive\": L * n_batches,\n",
        "            \"io_factor\": float(L * n_batches) / max(1, L)}\n",
        "def kvcache_qhitter_preset(harness, budget=32, bits=2, seed=0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Q-Hitter (Zhang et al., MLSys 2024; survey \u00a73.5): unified score S from\n",
        "    attention importance x quantization robustness; top-K by S stored\n",
        "    quantized, the rest discarded. The paper's balancing of the two metrics\n",
        "    is realized as S = normalized-attention * robustness (documented stand-in\n",
        "    for the unnamed formula). Reports mass and agreement with attention-only top-K.\"\"\"\n",
        "    S_all, mass, jac = [], [], []\n",
        "    for key, c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        K, V, S = c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"], c[\"S\"]\n",
        "        T = K.shape[0]\n",
        "        attn = S.sum(0)\n",
        "        attn = attn / (attn.sum() + 1e-12)\n",
        "        err = _t27.zeros(T)\n",
        "        for t in range(T):\n",
        "            pair = _t27.cat([K[t], V[t]])\n",
        "            qh, _ = kvc_sym_quant(pair.unsqueeze(0), bits, red_dim=1)\n",
        "            err[t] = float(((pair - qh.squeeze(0)).norm() / (pair.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "        robust = 1.0 / (1.0 + err)\n",
        "        Sscore = attn * robust\n",
        "        keep = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(Sscore, min(budget, T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "        keep_a = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(attn, min(budget, T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "        S_all.append(float(Sscore[_t27.tensor(sorted(keep))].sum()))\n",
        "        mass.append(float(S[-1, _t27.tensor(sorted(keep))].sum()))\n",
        "        jac.append(len(keep & keep_a) / max(1, len(keep | keep_a)))\n",
        "    nb = harness.n_heads_total * budget * 2 * harness.cache[(0, 0)][\"head_dim\"] * bits / 8\n",
        "    return {\"recipe\": {\"select\": \"unified S = attention x robustness\", \"store\": \"%d-bit top-K\" % bits},\n",
        "            \"mean_unified_mass\": float(sum(S_all) / max(1, len(S_all))),\n",
        "            \"mean_lastrow_mass\": float(sum(mass) / max(1, len(mass))),\n",
        "            \"jaccard_vs_attn_only\": float(sum(jac) / max(1, len(jac))), \"quant_bytes\": int(nb)}\n",
        "def kvcache_shadowkv_preset(harness, rank_ratio=0.25, chunk=16, tau=0.5, fetch_frac=0.25):\n",
        "    \"\"\"ShadowKV (Sun et al., arXiv:2410.21465; survey \u00a73.5/Fig.13): SVD on\n",
        "    pre-RoPE keys keeps top-rank on GPU (values offloaded); post-RoPE chunk\n",
        "    landmarks + low-cosine outliers stay on GPU; decode fetches landmark-top\n",
        "    chunks only. Harness has no RoPE (documented): landmarks use captured keys.\"\"\"\n",
        "    gpu, rec, n_out, mass = 0, [], 0, []\n",
        "    for key, c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        K, V, S = c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"], c[\"S\"]\n",
        "        T, d = K.shape\n",
        "        r = max(1, int(min(T, d) * rank_ratio))\n",
        "        U, Sg, Vh = _t27.linalg.svd(K, full_matrices=False)\n",
        "        gpu += (T * r + r * d) * 4\n",
        "        n_chunks = max(1, (T + chunk - 1) // chunk)\n",
        "        lm = _t27.stack([K[i * chunk:(i + 1) * chunk].mean(0) for i in range(n_chunks)])\n",
        "        cs = (K / (K.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 1e-12)) @ (lm / (lm.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 1e-12)).T\n",
        "        best = cs[_t27.arange(T), _t27.tensor([min(i // chunk, n_chunks - 1) for i in range(T)])]\n",
        "        out = best < tau\n",
        "        n_out += int(out.sum())\n",
        "        gpu += int(out.sum()) * 2 * d * 4\n",
        "        q = c[\"qlast\"]\n",
        "        cm = _t27.stack([S[-1, i * chunk:(i + 1) * chunk].sum() for i in range(n_chunks)])\n",
        "        m = max(1, int(n_chunks * fetch_frac))\n",
        "        sel = _t27.topk(cm, min(m, n_chunks)).indices\n",
        "        oracle = _t27.topk(S[-1], max(1, int(T * fetch_frac))).indices\n",
        "        inc = _t27.zeros(T, dtype=_t27.bool)\n",
        "        for cix in sel.tolist():\n",
        "            inc[cix * chunk:(cix + 1) * chunk] = True\n",
        "        rec.append(float(inc[oracle].float().mean()))\n",
        "        mass.append(float(S[-1][inc].sum()))\n",
        "    return {\"recipe\": {\"keys\": \"SVD top-rank on GPU\", \"values\": \"offloaded\",\n",
        "                       \"select\": \"landmark chunks + cosine outliers\"},\n",
        "            \"gpu_bytes\": int(gpu), \"outlier_tokens\": n_out,\n",
        "            \"chunk_recall\": float(sum(rec) / max(1, len(rec))),\n",
        "            \"fetched_mass\": float(sum(mass) / max(1, len(mass)))}\n",
        "def kvcache_tailorkv_preset(harness, top_k=8, bits=2, sparse_keep=32):\n",
        "    \"\"\"TailorKV (Yao et al., arXiv:2505.19586; survey \u00a73.5/Fig.14): per-layer\n",
        "    concentration = sum of top-k last-query scores; below-median layers are\n",
        "    quantization-friendly (aggressive static 2-bit on GPU), above-median are\n",
        "    sparsity-friendly (offloaded, dynamic top-K fetch with double buffering).\"\"\"\n",
        "    conc = {}\n",
        "    for (li, hi), c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        row = c[\"S\"][-1]\n",
        "        conc.setdefault(li, []).append(float(_t27.topk(row, min(top_k, row.numel())).values.sum()))\n",
        "    cl = {li: sum(v) / max(1, len(v)) for li, v in conc.items()}\n",
        "    med = sorted(cl.values())[len(cl) // 2]\n",
        "    qlayers = [li for li, v in cl.items() if v < med]\n",
        "    slayers = [li for li, v in cl.items() if v >= med]\n",
        "    gpu, rec = 0, []\n",
        "    for (li, hi), c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        if li in qlayers:\n",
        "            Kh, _ = kvc_sym_quant(c[\"K\"], bits, red_dim=0)\n",
        "            Vh, _ = kvc_sym_quant(c[\"V\"], bits, red_dim=1)\n",
        "            gpu += int((c[\"K\"].numel() + c[\"V\"].numel()) * bits / 8)\n",
        "            rec.append(float((c[\"K\"] - Kh).norm() / (c[\"K\"].norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            keep = _t27.topk(c[\"S\"][-1], min(sparse_keep, c[\"K\"].shape[0])).indices\n",
        "            gpu += int(keep.numel() * 2 * c[\"head_dim\"] * 4)\n",
        "    return {\"recipe\": {\"quant_layers\": sorted(qlayers), \"sparse_layers\": sorted(slayers),\n",
        "                       \"fetch\": \"dynamic top-K with double buffering (overlap flag)\"},\n",
        "            \"quant_layer_frac\": len(qlayers) / max(1, len(cl)), \"gpu_bytes\": gpu,\n",
        "            \"mean_quant_recon\": float(sum(rec) / max(1, len(rec))), \"overlap\": 1.0}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: KV-cache end-to-end | Prefills ONE harness, then exercises every compiled-path policy it can find (registries auto-collected from globals so partial paths report skips instead of crashing) + the 4 attention heads vs softmax + 4 combination presets | emits outputs/kvcache_results.json | plain orchestrator cell, no Impl tag by design | Small-scale mechanism metrics (Eq.1-2 bytes, retained mass, output error, recon, policy stats); Table-6 magnitudes are recorded as paper-reported claims, never as small-scale results.\n",
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "import json as _j27\n",
        "import time as _time27\n",
        "from pathlib import Path as _P27\n",
        "_EVICT27 = [\"NoneEvictor\", \"H2OEvictor\", \"SnapKVEvictor\", \"NACLEvictor\", \"InfiniPotEvictor\",\n",
        "             \"HashEvictEvictor\", \"MorphKVEvictor\", \"RocketKVEvictor\", \"KVzipEvictor\", \"AdaKVEvictor\"]\n",
        "_COMP27 = [\"NoneCompressor\", \"KIVICompressor\", \"KVQuantCompressor\", \"MiniCacheCompressor\", \"PALUCompressor\"]\n",
        "_PLACE27 = [\"ResidentPlacer\", \"PagedPlacer\", \"InfiniGenPlacer\", \"LayerKVPlacer\", \"INF2Placer\",\n",
        "            \"KVPRPlacer\", \"OneirosPlacer\", \"CLOPlacer\"]\n",
        "_ATTN27 = [\"LinearAttnHead\", \"LogLinearAttnHead\", \"LocalLinearAttnHead\", \"KimiLinearHead\"]\n",
        "_CLAIM27 = {\"NoneEvictor\": \"baseline (full cache)\",\n",
        " \"H2OEvictor\": \"reported: 5-10x mem, 29x thr, <=1.9x lat vs FlexGen, comparable acc\",\n",
        " \"SnapKVEvictor\": \"reported: 8.2x mem efficiency, 3.6x generation speedup\",\n",
        " \"NACLEvictor\": \"reported: 5x KV cut, O(1) single-shot eviction, 95% retention\",\n",
        " \"InfiniPotEvictor\": \"reported: 4k-1M ctx, consistent perf in fixed pot\",\n",
        " \"HashEvictEvictor\": \"reported: 30-70% compression, 1.5-2x prefill speedup\",\n",
        " \"MorphKVEvictor\": \"reported: 5x over full-attention, 4.68x vs SnapKV\",\n",
        " \"RocketKVEvictor\": \"reported: up to 400x compression, 3.7x speedup\",\n",
        " \"KVzipEvictor\": \"reported: 70% eviction, 2x FlashAttention latency cut, negligible loss\",\n",
        " \"AdaKVEvictor\": \"reported: 4x reduction, ~5% quality gain (within-layer allocation)\",\n",
        " \"NoneCompressor\": \"baseline (fp32)\",\n",
        " \"KIVICompressor\": \"reported: 2.6x peak mem, 2.35-3.47x thr, <2% acc drop\",\n",
        " \"KVQuantCompressor\": \"reported: 3.7-6.9x mem, <0.1 ppl degradation at 3-bit\",\n",
        " \"MiniCacheCompressor\": \"reported: 41% mem cut, ~5x thr, minimal loss\",\n",
        " \"PALUCompressor\": \"reported: ~50% compression, 1.89x (RoPE) / 2.91x (w/ quant)\",\n",
        " \"ResidentPlacer\": \"baseline (all-GPU)\",\n",
        " \"PagedPlacer\": \"reported: offload, lossless, 2-4x thr same latency\",\n",
        " \"InfiniGenPlacer\": \"reported: offload, 1.63-32.9x speedup\",\n",
        " \"LayerKVPlacer\": \"reported: offload, up to 69x TTFT improvement\",\n",
        " \"INF2Placer\": \"reported: offload, 3.46x thr, >80% KV I/O cut, lossless (CSD hw)\",\n",
        " \"KVPRPlacer\": \"reported: offload, -35.8% lat, +46.2% thr vs DeepSpeed/HF\",\n",
        " \"OneirosPlacer\": \"reported: offload, -44.8-82.5% TBT, +6.6-86.7% thr vs vLLM\",\n",
        " \"CLOPlacer\": \"reported: offload, +9.3-66.6% thr, near-lossless (<=0.42)\",\n",
        " \"LinearAttnHead\": \"reported: O(1) mem, up to 4000x on long sequences\",\n",
        " \"LogLinearAttnHead\": \"reported: O(log T) mem, 3x over naive\",\n",
        " \"LocalLinearAttnHead\": \"reported: softmax-like mem, faster than softmax, wins on regression tasks\",\n",
        " \"KimiLinearHead\": \"reported: 75% KV cut, 6x thr at 1M ctx, 3:1 KDA/full hybrid\",\n",
        " \"flexgen\": \"reported: 10x mem, 40-100x thr vs DeepSpeed/HF\",\n",
        " \"qhitter\": \"reported: 20x mem, 33x vs HF Accelerate, full quality\",\n",
        " \"shadowkv\": \"reported: 6x GPU mem, 3.04x thr, accurate until sparse <1.56%\",\n",
        " \"tailorkv\": \"reported: 73.8% GPU mem cut, 8-18x vs standard offloading\"}\n",
        "_OPS27 = {\"vanillaatten\": {\"train\": \"O(T^2)\", \"step\": \"O(T)\", \"state\": \"O(T)\"},\n",
        " \"linearatten\": {\"train\": \"O(T)\", \"step\": \"O(1)\", \"state\": \"O(1)\"},\n",
        " \"loglinearatten\": {\"train\": \"O(T log T)\", \"step\": \"O(log T)\", \"state\": \"O(log T)\"},\n",
        " \"locallinearatten\": {\"train\": \"O(T^2)\", \"step\": \"~O(T)\", \"state\": \"O(T)\"},\n",
        " \"kimilinear\": {\"train\": \"mainly O(T)\", \"step\": \"O(1)\", \"state\": \"O(1)\"}}\n",
        "def run_kvcache_benchmark(make_model, ids, seed=14, budget=32, evictors=None, compressors=None,\n",
        "                          placers=None, attn_heads=None, run_combos=True,\n",
        "                          out_path=\"outputs/kvcache_results.json\"):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Run every compiled-path KV-cache policy on one prefilled model.\n",
        "\n",
        "    make_model: zero-arg factory returning the compiled-path NanoGPT (the\n",
        "    factory seeds construction; the runner seeds its own draws).\n",
        "    Registries default to auto-collection from globals (partial paths list\n",
        "    skips, never crash). Writes outputs/kvcache_results.json.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    t0 = _time27.time()\n",
        "    G = globals()\n",
        "    evictors = evictors if evictors is not None else {n: G[n] for n in _EVICT27 if n in G}\n",
        "    compressors = compressors if compressors is not None else {n: G[n] for n in _COMP27 if n in G}\n",
        "    placers = placers if placers is not None else {n: G[n] for n in _PLACE27 if n in G}\n",
        "    attn_heads = attn_heads if attn_heads is not None else {n: G[n] for n in _ATTN27 if n in G}\n",
        "    skipped = {\"evict\": [n for n in _EVICT27 if n not in G], \"compress\": [n for n in _COMP27 if n not in G],\n",
        "               \"place\": [n for n in _PLACE27 if n not in G], \"attn\": [n for n in _ATTN27 if n not in G]}\n",
        "    skipped[\"compress\"] = [n for n in _COMP27 if n not in G]\n",
        "    model = make_model()\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    n_params = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
        "    H = KVCacheHarness(model, budget=budget).prefill(ids)\n",
        "    acc = {k: c[\"S\"].sum(0) for k, c in H.cache.items()}\n",
        "    res = {\"paper\": \"arXiv:2603.20397\", \"seed\": seed, \"T\": H.T, \"budget\": budget,\n",
        "           \"purpose\": \"small-scale mechanism metrics per policy (Eq.1-2 bytes, retained mass, \"\n",
        "           \"output error, recon, policy stats); Table-6 magnitudes recorded as paper-reported \"\n",
        "           \"claims only\", \"skipped_not_in_path\": skipped}\n",
        "    erows = {}\n",
        "    for i, (name, cls) in enumerate(evictors.items()):\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            ev = cls()\n",
        "            kept = {}\n",
        "            alloc = {}\n",
        "            if getattr(ev, \"scope\", \"head\") == \"layer\":\n",
        "                for li in range(H.n_layers):\n",
        "                    keys = sorted(k for k in H.cache if k[0] == li)\n",
        "                    al = [acc[k] for k in keys]\n",
        "                    kl = ev.select_layer(al, budget * len(keys), seed=seed + i)\n",
        "                    for k, kk in zip(keys, kl):\n",
        "                        kept[k] = kk\n",
        "                    alloc[li] = [int(x.numel()) for x in kl]\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
        "                    S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "                    W = min(8, H.T)\n",
        "                    kept[k] = ev.select(acc[k], min(budget, H.T), win=S[-W:], prox=S[-4:],\n",
        "                                        K=c[\"K\"], V=c[\"V\"], qlast=c[\"qlast\"], Smat=S,\n",
        "                                        recent_w=6, seed=seed + i)\n",
        "            m8 = H.retained_mass(kept, rows_last=8)\n",
        "            mall = H.retained_mass(kept, rows_last=H.T)\n",
        "            err = H.attn_output_error(kept)\n",
        "            by = H.eq12_bytes({k: int(v.numel()) for k, v in kept.items()})\n",
        "            erows[name] = {\"paper_claim\": _CLAIM27.get(name, \"\"),\n",
        "                           \"mass_last8\": float(sum(m8.values()) / max(1, len(m8))),\n",
        "                           \"mass_allrows\": float(sum(mall.values()) / max(1, len(mall))),\n",
        "                           \"out_err_mean\": float(sum(err.values()) / max(1, len(err))),\n",
        "                           \"out_err_max\": float(max(err.values())),\n",
        "                           \"bytes_ratio\": by[\"ratio\"], \"per_token_bytes\": by[\"per_token\"],\n",
        "                           \"allocation\": alloc}\n",
        "        except Exception as e:\n",
        "            erows[name] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
        "    res[\"evict\"] = erows\n",
        "    crows = {}\n",
        "    for name, cls in compressors.items():\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            cc = cls()\n",
        "            rks, rvs, nbytes, oerr = [], [], 0, []\n",
        "            if getattr(cc, \"scope\", \"token\") == \"layerpair\":\n",
        "                L = H.n_layers\n",
        "                for li in range(0, L - 1, 2):\n",
        "                    for hi in range(len(H.layers[0])):\n",
        "                        c1, c2 = H.cache[(li, hi)], H.cache[(li + 1, hi)]\n",
        "                        (K1h, V1h), (K2h, V2h), meta = cc.compress_pair((c1[\"K\"], c1[\"V\"]), (c2[\"K\"], c2[\"V\"]))\n",
        "                        rks.append(meta[\"recon_k\"])\n",
        "                        rvs.append(meta[\"recon_v\"])\n",
        "                        nbytes += meta[\"bytes\"]\n",
        "                        for c, Kh, Vh in ((c1, K1h, V1h), (c2, K2h, V2h)):\n",
        "                            lk = (_attn27(c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0), Kh) / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5))\n",
        "                            o2 = (_t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1) @ Vh).squeeze(0)\n",
        "                            o1 = (c[\"S\"][-1] @ c[\"V\"])\n",
        "                            oerr.append(float((o1 - o2).norm() / (o1.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "                crows[name] = {\"paper_claim\": _CLAIM27.get(name, \"\"), \"bytes\": nbytes,\n",
        "                               \"recon_k\": float(sum(rks) / max(1, len(rks))),\n",
        "                               \"recon_v\": float(sum(rvs) / max(1, len(rvs))),\n",
        "                               \"out_err_mean\": float(sum(oerr) / max(1, len(oerr)))}\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
        "                    Kh, Vh, meta = cc.compress(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"])\n",
        "                    rks.append(meta[\"recon_k\"])\n",
        "                    rvs.append(meta[\"recon_v\"])\n",
        "                    nbytes += meta[\"bytes\"]\n",
        "                    lk = (_attn27(c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0), Kh) / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5))\n",
        "                    o2 = (_t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1) @ Vh).squeeze(0)\n",
        "                    o1 = (c[\"S\"][-1] @ c[\"V\"])\n",
        "                    oerr.append(float((o1 - o2).norm() / (o1.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "                full = H.eq12_bytes()[\"full\"]\n",
        "                crows[name] = {\"paper_claim\": _CLAIM27.get(name, \"\"), \"bytes\": nbytes,\n",
        "                               \"bytes_ratio\": nbytes / max(1, full),\n",
        "                               \"recon_k\": float(sum(rks) / max(1, len(rks))),\n",
        "                               \"recon_v\": float(sum(rvs) / max(1, len(rvs))),\n",
        "                               \"out_err_mean\": float(sum(oerr) / max(1, len(oerr)))}\n",
        "        except Exception as e:\n",
        "            crows[name] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
        "    res[\"compress\"] = crows\n",
        "    spec = {\"T\": H.T, \"L\": H.n_layers, \"H\": len(H.layers[0]),\n",
        "            \"hs\": H.cache[(0, 0)][\"head_dim\"], \"bpe\": 4, \"param_bytes\": n_params * 4}\n",
        "    prows = {}\n",
        "    for name, cls in placers.items():\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            prows[name] = dict({\"paper_claim\": _CLAIM27.get(name, \"\")},\n",
        "                               **cls().plan(spec, scores=acc))\n",
        "        except Exception as e:\n",
        "            prows[name] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
        "    res[\"place\"] = prows\n",
        "    arows = {}\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        emb = model.token_embedding.weight.shape[1]\n",
        "        key0 = H.layers[0][0].key\n",
        "        hs = int(key0.weight.shape[0])\n",
        "        xb = (model.token_embedding(_t27.tensor([ids], dtype=_t27.long).to(dev))\n",
        "              + model.position_embedding(_t27.arange(len(ids), device=dev)))\n",
        "        base = Head(hs, emb).to(dev).eval()\n",
        "        _t27.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "        with _t27.no_grad():\n",
        "            y0 = base(xb)\n",
        "        arows[\"vanillaatten\"] = {\"complexity\": _OPS27[\"vanillaatten\"], \"baseline\": True}\n",
        "        for name, cls in attn_heads.items():\n",
        "            try:\n",
        "                tag = {\"LinearAttnHead\": \"linearatten\", \"LogLinearAttnHead\": \"loglinearatten\",\n",
        "                       \"LocalLinearAttnHead\": \"locallinearatten\", \"KimiLinearHead\": \"kimilinear\"}[name]\n",
        "                h2 = cls(hs, emb).to(dev).eval()\n",
        "                h2.key.weight.data.copy_(base.key.weight.data)\n",
        "                h2.query.weight.data.copy_(base.query.weight.data)\n",
        "                h2.value.weight.data.copy_(base.value.weight.data)\n",
        "                with _t27.no_grad():\n",
        "                    y1 = h2(xb)\n",
        "                    t1 = _time27.perf_counter()\n",
        "                    for _ in range(3):\n",
        "                        h2(xb)\n",
        "                    t_small = (_time27.perf_counter() - t1) / 3.0\n",
        "                    xb2 = xb.repeat(1, 4, 1)[:, :128, :] if xb.shape[1] >= 32 else xb\n",
        "                    t1 = _time27.perf_counter()\n",
        "                    for _ in range(3):\n",
        "                        h2(xb2)\n",
        "                    t_big = (_time27.perf_counter() - t1) / 3.0\n",
        "                arows[name] = {\"paper_claim\": _CLAIM27.get(name, \"\"), \"complexity\": _OPS27[tag],\n",
        "                               \"rel_err_vs_softmax\": float((y0 - y1).norm() / (y0.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                               \"seconds_T\": round(t_small, 4), \"seconds_4T\": round(t_big, 4)}\n",
        "            except Exception as e:\n",
        "                arows[name] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
        "    except Exception as e:\n",
        "        arows[\"harness_error\"] = str(e)\n",
        "    res[\"attn\"] = arows\n",
        "    grows = {}\n",
        "    if run_combos:\n",
        "        H2 = KVCacheHarness(model, budget=budget).prefill(ids)\n",
        "        for cname, fn in ((\"flexgen\", kvcache_flexgen_preset), (\"qhitter\", kvcache_qhitter_preset),\n",
        "                          (\"shadowkv\", kvcache_shadowkv_preset), (\"tailorkv\", kvcache_tailorkv_preset)):\n",
        "            try:\n",
        "                grows[cname] = dict({\"paper_claim\": _CLAIM27.get(cname, \"\")}, **fn(H2))\n",
        "            except Exception as e:\n",
        "                grows[cname] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
        "    res[\"combos\"] = grows\n",
        "    res[\"seconds\"] = round(_time27.time() - t0, 1)\n",
        "    _P27(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P27(out_path).write_text(_j27.dumps(res, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "    ok = {sec: sum(1 for v in rows.values() if \"error\" not in v) for sec, rows in\n",
        "          ((\"evict\", erows), (\"compress\", crows), (\"place\", prows), (\"attn\", arows), (\"combos\", grows))}\n",
        "    print(_j27.dumps({\"ok\": ok, \"skipped\": skipped}, indent=2))\n",
        "    return res\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "BENCH_RESULTS.append(live_call(\n",
        "    'kvcache', run_kvcache_benchmark, make_model=lambda: model,\n",
        "    ids=bench_ids(globals(), 128), budget=32))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Relations: KV Cache survey (arXiv:2603.20397) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Cache policies read frozen forward states and reshape what generation keeps; every prior section either trains, probes, steers, compresses, or audits those same states, so all relations below are STACK unless the bullet says otherwise. Evict/compress/place compose across axes (evict->compress->place) and with every existing technique; attention Impls replace the Head scoring at its site only.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probes read frozen states for signal; eviction reads the same states for retention mass (probe AUROC vs cache mass - two readouts, one frozen substrate). Probe-eval sequences can run under any evictor to test whether retained mass preserves probe signal.\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** SABER exits depth during generation; the KV cache persists across those exits - exit gating and cache residency are different stages (depth vs memory), and exit-confidence could one day gate retention, which is future work, not a claim.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Grokking checkpoints are substrates: heavy-hitter rankings can be re-measured at Tmem vs Tgrok to ask whether memorization-phase attention concentrates differently - same loop, new readout.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (kept).** ConvMem windows the forward context; eviction windows the retained past - both partition positions, never merged [see backprop: eviction inside fixed windows].\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** The harness hooks key/value projections, which exist under any readout head; re-running retained-mass under geodesicflat tests policy robustness to the readout, the same way s23 re-runs circuits.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Pruning shrinks H/D/L, which Eq.1-2 consumes directly: the byte accounting re-runs on pruned checkpoints with zero code change - analytic reuse, not retraining.\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Prefix steering and selective caching compose by protecting steered prefixes (SnapKV-style sink protection extended to the whole prefix): steer first, retain the steering.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam priors and cache scores are two frozen-state readouts (belief geometry vs retention geometry); interface/Jacobian columns from s26 stay untouched.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP localizes circuits with gradients; H2O ranks tokens with accumulated attention - forward retention meets backward attribution on the same frozen forward [see backprop: H2 ranking vs input-gradient attribution].\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): STACK (kept).** s25 compiles prompts into weights (rank-1); the cache compiles history into retained entries (SLERP/SVD factors) - exactness-preserving compression in two substrates, tested by logit-match and retained-mass respectively.\n",
        "- **vs LBI (arXiv:2605.09204, s26): STACK (kept).** s26 groups layers into regions for scan-parallel backward; LayerKV tiers layers for residency - regions and tiers are the same grouping instinct applied to gradients vs memory [see backprop: region-partitioned budgets].\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** Vaswani 2017 is cited by the survey itself (foundation, not a runtime surface); Eq.3-5 are its scaled dot-product form.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** Evict x Compress x Place compose freely (pipeline order evict->compress->place); any evictor/compressor/placer with any backbone, any vocab/scale/context, dense or bounded wiring (hooks read whatever the compiled Heads compute); attention Impls compose with every non-Attn axis (subclasses reuse the compiled projections).\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** one evictor per run; one compressor per run; one placer per run; one Attn kernel per run (the four new values join vanillaatten/mqa/gqa/mla/dsa/tokenformer/tpa at the same Head site); encoder-decoder Arch crossed with the new Attn Impls has no Impl provided and is out of scope here.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** eviction discards presented as lossless (every evictor reports retained mass AND output error; lossless claims belong to placers only, per Table 4); Table-6 magnitudes cited as small-scale evidence (the small-scale run reports mechanism metrics; paper numbers are labeled claims); wall-clock speedups derived from placer stand-in constants (policy simulation, declared); compression quality at small scale presented as paper-scale accuracy (recon/output-error only).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: eviction inside fixed windows (s15 ConvMem x s27 cache)\n",
        "\"\"\"Windowed vs global eviction on identical frozen scores.\n",
        "\n",
        "s15 partitions positions into convolution windows; here positions are\n",
        "partitioned into fixed windows (size 8, stride 4) and a top-K rule runs\n",
        "inside each window, then the union is ranked by accumulated attention and\n",
        "cut to budget. Compared against global H2O-style top-K at the same budget\n",
        "on the last-query mass. Takes a prefilled harness; returns per-head means.\"\"\"\n",
        "def kvcache_backprop_windowed(harness, budget=32, window=8, stride=4):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    T = harness.T\n",
        "    wins = [list(range(s, min(s + window, T))) for s in range(0, T, stride)]\n",
        "    per = max(1, budget // max(1, len(wins)))\n",
        "    mg, mw = [], []\n",
        "    for key, c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "        acc = S.sum(0)\n",
        "        glob = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(acc, min(budget, T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "        mg.append(float(S[-1, _t27.tensor(sorted(glob))].sum()))\n",
        "        union = set()\n",
        "        for w in wins:\n",
        "            sub = acc[w]\n",
        "            for i in _t27.topk(sub, min(per, len(w))).indices.tolist():\n",
        "                union.add(w[i])\n",
        "        ranked = sorted(union, key=lambda i: (-float(acc[i]), i))[:budget]\n",
        "        mw.append(float(S[-1, _t27.tensor(sorted(ranked))].sum()))\n",
        "    g = sum(mg) / max(1, len(mg))\n",
        "    w = sum(mw) / max(1, len(mw))\n",
        "    return {\"n_windows\": len(wins), \"mass_global\": g, \"mass_windowed\": w, \"delta\": w - g}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: H2 ranking vs input-gradient attribution (s23 SharedCircuits x s27 cache)\n",
        "\"\"\"Forward retention meets backward attribution on one frozen forward.\n",
        "\n",
        "s23's AP consumes gradients; H2O consumes accumulated attention. One backward\n",
        "on last-token cross-entropy yields per-token input-embedding gradient norms\n",
        "(attribution); top-K attribution vs top-K accumulated attention are compared\n",
        "by Jaccard against a chance baseline. Takes the model, ids, and one (T,)\n",
        "accumulated-score vector; returns the overlap verdict.\"\"\"\n",
        "def kvcache_backprop_attr_overlap(model, ids, acc_vec, K=16):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    xb = _t27.tensor([ids], dtype=_t27.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    grads = {}\n",
        "    def _bh(m, gin, gout):\n",
        "        grads[\"g\"] = gout[0].detach()\n",
        "    h = model.token_embedding.register_full_backward_hook(_bh)\n",
        "    logits = model(xb)\n",
        "    loss = _t27.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits[:, -1, :], xb[:, -1])\n",
        "    model.zero_grad()\n",
        "    loss.backward()\n",
        "    h.remove()\n",
        "    attr = grads[\"g\"].squeeze(0).norm(dim=-1)\n",
        "    T = attr.numel()\n",
        "    a = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(attr, min(K, T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "    b = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(acc_vec, min(K, T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "    j = len(a & b) / max(1, len(a | b))\n",
        "    chance = min(K, T) / max(1, 2 * T - min(K, T))\n",
        "    return {\"K\": K, \"jaccard\": j, \"chance\": chance, \"above_chance\": bool(j > chance)}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: region-partitioned budgets (s26 LBI regions x LayerKV tiers)\n",
        "\"\"\"Global vs per-region eviction budgets on identical frozen scores.\n",
        "\n",
        "s26 groups layers into regions for scan-parallel backward; LayerKV tiers\n",
        "layers for residency. Here layers are grouped into regions of region_size\n",
        "(the s26 grouping instinct) and each region receives a proportional budget\n",
        "share; per-head retained last-row mass is compared against global top-K at\n",
        "the same total budget. Takes a prefilled harness; returns per-head means.\"\"\"\n",
        "def kvcache_backprop_regions(harness, budget=32, region_size=2):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    L = harness.n_layers\n",
        "    T = harness.T\n",
        "    regs = [list(range(s, min(s + region_size, L))) for s in range(0, L, region_size)]\n",
        "    share = [max(1, int(round(budget * len(r) / L))) for r in regs]\n",
        "    mg, mr = [], []\n",
        "    for (li, hi), c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "        acc = S.sum(0)\n",
        "        glob = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(acc, min(budget, T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "        mg.append(float(S[-1, _t27.tensor(sorted(glob))].sum()))\n",
        "        ri = next(i for i, r in enumerate(regs) if li in r)\n",
        "        reg = set(int(i) for i in _t27.topk(acc, min(share[ri], T)).indices.tolist())\n",
        "        mr.append(float(S[-1, _t27.tensor(sorted(reg))].sum()))\n",
        "    g = sum(mg) / max(1, len(mg))\n",
        "    r = sum(mr) / max(1, len(mr))\n",
        "    return {\"regions\": [len(r) for r in regs], \"shares\": share,\n",
        "            \"mass_global\": g, \"mass_region\": r, \"delta\": r - g}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 28. SpindleKV - arXiv:2507.06517 (Tang, Shi, Li, Qi, Liu, Zhang, Wang 2025, ACL 2025 pp.28428-28442)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** KV-cache reduction split by depth: deep layers get attention-weight eviction with a pyramid allocation (accumulated scores Eq.2 with observation window, GQA-averaged Eq.3, linear retain schedule Eq.5-7 with floor beta=0.05); shallow layers get JIT codebook replacement (cosine graph Eq.4/9, greedy max-degree entries Eq.10-13, magnitudes Eq.8, reconstruction Eq.14, Alg.1); the GQA dilemma is solved by unfolding (repeat KV h_n times) and letting the codebook absorb the cos=1 duplicates; per-layer reserve r^l = r1*r2*r3 (Eq.15). Validated on LongBench (Table 1/10/11), Needle-in-a-Haystack (Table 4: 0.979/0.975 at 15%), ablations (Tables 2/5/6), reserve curves (Fig.1/5), distributions (Fig.3/7/8). Official code audited (0 issues/PRs); divergences recorded (per-layer default thresholds, DCT/prepool extras, online greedy, h_n/h_g statement).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** official repo EXISTS (tyxqc/SpindleKV, MIT, 1 star, 0 forks, 0 issues, 0 PRs, 6 commits; see graded 15_RepoAudit). Our integration reimplements the paper text (not their code): batch greedy max-degree codebook instead of the online match-or-append pool, Table-3 single thresholds instead of per-layer schedules, main-text algorithm only (no DCT/prepool/compensation).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): one Evict value + one Compress value + one plain preset.** The pyramid allocator is mutually exclusive with the other evictors at the same per-head selection site (it sets its own keep-count from Eq.5-7), so it compiles as @Technique::KVCacheEvict::spindlepyr with a layer-bound instance per layer. The greedy codebook is mutually exclusive with the other compressors at the same K/V transform site, so it compiles as @Technique::KVCacheCompress::spindlecodebook. The layer-regime split (shallow codebook-only, deep evict-then-codebook, Eq.15 composition) is a combination over the two axes plus GQA unfolding, so it is plain always-present composition code (spindle_preset), like the \u00a727 combos. The shared \u00a727 harness (prefill capture, Eq.1-2 accounting, mass/error metrics) is reused untouched; GQA-path handling is self-contained in the preset (own hooks on keys/values lists) because the harness is head-layout based.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Technique -> Impl -> original paper -> repo map\n",
        "\n",
        "| SpindleKV part | Paper ref | Impl value | Official repo |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Pyramid eviction (Eq.2/5-7) | arXiv:2507.06517 \u00a73.3 | KVCacheEvict::spindlepyr | tyxqc/SpindleKV |\n",
        "| Codebook replacement (Eq.8-14, Alg.1) | arXiv:2507.06517 \u00a73.4 | KVCacheCompress::spindlecodebook | tyxqc/SpindleKV |\n",
        "| Layer-regime composition (Eq.15) + GQA unfold | arXiv:2507.06517 \u00a73-4 | plain spindle_preset (no axis) | tyxqc/SpindleKV |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) batch greedy max-degree codebook (paper Alg.1) instead of the repo's online pool; (2) Table-3 single thresholds, not per-layer schedules; (3) GQA-averaged scores (Eq.3) computed live on the gqa path; unfolding repeats KV h_n times before the codebook; (4) harness has no RoPE: codebook runs on captured projections directly (same note as \u00a727); (5) Eq.5 upper branch (alpha,1] recorded verbatim with its negative-retain anomaly flagged in graded; experiments use r<=0.45; (6) Eq.2 denominator (l-a) and Eq.3 (n-a) kept verbatim with notation notes.\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::KVCacheEvict::spindlepyr{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"SpindleKV pyramid eviction (Tang et al., arXiv:2507.06517 \u00a73.3; Eq.2/5-7).\n",
        "\n",
        "Attention-weight eviction with a linear pyramid schedule: accumulated\n",
        "scores over the observation window (Eq.2; window tokens always reserved),\n",
        "per-layer retain rc(lam) interpolated between rc(0) and rc(m-1) (Eq.5-6,\n",
        "floor beta=0.05). Layer-bound instances (li, m, r); GQA averaging (Eq.3)\n",
        "is applied by the caller on the gqa path (scores arrive pre-averaged).\"\"\"\n",
        "class SpindlePyramidEvictor:\n",
        "    scope = \"head\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, li=0, m=1, r=0.4, window=8, beta=0.05, l=4000):\n",
        "        self.li, self.m, self.r, self.window, self.beta = li, m, r, window, beta\n",
        "        alpha = 0.5 * (1.0 + beta)\n",
        "        lw = min(window, l)\n",
        "        lc = max(1, l - lw)\n",
        "        rc = (r * l - lw) / lc\n",
        "        if beta < rc <= alpha:\n",
        "            rc0, rcm = 2 * rc - beta, beta\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            rc0, rcm = 1.0, 1.0 - 2 * rc\n",
        "        self.rc, self.rc0, self.rcm = rc, rc0, rcm\n",
        "        self.keep_frac = rc0 + (rcm - rc0) * self.li / max(1, m - 1)\n",
        "    def select(self, scores, budget, win=None, **kw):\n",
        "        T = int(scores.numel())\n",
        "        W = min(self.window, T)\n",
        "        base = win.sum(0) if win is not None else scores\n",
        "        lc = max(1, T - W)\n",
        "        k = min(lc, max(0, int(round(self.keep_frac * lc))))\n",
        "        if k >= lc:\n",
        "            return _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        top = _t27.topk(base[:lc], k).indices if k > 0 else base[:0]\n",
        "        keep = _t27.cat([top, _t27.arange(lc, T)])\n",
        "        return _t27.sort(keep).values\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::spindlecodebook{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"SpindleKV codebook replacement (Tang et al., arXiv:2507.06517 \u00a73.4; Eq.8-14, Alg.1).\n",
        "\n",
        "Batch greedy max-degree codebook (paper Alg.1): normalize by magnitudes\n",
        "(Eq.8), cosine graph at theta (Eq.9), max-degree entry + neighbor absorb\n",
        "(Eq.10-13), reconstruction C[r]*m (Eq.14). Stored bytes: entries + int32\n",
        "refs + fp32 magnitudes. Table-3 thresholds default (0.98 keys, 0.95 values).\"\"\"\n",
        "class SpindleCodebookCompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, theta_k=0.98, theta_v=0.95):\n",
        "        self.theta_k, self.theta_v = theta_k, theta_v\n",
        "    def _codebook(self, X, theta):\n",
        "        T, d = X.shape\n",
        "        m = X.norm(dim=-1).clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "        Xn = X / m.unsqueeze(-1)\n",
        "        G = (Xn @ Xn.T > theta).long()\n",
        "        alive = _t27.ones(T, dtype=_t27.bool)\n",
        "        entries, refs = [], _t27.full((T,), -1, dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "        while bool(alive.any()):\n",
        "            deg = (G * alive.unsqueeze(0) * alive.unsqueeze(1)).sum(1)\n",
        "            deg = deg.masked_fill(~alive, -1)\n",
        "            iota = int(deg.argmax())\n",
        "            entries.append(Xn[iota])\n",
        "            nbrs = (G[iota] == 1) & alive\n",
        "            refs[nbrs] = len(entries) - 1\n",
        "            alive[nbrs] = False\n",
        "        C = _t27.stack(entries)\n",
        "        return C, refs, m\n",
        "    def compress(self, K, V, **kw):\n",
        "        Ck, rk, mk = self._codebook(K, self.theta_k)\n",
        "        Cv, rv, mv = self._codebook(V, self.theta_v)\n",
        "        Kh = Ck[rk] * mk.unsqueeze(-1)\n",
        "        Vh = Cv[rv] * mv.unsqueeze(-1)\n",
        "        d = K.shape[-1]\n",
        "        T = K.shape[0]\n",
        "        nb = int((Ck.numel() + Cv.numel() + 2 * T + 2 * T) * 4)\n",
        "        return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": nb, \"entries_k\": int(Ck.shape[0]),\n",
        "                        \"entries_v\": int(Cv.shape[0]),\n",
        "                        \"recon_k\": float((K - Kh).norm() / (K.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                        \"recon_v\": float((V - Vh).norm() / (V.norm() + 1e-12))}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT \u00a728 SpindleKV composition (paper \u00a73-4) | Plain preset over the KVCache axes: shallow layers codebook-only, deep layers pyramid-evict then codebook survivors (Eq.15 r=r1*r2*r3 per layer); GQA handled by unfolding (repeat h_n) absorbed by the codebook | NOT a new axis (combination precedent) | GQA check is self-contained (own hooks on keys/values lists) because the harness is head-layout based.\n",
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "def spindle_preset(harness, r=0.4, split_frac=0.5, theta_k=0.98, theta_v=0.95, window=8, seed=0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Layer-regime SpindleKV composition on a prefilled harness.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Layers below split_frac*L: codebook-only (Table-5 mode). Layers at/above:\n",
        "    pyramid eviction (keep-count from Eq.5-7) then codebook on survivors.\n",
        "    Returns per-layer r1/r2/r3, mean r (Eq.15), mass, output error, bytes.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    L = harness.n_layers\n",
        "    split = int(round(split_frac * L))\n",
        "    cb = SpindleCodebookCompressor(theta_k, theta_v)\n",
        "    rows, mass, err, nbytes = {}, [], [], 0\n",
        "    for li in range(L):\n",
        "        keys = sorted(k for k in harness.cache if k[0] == li)\n",
        "        ev = SpindlePyramidEvictor(li=li, m=L, r=r, window=window)\n",
        "        for k in keys:\n",
        "            c = harness.cache[k]\n",
        "            S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "            T = c[\"K\"].shape[0]\n",
        "            W = min(window, T)\n",
        "            if li < split:\n",
        "                kept = _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "                r1 = 1.0\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                kept = ev.select(S.sum(0), T, win=S[-W:])\n",
        "                r1 = kept.numel() / max(1, T)\n",
        "            Kh, Vh, meta = cb.compress(c[\"K\"][kept], c[\"V\"][kept])\n",
        "            d = c[\"head_dim\"]\n",
        "            full = 2 * T * d * 4\n",
        "            kept_full = int(kept.numel() * 2 * d * 4)\n",
        "            r2 = meta[\"bytes\"] / max(1, kept_full if li >= split else full)\n",
        "            stored = meta[\"bytes\"]\n",
        "            r3 = (d + 32 / 33) / d\n",
        "            rows[k] = {\"r1\": float(r1), \"r2\": float(r2), \"r3\": float(r3),\n",
        "                       \"r\": float(r1 * r2 * r3), \"entries\": meta[\"entries_k\"] + meta[\"entries_v\"]}\n",
        "            nbytes += int(stored)\n",
        "            lk = (c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0) @ Kh.T / (d ** 0.5))\n",
        "            o2 = (_t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1) @ Vh).squeeze(0)\n",
        "            o1 = S[-1] @ c[\"V\"]\n",
        "            err.append(float((o1 - o2).norm() / (o1.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "            mass.append(float(S[-1, kept].sum()))\n",
        "    mean_r = sum(v[\"r\"] for v in rows.values()) / max(1, len(rows))\n",
        "    return {\"recipe\": {\"shallow\": \"codebook-only\", \"deep\": \"pyramid-evict + codebook\",\n",
        "                       \"split_layer\": split, \"r_target\": r},\n",
        "            \"per_head\": rows, \"mean_r\": mean_r, \"bytes\": nbytes,\n",
        "            \"mass\": float(sum(mass) / max(1, len(mass))),\n",
        "            \"out_err\": float(sum(err) / max(1, len(err)))}\n",
        "def spindle_gqa_check(model, ids, seed=0):\n",
        "    \"\"\"GQA-dilemma check, self-contained (paper \u00a73.3 + Table 2).\n",
        "\n",
        "    Hooks the gqa path keys/values/queries lists; per-KV-head scores averaged\n",
        "    over the query group (Eq.3); unfolds KV h_n times (repeat) and verifies\n",
        "    the codebook absorbs the cos=1 duplicates (entry count unchanged).\n",
        "    Returns skipped-note on non-gqa models.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    attn = model.blocks[0].self_attn\n",
        "    if not (hasattr(attn, \"keys\") and hasattr(attn, \"values\")):\n",
        "        return {\"skipped\": \"not a gqa-path model (needs keys/values lists)\"}\n",
        "    caps = {}\n",
        "    hooks = []\n",
        "    def _hk(name):\n",
        "        def fn(m, inp, out):\n",
        "            caps.setdefault(name, []).append(out.detach())\n",
        "        return fn\n",
        "    for lst, nm in ((attn.queries, \"q\"), (attn.keys, \"k\"), (attn.values, \"v\")):\n",
        "        for mod in lst:\n",
        "            hooks.append(mod.register_forward_hook(_hk(nm)))\n",
        "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
        "    xb = _t27.tensor([ids], dtype=_t27.long).to(dev)\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    with _t27.no_grad():\n",
        "        model(xb)\n",
        "    for h in hooks:\n",
        "        h.remove()\n",
        "    K = caps[\"k\"][0].squeeze(0)\n",
        "    V = caps[\"v\"][0].squeeze(0)\n",
        "    Q = _t27.stack([o.squeeze(0) for o in caps[\"q\"]])\n",
        "    nq, nkv = Q.shape[0], K.shape[0] if K.dim() == 3 else 1\n",
        "    if K.dim() == 3:\n",
        "        K0, V0 = K[0], V[0]\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        K0, V0 = K, V\n",
        "    hn = max(1, nq // max(1, len(attn.keys)))\n",
        "    cb = SpindleCodebookCompressor()\n",
        "    Ck0, _, _ = cb._codebook(K0, 0.98)\n",
        "    Ku = K0.repeat_interleave(max(1, hn), dim=0) if K0.dim() == 2 else K0\n",
        "    Cku, _, _ = cb._codebook(Ku, 0.98)\n",
        "    return {\"n_query_heads\": nq, \"n_kv_lists\": len(attn.keys), \"hn\": hn,\n",
        "            \"entries_plain\": int(Ck0.shape[0]), \"entries_unfolded\": int(Cku.shape[0]),\n",
        "            \"absorbed_ok\": bool(Cku.shape[0] == Ck0.shape[0])}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: SpindleKV end-to-end | Prefills one harness, runs full / pyramid-only / codebook-only / spindle measurement sets + Eq.15 row + optional gqa-model check (passed in, never constructed here) | emits outputs/spindle_results.json | plain orchestrator, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "import torch as _t27\n",
        "import json as _j28\n",
        "import time as _time28\n",
        "from pathlib import Path as _P28\n",
        "def run_spindle_benchmark(make_model, ids, r=0.4, split_frac=0.5, seed=15, gqa_model=None,\n",
        "                          out_path=\"outputs/spindle_results.json\"):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Run the SpindleKV measurement sets on one prefilled model.\n",
        "\n",
        "    make_model: zero-arg factory for the compiled-path NanoGPT (factory seeds\n",
        "    construction; runner seeds its own draws). gqa_model: optional prebuilt\n",
        "    gqa-path model for the unfold check. Writes outputs/spindle_results.json.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    t0 = _time28.time()\n",
        "    model = make_model()\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    H = KVCacheHarness(model, budget=None).prefill(ids)\n",
        "    L = H.n_layers\n",
        "    measurements = {}\n",
        "    full = H.eq12_bytes()[\"full\"]\n",
        "    m0 = H.retained_mass({k: _t27.arange(H.T) for k in H.cache})\n",
        "    measurements[\"full\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"baseline (FullKV 100%)\",\n",
        "                    \"mass\": float(sum(m0.values()) / max(1, len(m0))), \"bytes\": full, \"ratio\": 1.0}\n",
        "    mp, ep, bp = [], [], 0\n",
        "    for li in range(L):\n",
        "        ev = SpindlePyramidEvictor(li=li, m=L, r=r)\n",
        "        for k in sorted(x for x in H.cache if x[0] == li):\n",
        "            c = H.cache[k]\n",
        "            S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "            T = c[\"K\"].shape[0]\n",
        "            kept = ev.select(S.sum(0), T, win=S[-8:])\n",
        "            bp += int(kept.numel() * 2 * c[\"head_dim\"] * 4)\n",
        "    mall = H.retained_mass({k: SpindlePyramidEvictor(li=k[0], m=L, r=r).select(\n",
        "        H.cache[k][\"S\"].sum(0), H.T, win=H.cache[k][\"S\"][-8:]) for k in H.cache})\n",
        "    merr = H.attn_output_error({k: SpindlePyramidEvictor(li=k[0], m=L, r=r).select(\n",
        "        H.cache[k][\"S\"].sum(0), H.T, win=H.cache[k][\"S\"][-8:]) for k in H.cache})\n",
        "    measurements[\"pyramid_only\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: PyramidKV baseline (Table 1, beaten by SpindleKV)\",\n",
        "                            \"mass\": float(sum(mall.values()) / max(1, len(mall))),\n",
        "                            \"out_err\": float(sum(merr.values()) / max(1, len(merr))),\n",
        "                            \"bytes\": bp, \"ratio\": bp / max(1, full)}\n",
        "    cb = SpindleCodebookCompressor()\n",
        "    mc, ec, bc = [], [], 0\n",
        "    for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
        "        Kh, Vh, meta = cb.compress(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"])\n",
        "        bc += meta[\"bytes\"]\n",
        "        lk = (c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0) @ Kh.T / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5))\n",
        "        o2 = (_t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1) @ Vh).squeeze(0)\n",
        "        o1 = c[\"S\"][-1] @ c[\"V\"]\n",
        "        ec.append(float((o1 - o2).norm() / (o1.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
        "    measurements[\"codebook_only\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: Table 5 (47.8% ratio keeps 36.01 vs 35.78)\",\n",
        "                             \"mass\": 1.0,  # replacement keeps every token represented\n",
        "                             \"bytes\": bc, \"ratio\": bc / max(1, full),\n",
        "                             \"out_err\": float(sum(ec) / max(1, len(ec)))}\n",
        "    sp = spindle_preset(H, r=r, split_frac=split_frac, seed=seed)\n",
        "    measurements[\"spindle\"] = dict({\"paper_claim\": \"reported: best AVG per band (Table 1); 0.979/0.975 needle (Table 4)\"},\n",
        "                            **{k: v for k, v in sp.items() if k != \"per_head\"})\n",
        "    measurements[\"spindle\"][\"per_layer_r\"] = {str(k): v[\"r\"] for k, v in sp[\"per_head\"].items()}\n",
        "    gqa = spindle_gqa_check(gqa_model, ids, seed=seed) if gqa_model is not None else {\"skipped\": \"no gqa model passed\"}\n",
        "    res = {\"paper\": \"arXiv:2507.06517\", \"seed\": seed, \"T\": H.T, \"r\": r,\n",
        "           \"purpose\": \"small-scale mechanism measurement sets (mass/error/bytes/Eq.15 rows); paper magnitudes are reported claims only\",\n",
        "           \"measurements\": measurements, \"gqa\": gqa, \"seconds\": round(_time28.time() - t0, 1)}\n",
        "    _P28(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P28(out_path).write_text(_j28.dumps(res, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "    ok = {n: (\"error\" not in v) for n, v in measurements.items()}\n",
        "    print(_j28.dumps({\"measurements_ok\": ok, \"gqa\": gqa.get(\"absorbed_ok\", gqa.get(\"skipped\"))}, indent=2))\n",
        "    return res\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "BENCH_RESULTS.append(live_call(\n",
        "    'spindlekv', run_spindle_benchmark, make_model=lambda: model,\n",
        "    ids=bench_ids(globals(), 128), r=0.4))"
      ]
    },
