        "### Relations: SpindleKV (arXiv:2507.06517) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Shallow/deep split caching meets every prior section at the frozen forward: eviction reads accumulated attention (forward importance), codebooks read cosine structure (constituent redundancy). All relations STACK unless stated; spindlepyr/spindlecodebook extend the \u00a727 Evict/Compress axes; the preset composes them per layer.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probe signal can be re-measured on spindle-compressed caches; codebook-shared states are a new probe substrate (many tokens, few unique directions).\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Exit gating and spindle residency are different stages; needle-critical tokens argue for protection flags under early exits.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Codebook sizes re-measured at Tmem vs Tgrok track similarity drift during training - same loop, new readout.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** ConvMem windows, spindle observation windows, and pyramid allocation all partition positions/scores; never merged.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** Hooks read projections under any readout; compression re-runs under geodesicflat unchanged.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Pruned H/D/L feed Eq.1-2 and the codebook directly (fewer, denser vectors).\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Pyramid allocation protects the observation window (a suffix); steered prefixes get the same protection treatment - protection semantics compose.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam priors and retention/codebook structure are two frozen-state readouts.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP gradients vs accumulated-attention eviction scores; codebook entries as attribution units (which entry stands for which tokens).\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): STACK (kept).** Rank-1 weight compile (s25) vs codebook history compile (s28) vs SLERP merge (s27) - three low-rank compressions in three substrates.\n",
        "- **vs LBI (arXiv:2605.09204, s26): STACK (kept).** Regions (gradient groups) vs spindle layer regimes (retention groups) - same grouping instinct, plus region-partitioned spindle as a direct composition.\n",
        "- **vs KVCache survey (arXiv:2603.20397, s27): STACK (kept, closest kin).** SpindleKV instantiates the survey's families: pyramid eviction beside H2O/SnapKV/AdaKV (same accumulated-score site, new schedule), codebook beside MiniCache (merge) and KVzip (reconstruction) with magnitudes beside KIVI/KVQuant (exactness side), GQA-unfold beside the survey's GQA notes. Table-6-style claims stay labeled reported.\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** Eq.1 attention form is Vaswani 2017 (foundation, not a runtime surface).\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** spindlepyr with any backbone/vocab/scale/context/interface wiring (hooks read whatever the compiled Heads compute); spindlecodebook after any evictor (operates on survivors); preset composes both per layer; gqa check beside (not inside) the harness.\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** one evictor per run (spindlepyr joins the \u00a727 Evict axis); one compressor per run (spindlecodebook joins the \u00a727 Compress axis); encoder-decoder Arch crossed with the new Impls has no Impl provided and is out of scope here.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** codebook recon presented as lossless (recon error always reported; magnitudes are the exactness mechanism); LongBench/needle magnitudes cited as small-scale evidence (the small-scale run reports mass/error/bytes; paper numbers are labeled claims); Eq.5 upper-branch schedule used as-is (experiments stay in the lower branch; the anomaly is flagged, not patched).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: codebook without eviction (Table-5 analog, s28 x s27 axes)\n",
        "\"\"\"Codebook-only compression per layer on a prefilled harness.\n",
        "\n",
        "Table 5 shows the codebook alone halves the cache without accuracy loss.\n",
        "Takes a prefilled harness; returns per-layer entry counts, ratios, recon\n",
        "errors for keys and values (the live Table-5 row).\"\"\"\n",
        "def spindle_backprop_codebook_only(harness, theta_k=0.98, theta_v=0.95):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    cb = SpindleCodebookCompressor(theta_k, theta_v)\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for k, c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        Kh, Vh, meta = cb.compress(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"])\n",
        "        full = 2 * c[\"K\"].numel() * 4\n",
        "        rows.append({\"head\": list(k), \"entries_k\": meta[\"entries_k\"],\n",
        "                     \"entries_v\": meta[\"entries_v\"], \"ratio\": meta[\"bytes\"] / max(1, full),\n",
        "                     \"recon_k\": meta[\"recon_k\"], \"recon_v\": meta[\"recon_v\"]})\n",
        "    r = sum(v[\"ratio\"] for v in rows) / max(1, len(rows))\n",
        "    return {\"n_heads\": len(rows), \"mean_ratio\": r, \"rows\": rows}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: GQA-unfold absorption (GQA dilemma, s28 x Attn::gqa)\n",
        "\"\"\"Unfold-then-absorb on a gqa-path model (Table-2 mechanism).\n",
        "\n",
        "Takes a prebuilt gqa-path model plus ids; delegates to the self-contained\n",
        "spindle_gqa_check (Eq.3 averaging, repeat h_n, codebook absorption) and\n",
        "returns its verdict dict.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def spindle_backprop_gqa(model_gqa, ids, seed=0):\n",
        "    return spindle_gqa_check(model_gqa, ids, seed=seed)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 29. KeepKV - arXiv:2504.09936 (Tian, Wang, Peng, Yuan, Wang, Yi, Liu, Cui, Yang 2025, AAAI 2026)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** Merging with a losslessness guarantee: eviction perturbs output by Eq.4 (low-score priority justified); convex merging always sags (Thm.2: merged score below the pre-merge sum, nonzero perturbation); Electoral Votes (merge counts p, init 1, summed) plus ZIP-Merging (Eq.7: score-weighted value mean, log-scaled key mean) give single-step zero perturbation (Thm.3, Alg.1); EMA scores with bias correction (Eq.8) extend to multi-step with bound 2e(1+e)g/(1-e)^2 (Thm.5) and justify similarity merging (Lemma 6); merge-first in prefill beats evict-first (App Table 3); threshold T=0.8 default (App Table 4); periodic lossless scheme stores full cache externally and reloads compressed reps. Validated on HELM/LM-eval (Fig.4), LongBench (Table 2), throughput (Table 1: 255.99 tokens/s, over 2x), ablations with evictors (Fig.5). Official code audited (0 issues/PRs); built on the H2O codebase as sketch attention.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** official repo EXISTS (kkvcache/KeepKV, 3 stars, 2 forks, 0 issues, 0 PRs, 29 commits; see graded 16_RepoAudit). Our integration reimplements the paper text (not their code): batch ZIP merging with explicit votes instead of the sketch-attention fork, Table-3/4 values as parameters, main-text algorithm only.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): one Compress value + plain measurement sets.** Vote-weighted ZIP merging is mutually exclusive with the other compressors at the same K/V transform site (it replaces retained entries by merged ones plus a vote vector), so it compiles as @Technique::KVCacheCompress::keepkv. It takes its eviction/retention sets from any evictor (paper \u00a74.5 composes with H2O/PyramidInfer), so the combinations are plain runner measurement sets, not axes. The periodic scheme (external full store + resident compressed + reload schedule) is a byte/schedule policy simulation in the declared \u00a727-placer sense. The shared \u00a727 harness is reused untouched; vote-aware scoring lives in the Impl and the runner measurement set.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Technique -> Impl -> original paper -> repo map\n",
        "\n",
        "| KeepKV part | Paper ref | Impl value | Official repo |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| ZIP merging + votes (Eq.6-7, Alg.1) | arXiv:2504.09936 \u00a73.3 | KVCacheCompress::keepkv | kkvcache/KeepKV |\n",
        "| Evictor pairings (H2O/PyramidInfer sets) | arXiv:2504.09936 \u00a74.5 | plain runner measurement sets (no axis) | kkvcache/KeepKV |\n",
        "| Periodic lossless scheme | arXiv:2504.09936 \u00a73.3 | plain byte/schedule plan (no axis) | kkvcache/KeepKV |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) batch ZIP merging with explicit vote vectors (paper Alg.1 loop) instead of the repo's sketch-attention fork; (2) EMA predicted scores arrive as an argument (harness scores), the alpha/window as parameters; exact-score calls reproduce Thm.3 losslessness; (3) periodic external-store bytes counted exactly, reload timing labeled stand-in; (4) harness has no RoPE: merging runs on captured projections directly (same note as \u00a727/28); (5) CaM comparison (App C.2) recorded in relations, not reimplemented.\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::keepkv{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"KeepKV vote-weighted ZIP merging (Tian et al., arXiv:2504.09936 \u00a73.3; Eq.6-7, Alg.1).\n",
        "\n",
        "Merges evicted pairs into most-similar retained ones (cosine, threshold T)\n",
        "with Electoral Votes (counts init 1, summed) and ZIP weights (w = p*s).\n",
        "Stored: merged entries + vote vector. Vote-aware scoring\n",
        "(p-weighted attention, Eq.6/20) is provided by merged_attention for the\n",
        "ZIP weights need unnormalized exp scores (paper s^t); normalized rows\n",
        "break the log scaling (documented).\n",
        "runner leg; plain recon is also returned. Table-4 default T=0.8.\"\"\"\n",
        "class KeepKVCompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, threshold=0.8):\n",
        "        self.threshold = threshold\n",
        "    def zip_merge(self, K, V, e, c, se, sc, pe=1.0, pc=1.0):\n",
        "        se = max(float(se), 1e-30)\n",
        "        sc = max(float(sc), 1e-30)\n",
        "        we, wc = pe * se, pc * sc\n",
        "        vr = (we * V[e] + wc * V[c]) / (we + wc)\n",
        "        num = (we * K[e] + wc * K[c]) * _m27.log((we + wc) / (pe + pc))\n",
        "        den = we * _m27.log(se) + wc * _m27.log(sc)\n",
        "        if abs(float(den)) > 1e-30:\n",
        "            kr = num / den\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            kr = (we * K[e] + wc * K[c]) / (we + wc)\n",
        "        return kr, vr, pe + pc\n",
        "    def merged_attention(self, K, V, p, qlast, head_dim):\n",
        "        s = _t27.exp(qlast.unsqueeze(0) @ K.T / (head_dim ** 0.5)).squeeze(0)\n",
        "        w = p.to(s.dtype) * s\n",
        "        o = (w.unsqueeze(-1) * V).sum(0) / w.sum().clamp_min(1e-30)\n",
        "        return o, s\n",
        "    def compress(self, K, V, keep=None, scores=None, **kw):\n",
        "        T, d = K.shape\n",
        "        if keep is None:\n",
        "            keep = _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            keep = _t27.as_tensor(sorted(int(i) for i in keep), dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "        if keep.numel() == 0:\n",
        "            keep = _t27.arange(T)\n",
        "        ev = _t27.tensor([i for i in range(T) if i not in set(keep.tolist())], dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "        if scores is None:\n",
        "            scores = _t27.ones(T) / max(1, T)\n",
        "        Kn = K / K.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "        Kp, Vp, pp = [K[i] for i in keep.tolist()], [V[i] for i in keep.tolist()], [1.0] * keep.numel()\n",
        "        grp = {j: [int(keep[j])] for j in range(keep.numel())}\n",
        "        dropped = []\n",
        "        for e in ev.tolist():\n",
        "            sims = Kn[e] @ _t27.stack([Kn[i] for i in keep.tolist()]).T\n",
        "            ci = int(sims.argmax())\n",
        "            c = int(keep[ci])\n",
        "            if float(sims.max()) < self.threshold:\n",
        "                dropped.append(e)\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "            kr, vr, pr = self.zip_merge(K, V, e, c, float(scores[e]), float(scores[c]),\n",
        "                                        pe=1.0, pc=float(pp[ci]))\n",
        "            Kp[ci], Vp[ci], pp[ci] = kr, vr, pr\n",
        "            grp[ci].append(e)\n",
        "        Kh = _t27.stack(Kp)\n",
        "        Vh = _t27.stack(Vp)\n",
        "        p = _t27.tensor(pp)\n",
        "        Khf = _t27.zeros_like(K)\n",
        "        Vhf = _t27.zeros_like(V)\n",
        "        for j, srcs in grp.items():\n",
        "            for t in srcs:\n",
        "                Khf[t], Vhf[t] = Kh[j], Vh[j]\n",
        "        nb = int((Kh.numel() + Vh.numel()) * 4 + p.numel() * 4)\n",
        "        rep = _t27.tensor(sorted(t for srcs in grp.values() for t in srcs), dtype=_t27.long)\n",
        "        return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": nb, \"votes\": p, \"n_merged\": int(ev.numel()),\n",
        "                        \"dropped\": len(dropped), \"represented\": rep,\n",
        "                        \"recon_k\": float((K - Khf).norm() / (K.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                        \"recon_v\": float((V - Vhf).norm() / (V.norm() + 1e-12))}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
