        "### Relations: KeepKV (arXiv:2504.09936) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Vote-weighted merging meets every prior section at the frozen forward: eviction selects (forward importance), merging preserves (history-weighted), votes rescale (influence restoration). All relations STACK unless stated; keepkv extends the \u00a727 Compress axis; evictor pairings and the periodic plan are plain measurement sets.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probe signal re-measured on merged caches; vote vectors as probe weights (entries with more votes count more).\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Exit gating and vote-weighted residency are different stages; merged entries persist across exits.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Vote-count drift re-measured at Tmem vs Tgrok - same loop, new readout.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** Windows, observation windows, EMA windows: three window instincts, never merged.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** Merging runs on projections under any readout; re-runs under geodesicflat unchanged.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Pruned dims feed ZIP merging directly (fewer, denser pairs).\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Steered prefixes get protection from merge candidacy - protection semantics compose.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam priors and vote structure are two frozen-state readouts.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP gradients vs eviction scores for merge candidacy; merged entries as attribution units.\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): STACK (kept).** Rank-1 weight compile vs vote-weighted history compile - two exactness-flavored compressions.\n",
        "- **vs LBI (arXiv:2605.09204, s26): STACK (kept).** Regions (gradient groups) vs merge groups (similarity groups); region-partitioned merging is the direct composition.\n",
        "- **vs KVCache survey (arXiv:2603.20397, s27): STACK (kept, closest kin).** KeepKV instantiates survey merging (CaM/D2O/KVMerger rows): convex baselines reproduced as the sag leg, similarity selection justified by Lemma 6, quantization-orthogonality kept (merging x KIVI compose).\n",
        "- **vs SpindleKV (arXiv:2507.06517, s28): STACK (kept, sibling).** Codebook replacement (s28, direction+magnitude entries) vs vote-weighted merging (s29, history-weighted entries): two answers to eviction loss, composable per layer (pyramid sets feed ZIP merges).\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** Eq.1-3 attention form is Vaswani 2017 (foundation, not a runtime surface). App C.2 (CaM comparison) recorded here, not reimplemented.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** keepkv after any evictor (takes keep/evict sets as input); with any backbone/vocab/scale/context/interface wiring; periodic plan beside any placer (external vs tiered residency are different stores).\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** one compressor per run (keepkv joins the \u00a727 Compress axis); encoder-decoder Arch crossed with the new Impl has no Impl provided and is out of scope here.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** merged cache presented as lossless without the vote-weighted scoring (losslessness holds under p-weighted attention only; plain recon error is reported alongside); Table-1/2 magnitudes cited as small-scale evidence (the small-scale run reports mass/error/bytes/sag; paper numbers are labeled claims); bound cited as a live guarantee (measured Theta under the computed bound, not paper-scale coverage).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
