      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: sag vs ZIP on identical scores (Thm.2 vs Thm.3, s29 x s27 axes)\n",
        "\"\"\"Convex-vs-ZIP merge comparison on a prefilled harness.\n",
        "\n",
        "Per head: merge the lowest-score evicted pair into its most-similar retained\n",
        "pair both ways (cosine convex vs vote-weighted ZIP) and report both output\n",
        "perturbations. Takes a prefilled harness plus keep-sets; returns means.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def keepkv_backprop_sagzip(harness, kept_map, seed=0):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    kk = KeepKVCompressor()\n",
        "    sag, zip = [], []\n",
        "    for k, c in harness.cache.items():\n",
        "        S = c[\"S\"]\n",
        "        T = c[\"K\"].shape[0]\n",
        "        kept = kept_map[k]\n",
        "        ev = [i for i in range(T) if i not in set(int(x) for x in kept.tolist())]\n",
        "        if not ev:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        e0 = ev[0]\n",
        "        Kn = c[\"K\"] / c[\"K\"].norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "        sims = Kn[e0] @ Kn[kept].T\n",
        "        cc = int(kept[int(sims.argmax())])\n",
        "        o_full = S[-1] @ c[\"V\"]\n",
        "        krc, vrc = _keepkv_convex(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"], e0, cc)\n",
        "        src = float(torch.exp(c[\"qlast\"] @ krc / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5)))\n",
        "        rest = [i for i in range(T) if i not in (e0, cc)]\n",
        "        cur = _t27.exp(c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0) @ c[\"K\"].T / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5)).squeeze(0)\n",
        "        oc = (cur[rest] @ c[\"V\"][rest] + src * vrc) / (cur[rest].sum() + src)\n",
        "        sag.append(float((oc - o_full).norm()))\n",
        "        acc = S.sum(0)\n",
        "        krz, vrz, prz = kk.zip_merge(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"], e0, cc, float(cur[e0]), float(cur[cc]))\n",
        "        srz = float(torch.exp(c[\"qlast\"] @ krz / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5)))\n",
        "        oz = (cur[rest] @ c[\"V\"][rest] + prz * srz * vrz) / (cur[rest].sum() + prz * srz)\n",
        "        zip.append(float((oz - o_full).norm()))\n",
        "    return {\"sag_mean\": float(sum(sag) / max(1, len(sag))),\n",
        "            \"zip_mean\": float(sum(zip) / max(1, len(zip)))}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: periodic byte plan (headline scheme, s29 x s27 Place)\n",
        "\"\"\"External-store + resident + reload byte math on a spec dict.\n",
        "\n",
        "Takes {\"T\",\"L\",\"H\",\"hs\",\"bpe\"} plus period/resident_ratio; returns the\n",
        "keepkv_periodic_plan verdict (policy simulation, declared).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def keepkv_backprop_periodic(spec, period=64, resident_ratio=0.2):\n",
        "    return keepkv_periodic_plan(spec, period=period, resident_ratio=resident_ratio)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 30. Coupled Quantization - arXiv:2405.03917 (Zhang, Yi, Xu, Shrivastava 2024, NeurIPS 2024)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** Channel-coupled vector quantization for KV cache: joint entropy grows sublinearly in group size (Eq.3-4, Fig.2) so per-channel quantization is suboptimal; groups of c contiguous channels share one b-bit code (CQ-<c>c<b>b, Eq.5 k-means, Eq.6 Fisher-weighted with diag-Fisher importance); both keys and values channel-coupled (unlike KIVI/KVQuant split); 1-bit CQ-8c8b beats KVQuant-2b at half memory (Table 1); sliding-window FP16 + rest coupled reaches near-native accuracy (Table 4); ablations confirm coupling and Fisher gains (Tables 5/6/8, Fig.5); throughput via bigger batches (Fig.4, Table 14 on par with KIVI); BPA formula App F; centroid overhead App E. Official code: NONE (checklist Q5 proprietary xMAD.ai); third-party pseudo-implementation noted, not used. Zhaozhuo Xu co-authors KIVI and CQ.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** no public code exists (see graded 17_RepoAudit). Our integration reimplements the paper text (not third-party code): Lloyd k-means with k-means++ seeding, uniform and Fisher-weighted variants, grouped VQ with exact byte/BPA accounting.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule): one Compress value.** Grouped channel VQ is mutually exclusive with the other compressors at the same K/V transform site (it replaces entries by centroid codes plus a centroid table), so it compiles as @Technique::KVCacheCompress::coupledquant with (channels, bits, fisher) parameters. Fisher weights arrive as an optional argument from one backward pass (paper Eq.6 needs activation grads); without grads it runs uniform. Sliding-window (Table 4) and KIVI-analog measurement sets are plain runner measurement sets, not axes. The shared \u00a727 harness is reused untouched.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Technique -> Impl -> original paper -> repo map\n",
        "\n",
        "| CQ part | Paper ref | Impl value | Official repo |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Coupled VQ + centroids (Eq.5/6) | arXiv:2405.03917 \u00a73.2 | KVCacheCompress::coupledquant | none (proprietary xMAD.ai) |\n",
        "| Sliding-window composition (Table 4) | arXiv:2405.03917 \u00a74.2 | plain runner leg (no axis) | none |\n",
        "| BPA accounting (App F) | arXiv:2405.03917 App F | plain byte math (no axis) | none |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) Lloyd k-means (uniform/Fisher) instead of the paper's GPU k-means++100-iter runs - same objectives, reduced iteration counts; (2) Fisher grads from one last-token backward on harness captures (paper: calibration-set Fisher); (3) BPA table term uses the live context length (paper amortizes at T=65536); (4) harness has no RoPE: coupled groups run on captured projections directly; (5) kernel-fusion/shared-memory throughput claims stay paper-reported (policy note, not measured).\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::KVCacheCompress::coupledquant{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
      "\"\"\"Coupled Quantization (Zhang et al., arXiv:2405.03917 \u00a73.2; Eq.5-6).\n",
      "\n",
      "Groups of c contiguous channels share one b-bit code (nearest centroid,\n",
      "L2). Uniform Lloyd k-means by default; Fisher-weighted variant takes\n",
      "per-activation grads (diag-Fisher importance, Eq.6). Stored: codes +\n",
        "FP16 centroid table; bytes and BPA reported: code-BPA = b/c plus the\n",
        "paper's full App F figure b/c + 2^b/65536 (centroid amortization over\n",
        "L=65536). CQ-<c>c<b>b naming. Keys and values both channel-coupled\n",
        "(paper \u00a74.3).\"\"\"\n",
        "class CoupledQuantCompressor:\n",
        "    scope = \"token\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, channels=4, bits=8, fisher=False):\n",
        "        self.channels, self.bits, self.fisher = channels, bits, fisher\n",
      "    def _kmeans(self, X, k, weights=None, seed=0):\n",
      "        g = _t27.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
      "        C = [X[_t27.randint(X.shape[0], (1,), generator=g).item()]]\n",
      "        for _ in range(1, k):\n",
      "            d2 = ((X.unsqueeze(1) - _t27.stack(C).unsqueeze(0)) ** 2).sum(-1).min(-1).values\n",
      "            s = d2.sum()\n",
      "            if s <= 0:\n",
      "                probs = _t27.ones_like(d2) / max(1, d2.numel())\n",
      "            else:\n",
      "                probs = d2 / s\n",
      "            C.append(X[_t27.multinomial(probs, 1, generator=g).item()])\n",
      "        C = _t27.stack(C)\n",
        "        w = _t27.ones(X.shape[0]) if weights is None else weights\n",
        "        for _ in range(20):\n",
      "            a = ((X.unsqueeze(1) - C.unsqueeze(0)) ** 2).sum(-1).argmin(-1)\n",
      "            Cn = _t27.zeros_like(C)\n",
      "            for j in range(k):\n",
      "                m = a == j\n",
      "                if m.any():\n",
      "                    Cn[j] = (X[m] * w[m].unsqueeze(-1)).sum(0) / w[m].sum().clamp_min(1e-30)\n",
      "                else:\n",
      "                    Cn[j] = X[_t27.randint(X.shape[0], (1,), generator=g)]\n",
      "            if _t27.allclose(Cn, C):\n",
      "                C = Cn\n",
      "                break\n",
      "            C = Cn\n",
      "        a = ((X.unsqueeze(1) - C.unsqueeze(0)) ** 2).sum(-1).argmin(-1)\n",
      "        return C, a\n",
      "    def _vq(self, X, grads=None):\n",
      "        T, d = X.shape\n",
      "        c, b = self.channels, self.bits\n",
      "        assert d % c == 0\n",
      "        out = _t27.zeros_like(X)\n",
      "        tbl, used, poss = 0, 0, 0\n",
      "        for gi in range(d // c):\n",
      "            Xg = X[:, gi * c:(gi + 1) * c]\n",
      "            wg = None\n",
      "            if self.fisher and grads is not None:\n",
      "                wg = (grads[:, gi * c:(gi + 1) * c] ** 2).sum(-1)\n",
      "            C, a = self._kmeans(Xg, 2 ** b, wg, seed=gi)\n",
      "            out[:, gi * c:(gi + 1) * c] = C[a]\n",
      "            tbl += C.numel()\n",
      "            used += int(a.unique().numel())\n",
      "            poss += 2 ** b\n",
      "        return out, tbl, used / max(1, poss)\n",
      "    def compress(self, K, V, grads_k=None, grads_v=None, **kw):\n",
      "        Kh, tk, uk = self._vq(K, grads_k)\n",
      "        Vh, tv, uv = self._vq(V, grads_v)\n",
      "        T, d = K.shape\n",
      "        codes = T * (d // self.channels) * self.bits / 8\n",
      "        tbl = (tk + tv) * 2\n",
      "        nb = int(codes * 2 + tbl)\n",
      "        return Kh, Vh, {\"bytes\": nb, \"code_bpa\": self.bits / self.channels,\n",
      "                        \"paper_bpa\": self.bits / self.channels + 2.0 ** self.bits / 65536.0,\n",
      "                        \"table_bytes\": int(tbl), \"codes_used_frac\": (uk + uv) / 2,\n",
      "                        \"recon_k\": float((K - Kh).norm() / (K.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
      "                        \"recon_v\": float((V - Vh).norm() / (V.norm() + 1e-12))}\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
      "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: CQ end-to-end | Legs full / per-channel-2bit (KIVI-analog via kvc_sym_quant) / coupled (c=4,b=8 + c=8,b=8) / Fisher-weighted (one backward for grads) / sliding-window-32 + BPA row | emits outputs/cq_results.json | plain orchestrator, no Impl tag by design.\n",
      "import torch as _t27\n",
      "import json as _j30\n",
      "import time as _time30\n",
      "from pathlib import Path as _P30\n",
      "def _cq_harness_grads(model, ids):\n",
      "    \"\"\"One forward+backward on last-token CE; per-head K/V activation grads.\n",
      "\n",
      "    Hooks Head.key/Head.value outputs (head-layout models); returns\n",
      "    {(li,hi): (gK, gV)}. Self-contained for the Fisher leg.\n",
      "    \"\"\"\n",
      "    caps, grads, hooks = {}, {}, []\n",
      "    def _fh(name):\n",
      "        def fn(m, inp, out):\n",
      "            caps[name] = out\n",
      "        return fn\n",
      "    for li, b in enumerate(model.blocks):\n",
      "        for hi, h in enumerate(b.self_attn.heads):\n",
      "            hooks.append(h.key.register_forward_hook(_fh((li, hi, \"k\"))))\n",
      "            hooks.append(h.value.register_forward_hook(_fh((li, hi, \"v\"))))\n",
      "    dev = next(model.parameters()).device\n",
      "    xb = _t27.tensor([ids], dtype=_t27.long).to(dev)\n",
      "    model.eval()\n",
      "    logits = model(xb)\n",
      "    loss = _t27.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits[:, -1, :], xb[:, -1])\n",
      "    model.zero_grad()\n",
      "    gs = _t27.autograd.grad(loss, [caps[k] for k in caps])\n",
      "    for h in hooks:\n",
      "        h.remove()\n",
      "    out = {}\n",
      "    items = list(caps.items())\n",
      "    for (key, g) in zip([k for k, _ in items], gs):\n",
      "        out.setdefault((key[0], key[1]), {})[key[2]] = g.detach().squeeze(0)\n",
      "    return out\n",
      "def run_cq_benchmark(make_model, ids, seed=17, out_path=\"outputs/cq_results.json\"):\n",
      "    \"\"\"Run CQ measurement sets on one prefilled model.\n",
      "\n",
      "    make_model: zero-arg factory for the compiled-path NanoGPT (factory seeds\n",
      "    construction; runner seeds its own draws). Writes outputs/cq_results.json.\n",
      "    \"\"\"\n",
      "    t0 = _time30.time()\n",
      "    model = make_model()\n",
      "    model.eval()\n",
      "    H = KVCacheHarness(model, budget=None).prefill(ids)\n",
      "    full = H.eq12_bytes()[\"full\"]\n",
      "    m0 = H.retained_mass({k: _t27.arange(H.T) for k in H.cache})\n",
      "    measurements = {\"full\": {\"paper_claim\": \"baseline (FP16 16 BPA)\",\n",
      "                     \"mass\": float(sum(m0.values()) / max(1, len(m0))),\n",
      "                     \"bytes\": full, \"ratio\": 1.0}}\n",
      "    rk, rv, nk = [], [], 0\n",
      "    for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
      "        Kh, _ = kvc_sym_quant(c[\"K\"], 2, red_dim=0)\n",
      "        Vh, _ = kvc_sym_quant(c[\"V\"], 2, red_dim=1)\n",
      "        rk.append(float((c[\"K\"] - Kh).norm() / (c[\"K\"].norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
      "        rv.append(float((c[\"V\"] - Vh).norm() / (c[\"V\"].norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
      "        nk += int(c[\"K\"].numel() + c[\"V\"].numel()) * 2 / 8\n",
      "    measurements[\"perchannel_2b\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: KIVI-style collapses at 1-2b; CQ wins (Tables 1/5)\",\n",
      "                            \"recon_k\": float(sum(rk) / max(1, len(rk))),\n",
      "                            \"recon_v\": float(sum(rv) / max(1, len(rv))),\n",
      "                            \"bytes\": nk, \"ratio\": nk / max(1, full)}\n",
      "    for tag, cc, bb in ((\"cq4c8b\", 4, 8), (\"cq8c8b\", 8, 8)):\n",
      "        cq = CoupledQuantCompressor(channels=cc, bits=bb)\n",
      "        rks, rvs, nbytes, oerr, cu = [], [], 0, [], []\n",
      "        for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
      "            Kh, Vh, meta = cq.compress(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"])\n",
      "            rks.append(meta[\"recon_k\"])\n",
      "            rvs.append(meta[\"recon_v\"])\n",
      "            nbytes += meta[\"bytes\"]\n",
      "            cu.append(meta[\"codes_used_frac\"])\n",
      "            lk = (c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0) @ Kh.T / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5))\n",
      "            o2 = (_t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1) @ Vh).squeeze(0)\n",
      "            o1 = c[\"S\"][-1] @ c[\"V\"]\n",
      "            oerr.append(float((o1 - o2).norm() / (o1.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
      "        measurements[tag] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: CQ-4c8b 2.00 BPA / CQ-8c8b 1.00 BPA (Table 1)\",\n",
      "                     \"code_bpa\": bb / cc, \"bytes\": nbytes, \"ratio\": nbytes / max(1, full),\n",
      "                     \"recon_k\": float(sum(rks) / max(1, len(rks))),\n",
      "                     \"recon_v\": float(sum(rvs) / max(1, len(rvs))),\n",
      "                     \"codes_used\": float(sum(cu) / max(1, len(cu))),\n",
      "                     \"out_err\": float(sum(oerr) / max(1, len(oerr)))}\n",
      "    try:\n",
      "        fg = _cq_harness_grads(model, ids)\n",
      "        cqf = CoupledQuantCompressor(channels=8, bits=8, fisher=True)\n",
      "        rks, rvs, nbytes, cu = [], [], 0, []\n",
      "        for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
      "            gk = fg.get(k, {}).get(\"k\")\n",
      "            gv = fg.get(k, {}).get(\"v\")\n",
      "            Kh, Vh, meta = cqf.compress(c[\"K\"], c[\"V\"], grads_k=gk, grads_v=gv)\n",
      "            rks.append(meta[\"recon_k\"])\n",
      "            rvs.append(meta[\"recon_v\"])\n",
      "            nbytes += meta[\"bytes\"]\n",
      "            cu.append(meta[\"codes_used_frac\"])\n",
      "        measurements[\"fisher_8c8b\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: Fisher 8.09 vs uniform 32.12 (Table 6)\",\n",
      "                               \"recon_k\": float(sum(rks) / max(1, len(rks))),\n",
      "                               \"recon_v\": float(sum(rvs) / max(1, len(rvs))),\n",
      "                               \"codes_used\": float(sum(cu) / max(1, len(cu))),\n",
      "                               \"bytes\": nbytes, \"ratio\": nbytes / max(1, full)}\n",
      "    except Exception as e:\n",
      "        measurements[\"fisher_8c8b\"] = {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
      "    W = min(32, H.T)\n",
      "    cq = CoupledQuantCompressor(channels=8, bits=8)\n",
      "    nbytes, oerr, cu = 0, [], []\n",
      "    for k, c in H.cache.items():\n",
      "        Kh, Vh, meta = cq.compress(c[\"K\"][:-W], c[\"V\"][:-W])\n",
      "        nbytes += meta[\"bytes\"] + int(2 * W * c[\"head_dim\"] * 4)\n",
      "        cu.append(meta[\"codes_used_frac\"])\n",
      "        Kf = _t27.cat([Kh, c[\"K\"][-W:]])\n",
      "        Vf = _t27.cat([Vh, c[\"V\"][-W:]])\n",
      "        lk = (c[\"qlast\"].unsqueeze(0) @ Kf.T / (c[\"head_dim\"] ** 0.5))\n",
      "        o2 = (_t27.softmax(lk, dim=-1) @ Vf).squeeze(0)\n",
      "        o1 = c[\"S\"][-1] @ c[\"V\"]\n",
      "        oerr.append(float((o1 - o2).norm() / (o1.norm() + 1e-12)))\n",
      "    measurements[\"window32_8c8b\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: -0.618/-0.476 avg loss at 1-bit (Table 4)\",\n",
      "                             \"bytes\": nbytes, \"ratio\": nbytes / max(1, full),\n",
      "                             \"codes_used\": float(sum(cu) / max(1, len(cu))),\n",
      "                             \"out_err\": float(sum(oerr) / max(1, len(oerr)))}\n",
      "    res = {\"paper\": \"arXiv:2405.03917\", \"seed\": seed, \"T\": H.T,\n",
      "           \"purpose\": \"small-scale mechanism measurement sets (recon/bytes/BPA); paper magnitudes are reported claims only\",\n",
      "           \"measurements\": measurements, \"seconds\": round(_time30.time() - t0, 1)}\n",
      "    _P30(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
      "    _P30(out_path).write_text(_j30.dumps(res, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
      "    ok = {n: (\"error\" not in v) for n, v in measurements.items()}\n",
      "    print(_j30.dumps({\"measurements_ok\": ok}, indent=2))\n",
      "    return res\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
