        "### Relations: CQ (arXiv:2405.03917) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Joint channel VQ meets every prior section at the frozen forward: groups share codes (dependence exploited), centroids learned once (calibration transfer), Fisher weights protect salient activations. All relations STACK unless stated; coupledquant extends the \u00a727 Compress axis.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probe signal re-measured on coupled-quantized states; centroid tables as shared probe geometry.\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Exit gating and code precision are different stages; quantized entries persist across exits.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Correlation drift re-measured at Tmem vs Tgrok - same loop, new readout.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** Context windows, code groups, calibration windows: three grouping instincts, never merged.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** Grouped VQ runs on projections under any readout; re-runs under geodesicflat unchanged.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Pruned dims feed grouped VQ directly (fewer channels per group budget).\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Steered tokens kept at higher precision (mixed-precision instinct shared with MiKV); protection semantics compose.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam priors and code structure are two frozen-state readouts.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP gradients vs Fisher activation-grads: two gradient consumers, one backward; centroids as attribution units.\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): STACK (kept).** Rank-1 weight compile vs grouped-code history compile - two compressions.\n",
        "- **vs LBI (arXiv:2605.09204, s26): STACK (kept).** Regions (gradient groups) vs channel groups (dependence groups); region-partitioned codebooks compose directly.\n",
        "- **vs KVCache survey (arXiv:2603.20397, s27): STACK (kept, closest kin).** CQ sits beside KIVI (asymmetric 2-bit, same first author Zhaozhuo Xu) and KVQuant (NUQ tables) on the Compress axis: per-channel/per-token vs coupled-group, same BPA accounting, quantization-orthogonality kept.\n",
        "- **vs SpindleKV (arXiv:2507.06517, s28): STACK (kept, sibling).** Codebook replacement (direction+magnitude entries) vs coupled VQ (centroid codes): two codebooks, different alphabets; pyramid sets feed grouped codes.\n",
        "- **vs KeepKV (arXiv:2504.09936, s29): STACK (kept, sibling).** Vote-weighted merging vs grouped quantization: history weights vs channel codes; merge-then-quantize composes per head.\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** Scaled dot-product form is Vaswani 2017 (foundation, not a runtime surface).\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** coupledquant after any evictor (operates on survivors); with any backbone/vocab/scale/context/interface wiring; Fisher grads from any backward; sliding-window leg beside any placer.\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** one compressor per run (coupledquant joins the \u00a727 Compress axis); encoder-decoder Arch crossed with the new Impl has no Impl provided and is out of scope here.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** centroid tables presented as free (table bytes always counted; App-F term uses live context); paper PPL/accuracy cited as small-scale evidence (the small-scale run reports recon/bytes/BPA; paper numbers are labeled claims); Fisher live gain presented as paper-scale PPL gain (the small-scale run reports weighted-objective convergence + recon deltas).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
