        "### Relations: EpiCache (arXiv:2509.17396) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Episodic multi-turn caching meets every prior section at the frozen forward: blocks bound memory, episodes partition topics, medoids score, sensitivity splits budgets. All relations STACK unless stated; episodic extends the \u00a727 Evict axis; clustering/matching/allocation compose plainly.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probe signal re-measured on episodic caches; episode centroids as probe strata (topic-stratified probing).\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Exit gating and episode residency are different stages; per-turn exits reuse resident episode caches.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** Episode structure re-measured at Tmem vs Tgrok - same loop, new readout.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** ConvMem windows, block-prefill blocks, episode segments: three partitions, never merged.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** Clustering/matching run on captures under any readout; re-runs under geodesicflat unchanged.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Pruned dims feed episode means directly (fewer dims per segment budget).\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Steered turns pin episode membership (steer first, cluster second); protection semantics compose.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam priors and episode structure are two frozen-state readouts.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP gradients vs patched-prompt scores for candidacy; episodes as attribution scopes.\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): STACK (kept).** Rank-1 weight compile vs episodic history partition - compile vs organize.\n",
        "- **vs LBI (arXiv:2605.09204, s26): STACK (kept).** Regions (gradient groups) vs episodes (topic groups); region-partitioned episodic caches compose directly.\n",
        "- **vs KVCache survey (arXiv:2603.20397, s27): STACK (kept, closest kin).** EpiCache instantiates survey eviction beside H2O/SnapKV/AdaKV with block bounds; AdaKV allocates across heads, episodic across layers - complementary scopes, same Eq.1-2 accounting.\n",
        "- **vs SpindleKV (arXiv:2507.06517, s28): STACK (kept, sibling).** Pyramid layer schedule (static) vs sensitivity schedule (measured); codebooks beside episode caches: two organizations of history.\n",
        "- **vs KeepKV (arXiv:2504.09936, s29): STACK (kept, sibling).** Vote-weighted merging vs episodic partitioning: history weights vs topic caches; merge-then-partition composes per episode.\n",
        "- **vs CQ (arXiv:2405.03917, s30): STACK (kept, sibling).** Grouped channel codes vs grouped topic caches: channel groups vs episode groups; quantize-then-partition composes (paper's own future work: quantization into episodic caches).\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** Cross-attention scoring form is Vaswani 2017 (foundation, not a runtime surface).\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** episodic after any backbone/vocab/scale/context/interface wiring (hooks read whatever the compiled Heads compute); block loop around any evictor (peak bound is structural); sensitivity allocation over any layer count; episode caches beside any placer (resident vs offloaded are different stores).\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** one evictor per run (episodic joins the \u00a727 Evict axis); encoder-decoder Arch crossed with the new Impl has no Impl provided and is out of scope here.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** episode caches presented as lossless (matched mass + output error always reported; full-cache parity belongs to the none baseline); LongConvQA magnitudes cited as small-scale evidence (the small-scale run reports mass/error/bytes/peak; paper numbers are labeled claims); key-similarity proxy presented as fembed equivalence (proxy documented as stand-in, medoid math exact).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
