      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: block-vs-post peak and mass (Fig.1 analog, s31 x s27 Place)\n",
        "\"\"\"Streaming block-prefill audit on a prefilled harness.\n",
        "\n",
        "Fig.1 shows post-prefill peak scaling linearly while block prefill stays\n",
        "flat. Takes a prefilled harness plus budget/block; replays the block loop\n",
        "and returns peak usage vs the M+Mblock bound alongside retained mass.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def epicache_backprop_block(harness, budget=16, Mblock=8, seed=0):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    c0 = harness.cache[(0, 0)]\n",
        "    T = c0[\"K\"].shape[0]\n",
        "    S = _t27.stack([harness.cache[(0, h)][\"S\"] for h in range(len(harness.layers[0]))]).mean(0)\n",
        "    kept, peak = [], 0\n",
        "    for s in range(0, T, Mblock):\n",
        "        block = list(range(s, min(s + Mblock, T)))\n",
        "        W = S[max(0, min(s + Mblock, T) - 1):min(s + Mblock, T) + 7]\n",
        "        base = W.max(0).values\n",
        "        cand = sorted(set(kept) | set(block))\n",
        "        kept = sorted(cand, key=lambda i: -float(base[i]))[:budget]\n",
        "        peak = max(peak, len(cand))\n",
        "    return {\"T\": T, \"peak\": peak, \"bound\": budget + Mblock,\n",
        "            \"bound_ok\": bool(peak <= budget + Mblock),\n",
        "            \"mass\": float(S[-1][kept].sum())}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: sensitivity allocation audit (Fig.4 analog, s31 x s26 regions)\n",
        "\"\"\"Layer-sensitivity budget split on a prefilled harness.\n",
        "\n",
        "Fig.4 shows sensitivity-aware allocation beating uniform/pyramid splits.\n",
        "Takes a prefilled harness; measures per-layer key drift under a\n",
        "sink+recent restriction analog, allocates by Eq.10, and compares the\n",
        "sensitivity-weighted retained mass against a uniform split.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def epicache_backprop_sens(harness, budget=16, alpha=1.1, seed=0):\n",
        "    import torch as _t27\n",
        "    ev = EpisodicEvictor(budget=budget)\n",
        "    sens = []\n",
        "    for li in range(harness.n_layers):\n",
        "        Ks = [harness.cache[(li, h)][\"K\"] for h in range(len(harness.layers[0]))]\n",
        "        Kf = _t27.stack(Ks).mean(0)\n",
        "        Kb = Kf.clone()\n",
        "        Kb[4:-8] = 0.3 * _t27.randn_like(Kb[4:-8]) + 0.1 * Kb[4:-8]\n",
        "        cos = (Kf * Kb).sum(-1) / (Kf.norm(dim=-1) * Kb.norm(dim=-1)).clamp_min(1e-12)\n",
        "        sens.append(1.0 - float(cos.mean()))\n",
        "    alloc = ev.allocate_layer(sens, budget, alpha=alpha)\n",
        "    mass_s, mass_u = [], []\n",
        "    for li in range(harness.n_layers):\n",
        "        S = _t27.stack([harness.cache[(li, h)][\"S\"] for h in range(len(harness.layers[0]))]).mean(0)\n",
        "        acc = S.sum(0)\n",
        "        ks = max(1, int(round(alloc[li])))\n",
        "        ku = max(1, budget)\n",
        "        mass_s.append(float(S[-1][_t27.topk(acc, min(ks, acc.numel())).indices].sum()))\n",
        "        mass_u.append(float(S[-1][_t27.topk(acc, min(ku, acc.numel())).indices].sum()))\n",
        "    gs = sum(mass_s) / max(1, len(mass_s))\n",
        "    gu = sum(mass_u) / max(1, len(mass_u))\n",
        "    return {\"sensitivities\": sens, \"allocation\": alloc,\n",
        "            \"sums_ok\": bool(abs(sum(alloc) - harness.n_layers * budget) < 1e-6),\n",
        "            \"mass_sens\": gs, \"mass_uniform\": gu}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 32. Training-Free Looped Transformers - arXiv:2605.23872 (Chen, Li, Liang, Lao, Liu 2026, UT Austin)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Paper in one paragraph.** An inference-time wrapper loops a contiguous mid-stack window `g = L_b o ... o L_a` of a FROZEN checkpoint K times with no fine-tuning, no new parameters and no architecture change (Eq.1-2, Fig.1). Naive re-application degrades performance, because a pre-norm block is exactly one forward Euler step on the window residual field `x' = F_g(x)`, `F_g(x) := g(x) - x` (Eq.5-8), so K-fold naive looping integrates to t=K while the post-loop layers were trained to read the t=1 endpoint. The remedy is to keep t=1 and refine it: K damped sub-steps of size h=1/K (Eq.10), or the s-stage explicit Runge-Kutta family (Eq.11-12) instantiated with the front-loaded tableau `a_ij = (1/K)1(j<i)`, `b_1 = beta + (1-beta)/K`, `b_i = (1-beta)/K` (Eq.13-16, Algorithms 1-3), whose output is exactly `beta g(x0) + (1-beta) F^(K)(x0)`. Block-mode `(L_b...L_a)^K` and layer-mode `L_b^K o ... o L_a^K` (Eq.3-4) behave similarly on dense backbones, but on MoE the gate is re-evaluated on the perturbed state each iteration and routing thrashes, so layer-mode (gate computed once, same expert mixture applied K times) is the required default (Sec.2.2, Sec.3.3, Table 2c). Decode-time KV handling uses snapshot/restore per loop layer plus one stash pass (cache = first / last / none, Eq.19, Algorithms 4-5). Results: +2.64 pp MMLU-Pro and +2.01 pp GPQA-Main on Qwen3-4B-Instruct, +1.14 pp CSQA on Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct, +1.20 pp OBQA on Moonlight-16B-A3B (Tables 3-4), 87% of 45 cells non-negative under one untuned recipe (n=4 window at depth fraction 0.45-0.60, Sec.3.2, Fig.6), stable across K in 1..24 while uniform loop fails after K>=6 and naive loop falls to -17.71 pp at K=6 (Fig.4), and no higher-order solver or fixed-point accelerator beats K=2 damped Euler across 40+ configurations (Tables 8-11) - the block is not a contraction.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Repo note:** NO official code is publicly verifiable. The PDF carries a single link (its own arXiv abs page), the arXiv abs page and the first author's homepage carry no code URL, and `github.com/L-z-Chen/Training-Free-Looped-Transformer` returns 404 with no Wayback snapshot, while two independent reproductions cite that slug as the 'public upstream' (see graded 19_RepoAudit). Our integration is therefore derived from the paper text alone; third-party repos (`JegZheng/tflt-dev`, `Navi-AI-Lab/loopgraft`, `EdoardoPona/looped-laguna`, `singularity119/Training-Free-Looped-Transformers-Reproduction`) are used as non-authoritative symbol cross-checks only, and one of them (loopgraft) diverges by using per-pass replay KV caches instead of the paper's snapshot/restore + single stash pass.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Five paper-side discrepancies recorded (graded 19_RepoAudit):** Algorithm 3 as printed performs K-1 sub-steps while Eq. (16) requires K (we verify the resulting gap numerically); Table 2c caption says layer K=2 while its column header says layer K=3; the 16-task no-loop baseline is quoted as 55.54 (Table 2a), 55.60 (Table 6) and 55.598 (Table 10); Table 1 budgets K forward passes for Aitken d2 although the stated per-step update needs two evaluations of g unless the next iterate's evaluation is reused; Table 6 lists Qwen1.5-MoE rows in block-mode although Sec. 3.1 prescribes layer-mode for MoE.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Integration reasoning (s17 rule: one new value per genuine delta).** Looping is a new runtime surface - it re-applies a depth window inside a frozen forward - so it gets its own axis rather than joining Attn (an attention score rule) or the KV-cache axes (a history-store rule). The loop strategy family is one axis (`DepthLoop`) because every value replaces the SAME site (the update applied to the window iterate between g evaluations); iteration mode is a second axis (`LoopMode`) because it changes what is nested (window-as-a-unit vs layer-by-layer); the KV stash rule is a third (`LoopCache`) and the decode-time gating a fourth (`LoopDecode`), because each is an independent switch on a different code path. Four axes rather than one long value list: the paper's own per-cell configurations are `[start-end] mode K strategy cache decode`, so the axes decompose exactly along the paper's configuration grammar.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Technique -> Impl -> original paper -> repo map\n",
        "\n",
        "| Looped-transformer part | Paper ref | Impl value | Official repo |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Loop wrapper over window [a,b] (Eq.1-2) | arXiv:2605.23872 Sec.2.1 | DepthLoop (substrate, always present) | none exists |\n",
        "| Naive loop `x <- g(x)` x K | Table 1, Fig.4b | DepthLoop::naiveloop | none exists |\n",
        "| Damped sub-steps `x + (1/K)(g(x)-x)` (Eq.10) | Sec.2.3, Table 1 | DepthLoop::dampedeuler | none exists |\n",
        "| Midpoint / Heun / RK4 (Eq.11-12, Table 1) | Table 1 | DepthLoop::rkmidpoint, ::rkheun, ::rk4 | none exists |\n",
        "| Heavy-ball / Anderson / Aitken (Table 1) | Table 1, Tables 9-11 | DepthLoop::heavygball, ::anderson, ::aitken | none exists |\n",
        "| norm_stab / poly_blend (Table 10) | Table 10 | DepthLoop::normstab, ::polyblend | none exists |\n",
        "| Front-loaded anchored RK (Eq.13-16, Alg.3) | Sec.2.3, Table 6 | DepthLoop::blockanchored | none exists |\n",
        "| Block-mode `(L_b..L_a)^K` (Eq.3, Alg.1/4) | Sec.2.2 | LoopMode::blockmode | none exists |\n",
        "| Layer-mode `L_b^K..L_a^K` (Eq.4, Alg.2/5) | Sec.2.2, Sec.3.3 | LoopMode::layermode | none exists |\n",
        "| KV stash from x_a / from g(K)(x_a) / no write (Eq.19) | App. C, Table 20 | LoopCache::first, ::last, ::none | none exists |\n",
        "| Loop only at prefill / every decode step / first n tokens | App. C.3, Table 15 | LoopDecode::bypass, ::full, ::firstn | none exists |\n",
        "| Depth-fraction window rule (Sec.3.2, Fig.6) | Sec.3.2 | plain always-present helper (no axis) | none exists |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Adaptations with consequences (documented, kept):** (1) our residual window is the compiled model's own `nn.Sequential` of blocks, so the wrapper duplicates no model class and adds no parameters - it re-runs the window map; (2) nanoGPT here has no KV cache object, so the paper's snapshot/restore + stash protocol is exercised by an explicit per-layer length accounting simulator (`LoopCacheSim`) that reproduces the paper's invariant (net cache delta exactly b-a+1 entries regardless of K) rather than a transformers `DynamicCache`; (3) there is no MoE backbone here, so the routing-thrash mechanism is exercised by an explicit top-1 gate proxy (gate re-evaluated on the perturbed state vs pinned), not by an MoE model; (4) paper magnitudes (accuracy deltas on Qwen3/Llama/Moonlight checkpoints, wall-clock seconds, 20000 H100 hours) are reported claims - our measurement sets report mechanism metrics only.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT s32 loop-window substrate (arXiv:2605.23872 Sec.2.1-2.3, Eq.1-2, 5-10) | LoopWrapper re-applies a contiguous mid-stack window of the compiled model's OWN blocks K times under one DepthLoop update rule, with LoopMode nesting, LoopCache stash accounting and LoopDecode gating | No parameters added, no architecture change: pre-loop blocks 0..a-1, looped window g = L_b o ... o L_a, post-loop blocks b+1..N-1 (Eq.2) | runner uses the default path.\n",
        "import torch as _t32\n",
        "class LoopWrapper:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Training-free loop window over a frozen model's own block stack.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Eq.(1) g := L_b o ... o L_a ; Eq.(2) splits the network into\n",
        "    pre-loop / g^(K) / post-loop ; Eq.(6) F_g(x) := g(x) - x is the window\n",
        "    residual field, so one window application is a forward Euler step at\n",
        "    h=1. Block pass counts are instrumented per block in self.calls.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, model, a, b, K=1, mode=\"blockmode\", update=None,\n",
        "                 beta=0.5, h=1.0, cache=\"last\", decode=\"bypass\", first_n=0,\n",
        "                 state=None):\n",
        "        self.model = model\n",
        "        self.a, self.b, self.K = int(a), int(b), int(K)\n",
        "        self.mode = mode\n",
        "        self.update = update\n",
        "        self.state = state\n",
        "        self.beta, self.h = float(beta), float(h)\n",
        "        self.cache, self.decode, self.first_n = cache, decode, int(first_n)\n",
        "        self.n_layers = len(model.blocks)\n",
        "        self.width = self.b - self.a + 1\n",
        "        self._dec = 0\n",
        "        self._pred = self._decode_pred()\n",
        "        self.reset_state()\n",
        "    def _decode_pred(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"LoopDecode predicate from the compiled path (App.C.3); None if uncompiled.\"\"\"\n",
        "        for _name in (\"LoopDecodeBypass\", \"LoopDecodeFull\", \"LoopDecodeFirstN\"):\n",
        "            _cls = globals().get(_name)\n",
        "            if _cls is not None:\n",
        "                return _cls()\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    def _loop_check(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"LoopDecode gate: loop body during always-prefill, per value at decode.\"\"\"\n",
        "        seq_len = int(x.shape[1])\n",
        "        if seq_len > 1:\n",
        "            return True\n",
        "        if self._pred is None:\n",
        "            return True\n",
        "        if not self._pred.loops_on_decode:\n",
        "            return False\n",
        "        if self.first_n and hasattr(self._pred, \"n_first\"):\n",
        "            self._pred.n_first = self.first_n\n",
        "        gate = bool(self._pred.should_loop(seq_len, self._dec))\n",
        "        self._dec += 1\n",
        "        return gate\n",
        "    def reset_calls(self):\n",
        "        self.calls = {li: 0 for li in range(self.n_layers)}\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def reset_state(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Clear per-window iteration state of the selected DepthLoop update.\"\"\"\n",
        "        self.reset_calls()\n",
        "        self._dec = 0\n",
        "        if self.state is not None and hasattr(self.state, \"reset\"):\n",
        "            self.state.reset()\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def block(self, li, x):\n",
        "        self.calls[li] = self.calls.get(li, 0) + 1\n",
        "        return self.model.blocks[li](x)\n",
        "    def g(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"One window application (Eq.1): L_b o ... o L_a.\"\"\"\n",
        "        for li in range(self.a, self.b + 1):\n",
        "            x = self.block(li, x)\n",
        "        return x\n",
        "    def field(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Window residual field F_g(x) = g(x) - x (Eq.6).\"\"\"\n",
        "        return self.g(x) - x\n",
        "    def substeps(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"K damped sub-steps of size h/K (Eq.10).\"\"\"\n",
        "        step = self.h / max(1, self.K)\n",
        "        for _ in range(self.K):\n",
        "            x = x + step * self.field(x)\n",
        "        return x\n",
        "    def layer_apply(self, li, x, update):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Layer-mode: iterate ONE window layer K times (Alg.2/5).\n",
        "\n",
        "        The anchor of Alg.3 line 4 is taken per layer, so per-window\n",
        "        iteration state is reset before each layer.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        if self.state is not None and hasattr(self.state, \"reset\"):\n",
        "            self.state.reset()\n",
        "        if update is None:\n",
        "            return self.block(li, x)\n",
        "        for _ in range(self.K):\n",
        "            y = self.block(li, x)\n",
        "            x = update(self, x, y)\n",
        "        return x\n",
        "    def loop_body(self, x):\n",
        "        if self.state is not None and hasattr(self.state, \"reset\"):\n",
        "            self.state.reset()\n",
        "        if self.mode == \"layermode\":\n",
        "            for li in range(self.a, self.b + 1):\n",
        "                x = self.layer_apply(li, x, self.update)\n",
        "            return x\n",
        "        upd = self.update\n",
        "        if upd is None:\n",
        "            return self.g(x)\n",
        "        for _ in range(self.K):\n",
        "            y = self.g(x)\n",
        "            x = upd(self, x, y)\n",
        "        return x\n",
        "    def stream(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"pre-loop 0..a-1, looped window, post-loop b+1..N-1 (Eq.2); LoopDecode-gated.\"\"\"\n",
        "        for li in range(0, self.a):\n",
        "            x = self.block(li, x)\n",
        "        if self._loop_check(x):\n",
        "            x = self.loop_body(x)\n",
        "        for li in range(self.b + 1, self.n_layers):\n",
        "            x = self.block(li, x)\n",
        "        return x\n",
        "    def forward(self, idx, position=0):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Same forward as the compiled model, with g^(K) in the window.\"\"\"\n",
        "        T = idx.shape[1]\n",
        "        pos = _t32.arange(position, position + T, dtype=_t32.long, device=idx.device)\n",
        "        x = self.model.token_embedding(idx) + self.model.position_embedding(pos)\n",
        "        x = self.stream(x)\n",
        "        return self.model.lm_head(self.model.ln_final(x))\n",
        "    def window_center_fraction(self):\n",
        "        return (self.a + self.b) / 2.0 / max(1, self.n_layers)\n",
        "    def pass_counts(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Forward passes per block; paper cost model 1 + (K-1)*W/N.\"\"\"\n",
        "        per = getattr(self.update, \"evals_per_step\", 1) if self.update is not None else 1\n",
        "        win = per * self.K\n",
        "        exp = {li: (win if self.a <= li <= self.b else 1) for li in range(self.n_layers)}\n",
        "        return dict(self.calls), exp\n",
        "def loop_window_for(n_layers, width=4, lo=0.45, hi=0.60):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Depth-fraction rule (Sec.3.2, Fig.6).\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns the n-layer window whose centre depth fraction is closest to the\n",
        "    middle of the empirical sweet-spot band [lo, hi] (0.45-0.60).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    w = max(1, min(int(width), n_layers))\n",
        "    mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n",
        "    cands = [(abs((2 * a + w - 1) / 2.0 / n_layers - mid), a) for a in range(0, n_layers - w + 1)]\n",
        "    a = min(cands)[1]\n",
        "    return a, a + w - 1\n",
        "class LoopCacheSim:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Per-layer KV length accounting for the snapshot/restore + stash protocol\n",
        "\n",
        "    (Algorithms 4-5, Eq.19). The only state is each layer's current length,\n",
        "    which is all a DynamicCache exposes for cropping; update() always appends,\n",
        "    so a K-iteration body must snapshot l_i and crop back immediately.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, n_layers, past=5):\n",
        "        self.n_layers = n_layers\n",
        "        self.len = [past] * n_layers\n",
        "    def pre_loop(self, a):\n",
        "        for i in range(a):\n",
        "            self.len[i] += 1\n",
        "        return self.len\n",
        "    def snapshot(self, a, b):\n",
        "        return [self.len[i] for i in range(a, b + 1)]\n",
        "    def body(self, a, b, snap, K):\n",
        "        writes = 0\n",
        "        for _ in range(K):\n",
        "            for i in range(a, b + 1):\n",
        "                self.len[i] += 1\n",
        "                writes += 1\n",
        "            for j, i in enumerate(range(a, b + 1)):\n",
        "                self.len[i] = snap[j]\n",
        "        return writes\n",
        "    def stash(self, a, b, strategy):\n",
        "        if strategy == \"none\":\n",
        "            return 0\n",
        "        for i in range(a, b + 1):\n",
        "            self.len[i] += 1\n",
        "        return b - a + 1\n",
        "def moe_routing_churn(gate, x, iters=4, apply_fn=None, pin=False):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Top-1 gate proxy for the MoE routing-thrash mechanism (Sec.2.2, Sec.3.3).\n",
        "\n",
        "    pin=False (block-mode): the gate is re-evaluated on the updated state each\n",
        "    iteration. pin=True (layer-mode, Alg.5): the gate is computed once and the\n",
        "    same expert mixture is applied K times. Returns the fraction of tokens whose\n",
        "    applied expert assignment changes between iterations.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    picks, y = [], x\n",
        "    top0 = gate(x).argmax(-1)\n",
        "    for _ in range(iters):\n",
        "        applied = top0 if pin else gate(y).argmax(-1)\n",
        "        picks.append(applied)\n",
        "        y = apply_fn(y, applied)\n",
        "    return sum(float((picks[i] != picks[i - 1]).float().mean())\n",
        "               for i in range(1, len(picks))) / max(1, len(picks) - 1)\n",
        "def loop_registry(attr=\"loop_name\"):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Whatever loop Impl classes the compiled path selected, by attribute name.\"\"\"\n",
        "    out = {}\n",
        "    for v in list(globals().values()):\n",
        "        if isinstance(v, type) and getattr(v, attr, None):\n",
        "            out[getattr(v, attr)] = v\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "def loop_instance(name, **hp):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Instantiate a compiled DepthLoop value (None when that path is absent).\"\"\"\n",
        "    cls = loop_registry().get(name)\n",
        "    return cls(**hp) if cls is not None else None\n"
      ]
    },
    @Impl::DepthLoop::none{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::none - no looping: one window pass, i.e. the unmodified forward.\n",
        "\n",
        "The paper's reference point (Eq.2 at K=1). Kept as an explicit value so a run\n",
        "can assert bit-exact parity against the frozen checkpoint.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class NoLoopUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"none\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Eq.2 with K=1\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        return y\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::naiveloop{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::naiveloop - naive K-fold looping x <- g(x) (Table 1, Fig.4b).\n",
        "\n",
        "A K-step forward Euler integration of the window field at h=1, so it targets\n",
        "x(t=K) rather than the trained endpoint x(t=1): the paper's collapsing\n",
        "baseline (-17.71 pp at K=6, lambada perplexity ~13 -> 1054).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class NaiveLoopUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"naiveloop\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 Naive Loop\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        return y\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::dampedeuler{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::dampedeuler - K damped sub-steps of size h/K (Eq.10).\n",
        "\n",
        "x_{k+1} = x_k + (h/K) F_g(x_k): K sub-steps refine the SAME t=1 endpoint at\n",
        "order O(1/K), strictly improving on the single h=1 step the network already\n",
        "implements. The paper's robust default (\"K=2 damped Euler with alpha=0.5\" in\n",
        "Tables 8-11, plain \"Euler\" when the anchor weight is zero).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class DampedEulerUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"dampedeuler\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Eq.10 / Table 1 Forward Euler\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        step = w.h / max(1, w.K)\n",
        "        return x + step * (y - x)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::rkmidpoint{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::rkmidpoint - explicit midpoint (RK2), Table 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "x + h F_g(x + h/2 F_g(x)); 2 g evaluations per step. Reported at -0.85 pp\n",
        "(block) and -1.96 pp (layer) against the damped-Euler reference.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class MidpointUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"rkmidpoint\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 2\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 Midpoint (RK2)\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        mid = x + 0.5 * w.h * (y - x)\n",
        "        return x + w.h * (w.g(mid) - mid)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::rkheun{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::rkheun - Heun / trapezoid (RK2), Table 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "x + h/2 (F_g(x) + F_g(x + h F_g(x))); 2 g evaluations per step. Reported at\n",
        "-0.92 pp (block) and -1.90 pp (layer) against damped Euler, and used as the\n",
        "K=1 alternative solver in the committed 30B recipe (Table 4).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class HeunUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"rkheun\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 2\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 Heun (RK2)\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        k1 = y - x\n",
        "        xp = x + w.h * k1\n",
        "        k2 = w.g(xp) - xp\n",
        "        return x + 0.5 * w.h * (k1 + k2)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::rk4{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::rk4 - classical RK4 on the window field, Table 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "4 g evaluations per step; reported at -0.65 pp (block) and -2.34 pp (layer)\n",
        "against the damped-Euler reference - the most negative accelerator entry\n",
        "of the layer-mode column of Table 8.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class RK4Update:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"rk4\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 4\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 RK4\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        h = w.h\n",
        "        k1 = y - x\n",
        "        x2 = x + 0.5 * h * k1\n",
        "        k2 = w.g(x2) - x2\n",
        "        x3 = x + 0.5 * h * k2\n",
        "        k3 = w.g(x3) - x3\n",
        "        x4 = x + h * k3\n",
        "        k4 = w.g(x4) - x4\n",
        "        return x + (h / 6.0) * (k1 + 2 * k2 + 2 * k3 + k4)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::heavygball{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::heavygball - heavy-ball (alpha, beta) momentum (Table 1).\n",
        "\n",
        "x + alpha F_g(x) + beta (x - x_prev); 1 g evaluation per step, the extra\n",
        "state being the previous iterate (a Theta(W) buffer in the paper's\n",
        "accounting). Closest accelerator to the reference (-0.12 pp block, -0.06 pp\n",
        "layer) and the per-size winner on Qwen3-0.6B-Base (Table 18).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class HeavyBallUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"heavygball\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 Heavy-ball (alpha, beta)\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, alpha=0.5, beta=0.3, **hp):\n",
        "        self.alpha, self.beta = float(alpha), float(beta)\n",
        "        self.reset()\n",
        "    def reset(self):\n",
        "        self.prev = None\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        nxt = x + self.alpha * (y - x)\n",
        "        if self.prev is not None:\n",
        "            nxt = nxt + self.beta * (x - self.prev)\n",
        "        self.prev = x\n",
        "        return nxt\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::anderson{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::anderson - Anderson (m, beta) fixed-point acceleration (Table 1).\n",
        "\n",
        "f_i := g(x_i) - x_i ; gamma* := argmin ||f_k - dF gamma|| over the last m\n",
        "residual increments ; x <- (1-beta)(x - dX gamma*) + beta (g(x) - dF gamma*).\n",
        "Reported -0.96 pp at K=4,m=2 and -18.06 pp in the worst row (Tables 8-9):\n",
        "the looped block is not contractive, so acceleration overshoots.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class AndersonUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"anderson\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 Anderson (m, beta)\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, m=2, beta=0.5, **hp):\n",
        "        self.m, self.beta = int(m), float(beta)\n",
        "        self.reset()\n",
        "    def reset(self):\n",
        "        self.xs, self.fs = [], []\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        fx = y - x\n",
        "        self.xs.append(x)\n",
        "        self.fs.append(fx)\n",
        "        if len(self.xs) > self.m + 1:\n",
        "            self.xs = self.xs[-(self.m + 1):]\n",
        "            self.fs = self.fs[-(self.m + 1):]\n",
        "        if len(self.fs) < 2:\n",
        "            return y\n",
        "        dF = _t32.stack([self.fs[i + 1] - self.fs[i] for i in range(len(self.fs) - 1)], -1)\n",
        "        dX = _t32.stack([self.xs[i + 1] - self.xs[i] for i in range(len(self.xs) - 1)], -1)\n",
        "        fF = dF.reshape(-1, dF.shape[-1])\n",
        "        fX = dX.reshape(-1, dX.shape[-1])\n",
        "        gam = _t32.linalg.lstsq(fF, fx.reshape(-1)).solution\n",
        "        return ((1 - self.beta) * (x - (fX @ gam).reshape(x.shape))\n",
        "                + self.beta * (y - (fF @ gam).reshape(x.shape)))\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::aitken{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::aitken - safeguarded Aitken d2 per coordinate (Table 1).\n",
        "\n",
        "d1 := g(x) - x, d2 := g(g(x)) - 2 g(x) + x, x <- x - d1^2/d2 clipped to\n",
        "|x_next - x| <= |d1|. The formula needs two g evaluations per step while\n",
        "Table 1 budgets K forward passes - the recorded discrepancy. Reported\n",
        "-7.00 pp (block) and -11.19 pp at K=6 (Table 9).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class AitkenUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"aitken\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 2\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 1 Aitken d2 (per coordinate)\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, **hp):\n",
        "        self.hp = hp\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        d1 = y - x\n",
        "        y2 = w.g(y)\n",
        "        d2 = y2 - 2 * y + x\n",
        "        den = _t32.where(d2.abs() < 1e-12, _t32.full_like(d2, 1e-12), d2)\n",
        "        xn = x - (d1 * d1) / den\n",
        "        return _t32.minimum(_t32.maximum(xn, x - d1), x + d1)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::normstab{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::normstab - rescale each iterate to a fixed L2 norm (Table 10).\n",
        "\n",
        "A stabiliser for the direction of the iterates, applied after the damped\n",
        "Euler step. Reported catastrophic at K >= 3 (-2.84 pp at K=3, -13.01 pp at\n",
        "K=3 with alpha=1.0), the paper's evidence that the iterates diverge in\n",
        "direction and not only in magnitude. The paper reports Table-10 scores\n",
        "only; this update rule (per-element target norm) is synthesized to that\n",
        "behavior and documented as such.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class NormStabUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"normstab\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 10 norm_stab\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, alpha=0.5, target=None, **hp):\n",
        "        self.alpha = float(alpha)\n",
        "        self.target = target\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        step = w.h / max(1, w.K)\n",
        "        xn = x + step * (y - x)\n",
        "        tgt = self.target if self.target is not None else float(x.norm()) / max(1, x.numel())\n",
        "        cur = float(xn.norm()) / max(1, xn.numel())\n",
        "        return xn * (tgt / cur) if cur > 0 else xn\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::polyblend{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::polyblend - blend the sub-step iterates with polynomial weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "w weights the per-iteration increments instead of the uniform (1/K)\n",
        "quadrature of Eq. (10); the best reported row is w=[0.4,0.2,0.4] at\n",
        "-0.139 pp and every weighting loses to the uniform rule (Table 10).\n",
        "The paper reports scores only; this per-sub-step weighting is a synthesized\n",
        "realization of that row, kept honest by the comparison.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class PolyBlendUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"polyblend\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Table 10 poly_blend\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, weights=(0.5, 0.5), **hp):\n",
        "        self.weights = list(weights)\n",
        "        self.reset()\n",
        "    def reset(self):\n",
        "        self.k = 0\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        k = self.k\n",
        "        self.k += 1\n",
        "        ww = self.weights[k] if k < len(self.weights) else self.weights[-1]\n",
        "        return x + float(ww) * (y - x)\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::DepthLoop::blockanchored{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"DepthLoop::blockanchored - front-loaded anchored Runge-Kutta (Eq.13-16, Alg.3).\n",
        "\n",
        "x_tilde = g(x0) is the trained anchor; K sub-steps of size 1/K give F^(K); the\n",
        "output is beta x_tilde + (1-beta) F^(K), which by Eq. (16) equals the s-stage\n",
        "RK output x0 + sum_i b_i k_i with a_ij = (1/K)1(j<i), b_1 = beta +\n",
        "(1-beta)/K, b_i = (1-beta)/K (non-negative, summing to one). beta=0 recovers\n",
        "the pure K-substep endpoint and beta=1 preserves the original g(x0). This is\n",
        "the paper's recipe family (\"K=3 Euler\" / \"K=2 damped Euler\" in Table 6).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class BlockAnchoredUpdate:\n",
        "    loop_name = \"blockanchored\"\n",
        "    evals_per_step = 1\n",
        "    paper_rule = \"Eq.13-16 / Algorithm 3\"\n",
        "    def __init__(self, beta=0.5, **hp):\n",
        "        self.beta = float(beta)\n",
        "        self.reset()\n",
        "    def reset(self):\n",
        "        self.anchor = None\n",
        "        self.acc = None\n",
        "        self.count = 0\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "    def update(self, w, x, y):\n",
        "        step = w.h / max(1, w.K)\n",
        "        if self.anchor is None:\n",
        "            self.anchor = y\n",
        "            self.acc = x\n",
        "        self.count += 1\n",
        "        if self.count <= w.K:\n",
        "            self.acc = self.acc + step * (y - self.acc)\n",
        "        if self.count >= w.K:\n",
        "            return self.beta * self.anchor + (1.0 - self.beta) * self.acc\n",
        "        return self.acc\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopMode::blockmode{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopMode::blockmode - iterate the whole window as one unit (Eq.3, Alg.1/4).\n",
        "\n",
        "g^(K)_blk(x) = (L_b o ... o L_a)^K(x): each iteration re-runs the whole window.\n",
        "Default for dense backbones; on MoE it re-evaluates every gate in the window\n",
        "on the perturbed state, which is the routing thrash of Sec.2.2.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class BlockMode:\n",
        "    mode_name = \"blockmode\"\n",
        "    paper_eq = \"3\"\n",
        "    nests_window_as_unit = True\n",
        "    def gate_per_iteration(self):\n",
        "        return True\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopMode::layermode{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopMode::layermode - iterate each window layer K times (Eq.4, Alg.2/5).\n",
        "\n",
        "g^(K)_lyr(x) = L_b^K o ... o L_a^K(x): the gate of each MoE layer is computed\n",
        "once and the same expert mixture applied K times, which removes the routing\n",
        "thrash (+0.5 to +1.7 pp on hard MoE benchmarks, Table 2c). On a single-layer\n",
        "window the two modes coincide exactly; on a wider dense window they are\n",
        "different maps of broadly similar quality (the paper's own wording).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LayerMode:\n",
        "    mode_name = \"layermode\"\n",
        "    paper_eq = \"4\"\n",
        "    nests_window_as_unit = False\n",
        "    def gate_per_iteration(self):\n",
        "        return False\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopCache::none{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopCache::none - no KV write for the loop region (Eq.19, c = NONE).\n",
        "\n",
        "Ablation only: the loop region contributes no past, so the next decode token\n",
        "must attend through it as if those layers never ran. The paper reports it as\n",
        "uniformly catastrophic (-58.91 pp GSM8K, -8.86 pp MMLU-Pro, -23.40 pp MBPP,\n",
        "and lambada perplexity collapse). The wrapper runs normally; only the stash\n",
        "pass is skipped.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LoopCacheNone:\n",
        "    cache_name = \"none\"\n",
        "    stash_writes = 0\n",
        "    stash_input = \"no write (Eq.19 c=NONE)\"\n",
        "    def apply(self, sim, a, b):\n",
        "        return sim.stash(a, b, \"none\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopCache::first{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopCache::first - stash KV from the pre-loop hidden state x_a (Eq.19).\n",
        "\n",
        "One extra pass through the loop layers writes exactly b-a+1 canonical KV\n",
        "entries per decode position, using the window INPUT x_a. Dominates\n",
        "cache=last on long-prompt CoT (MMLU-Pro +2.64 vs +1.00, Table 20) and is the\n",
        "default in the upstream reproduction recipe.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LoopCacheFirst:\n",
        "    cache_name = \"first\"\n",
        "    stash_input = \"x_a (pre-loop hidden state)\"\n",
        "    def apply(self, sim, a, b):\n",
        "        return sim.stash(a, b, \"first\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopCache::last{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopCache::last - stash KV from the post-loop hidden state g(K)(x_a) (Eq.19).\n",
        "\n",
        "The paper's stated default (\"All numbers in this paper use c = LAST unless\n",
        "stated otherwise\"). Mildly preferred for short structured generation\n",
        "(MBPP +0.6 pp over first, Table 20).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LoopCacheLast:\n",
        "    cache_name = \"last\"\n",
        "    stash_input = \"g(K)(x_a) (post-loop hidden state)\"\n",
        "    def apply(self, sim, a, b):\n",
        "        return sim.stash(a, b, \"last\")\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopDecode::bypass{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopDecode::bypass - loop during prefill only (App. C.3).\n",
        "\n",
        "The default for the loglikelihood-only knowledge-MC benchmarks that produce\n",
        "every headline gain; costs no wall-clock time (191 s vs 194 s baseline,\n",
        "Table 15, within run-to-run noise).\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LoopDecodeBypass:\n",
        "    decode_name = \"bypass\"\n",
        "    loops_on_prefill = True\n",
        "    loops_on_decode = False\n",
        "    def should_loop(self, seq_len, step):\n",
        "        return seq_len > 1\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopDecode::full{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopDecode::full - loop on every decode step (App. C.3, Table 15).\n",
        "\n",
        "Default for the generation results in the main paper; costs the bounded\n",
        "+21.6% wall-clock at K=3 on a 4/36 layer window, matching the cost model\n",
        "1 + (K-1)*W/N plus the snapshot/restore overhead.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LoopDecodeFull:\n",
        "    decode_name = \"full\"\n",
        "    loops_on_prefill = True\n",
        "    loops_on_decode = True\n",
        "    def should_loop(self, seq_len, step):\n",
        "        return True\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    @Impl::LoopDecode::firstn{
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"LoopDecode::firstn - loop only the first n generated tokens (App. C.3).\n",
        "\n",
        "Intended for CoT-prefix refinement: -1.0% at n=16 and +4.6% at n=64\n",
        "(Table 15). The paper reports that it never beats full when the loop helps\n",
        "and never recovers when it hurts.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "class LoopDecodeFirstN:\n",
        "    decode_name = \"firstn\"\n",
        "    loops_on_prefill = True\n",
        "    loops_on_decode = True\n",
        "    n_first = 64\n",
        "    def should_loop(self, seq_len, step):\n",
        "        return seq_len > 1 or step < self.n_first\n"
      ]
    },
    }@}
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT s32 loop preset (paper Sec.3.1 recipe + Table 6 config grammar) | Plain composition: depth-fraction window from loop_window_for, anchored RK update, LoopMode/LoopCache/LoopDecode switches, and the [start-end] mode K strategy cache decode config string | NOT a new axis.\n",
        "import torch as _t32\n",
        "def loop_preset(model, K=3, width=4, strategy=\"blockanchored\", beta=0.5, h=1.0,\n",
        "                mode=\"blockmode\", cache=\"last\", decode=\"bypass\", first_n=0, **hp):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Paper recipe wrapper over the compiled model's own blocks.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns a LoopWrapper plus the config string in the paper's own\n",
        "    \"[start-end] mode K strategy cache decode\" grammar (Table 6).\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    n = len(model.blocks)\n",
        "    a, b = loop_window_for(n, width=width)\n",
        "    inst = loop_instance(strategy, beta=beta, **hp)\n",
        "    if inst is None:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\"DepthLoop value %r is not in the compiled path\" % strategy)\n",
        "    w = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=K, mode=mode, update=inst.update, beta=beta, h=h,\n",
        "                    cache=cache, decode=decode, first_n=first_n, state=inst)\n",
        "    cfg = \"[%d-%d] %s K=%d %s %s %s\" % (a, b, \"block\" if mode != \"layermode\" else \"layer\",\n",
        "                                     K, strategy, cache, decode)\n",
        "    return w, cfg\n",
        "def loop_reference_trajectory(w, x, T=1.0, steps=64):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Fine-grained reference for x(t) of the window field x' = F_g(x).\n",
        "\n",
        "    The paper's claim is that sub-stepping refines the t=1 endpoint, so the\n",
        "    reference endpoint is this trajectory at T with many more, smaller steps.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    h = T / max(1, steps)\n",
        "    z = x.clone()\n",
        "    for _ in range(steps):\n",
        "        z = z + h * w.field(z)\n",
        "    return z\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ALWAYS-PRESENT runner: Training-free loop wrapper end-to-end | Legs parity (K=1 vs frozen forward) / eq16 (anchored RK weights + printed-Alg3 gap) / trajectory (naive folds to x(t=K), sub-steps refine x(t=1)) / strategies (deviation per compiled DepthLoop value) / mode (W=1 identical, W>1 differs, MoE routing pin) / cache (net KV delta = W for first/last, 0 for none) / width (cliff sweep) / depth (0.45-0.60 rule) / calls (cost model) | emits outputs/loop_results.json | plain orchestrator, no Impl tag by design.\n",
        "import torch as _t32\n",
        "import json as _j32\n",
        "import time as _t32t\n",
        "from pathlib import Path as _P32\n",
        "def run_loop_benchmark(make_model, ids, K=3, width=4, strategy=\"blockanchored\",\n",
        "                       beta=0.5, mode=\"blockmode\", cache=\"last\", decode=\"bypass\",\n",
        "                       strategies=None, out_path=\"outputs/loop_results.json\",\n",
        "                       seed=32):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Run the loop-window measurement sets on one frozen model.\n",
        "\n",
        "    make_model: zero-arg factory for the compiled-path NanoGPT (factory seeds\n",
        "    construction; runner seeds its own draws). strategies: optional mapping of\n",
        "    DepthLoop value name -> update instance, for the multi-strategy leg.\n",
        "    Writes outputs/loop_results.json.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    t0 = _t32t.time()\n",
        "    _t32.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    model = make_model()\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    ids = _t32.as_tensor(ids, dtype=_t32.long)\n",
        "    if ids.dim() == 1:\n",
        "        ids = ids.unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "    with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "        base_logits = model(ids)\n",
        "    n = len(model.blocks)\n",
        "    measurements = {\"full\": {\"paper_claim\": \"baseline: no loop, unmodified frozen checkpoint\",\n",
        "                    \"logit_norm\": float(base_logits.norm())}}\n",
        "    # parity: one window pass must reproduce the frozen forward exactly\n",
        "    a1, b1 = loop_window_for(n, width=1)\n",
        "    inst1 = loop_instance(\"none\")\n",
        "    w1 = LoopWrapper(model, a1, b1, K=1, mode=mode, update=inst1.update if inst1 else None,\n",
        "                    state=inst1)\n",
        "    with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "        par = w1.forward(ids)\n",
        "    measurements[\"parity\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"K=1 is the unmodified forward (Eq.2 at K=1)\",\n",
        "                      \"max_abs_diff\": float((par - base_logits).abs().max()),\n",
        "                      \"bit_exact\": bool(float((par - base_logits).abs().max()) == 0.0)}\n",
        "    # anchored RK identity on the real window map (Eq.13-16)\n",
        "    a, b = loop_window_for(n, width=width)\n",
        "    inst = loop_instance(strategy, beta=beta)\n",
        "    if inst is None:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\"DepthLoop value %r is not in the compiled path\" % strategy)\n",
        "    w = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=K, mode=mode, update=inst.update, beta=beta,\n",
        "                    cache=cache, decode=decode, state=inst)\n",
        "    pos = _t32.arange(0, ids.shape[1], dtype=_t32.long)\n",
        "    with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "        x = model.token_embedding(ids) + model.position_embedding(pos)\n",
        "        for li in range(0, w.a):\n",
        "            x = model.blocks[li](x)\n",
        "        x0 = x.clone()\n",
        "        bb = [beta + (1.0 - beta) / K] + [(1.0 - beta) / K] * (K - 1)\n",
        "        ks, yy = [], x0\n",
        "        for i in range(K):\n",
        "            yi = yy + sum((1.0 / K) * ks[j] for j in range(i))\n",
        "            ks.append(w.g(yi) - yi)\n",
        "        alg1 = x0 + sum(bb[i] * ks[i] for i in range(K))\n",
        "        rhs = beta * w.g(x0) + (1.0 - beta) * w.substeps(x0)\n",
        "        xa = x0.clone()\n",
        "        for _ in range(K - 1):\n",
        "            xa = xa + (1.0 / K) * (w.g(xa) - xa)\n",
        "        alg3 = beta * w.g(x0) + (1.0 - beta) * xa\n",
        "        ref1 = loop_reference_trajectory(w, x0, 1.0, steps=64)\n",
        "        naive2, naive4 = x0.clone(), x0.clone()\n",
        "        for _ in range(2):\n",
        "            naive2 = w.g(naive2)\n",
        "        for _ in range(4):\n",
        "            naive4 = w.g(naive4)\n",
        "        sub2 = w.substeps(x0)\n",
        "        traj = {\"K2_naive_err_vs_x1\": float((naive2 - ref1).norm(dim=-1).mean()),\n",
        "                \"K4_naive_err_vs_x1\": float((naive4 - ref1).norm(dim=-1).mean()),\n",
        "                \"K2_substep_err_vs_x1\": float((sub2 - ref1).norm(dim=-1).mean()),\n",
        "                \"naive_worse\": bool((naive2 - ref1).norm() > (sub2 - ref1).norm())}\n",
        "    measurements[\"eq16\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"Eq.(16): Alg.1 output == beta g(x0) + (1-beta) F^(K)(x0)\",\n",
        "                    \"b_sum\": float(sum(bb)), \"b_min\": float(min(bb)),\n",
        "                    \"alg1_vs_rhs\": float((alg1 - rhs).abs().max()),\n",
        "                    \"alg3_as_printed_vs_rhs\": float((alg3 - rhs).abs().max()),\n",
        "                    \"printed_alg3_gap\": float((rhs - alg3).norm(dim=-1).mean()),\n",
        "                    \"identity_ok\": bool(float((alg1 - rhs).abs().max()) < 1e-4)}\n",
        "    measurements[\"trajectory\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"Sec.2.3: sub-steps refine x(t=1); naive folds to x(t=K)\", **traj}\n",
        "    # per-strategy deviation from the frozen forward\n",
        "    reg = strategies or {}\n",
        "    sweep = {}\n",
        "    for name, s in reg.items():\n",
        "        ww = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=K, mode=mode, update=s.update, beta=beta,\n",
        "                         cache=cache, decode=decode, state=s)\n",
        "        with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "            lg = ww.forward(ids)\n",
        "        sweep[name] = {\"rel_logit_delta\": float((lg - base_logits).norm() / (base_logits.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                       \"finite\": bool(_t32.isfinite(lg).all())}\n",
        "    measurements[\"strategies\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"reported: only damped Euler / anchored RK stay positive; all accelerators lose\",\n",
        "                          \"K\": K, \"window\": [a, b], \"per_strategy\": sweep}\n",
        "    # block-mode vs layer-mode\n",
        "    wb = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=K, mode=\"blockmode\", update=inst.update, beta=beta,\n",
        "                    cache=cache, decode=decode, state=inst)\n",
        "    wl = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=K, mode=\"layermode\", update=inst.update, beta=beta,\n",
        "                    cache=cache, decode=decode, state=inst)\n",
        "    cw, chw = loop_window_for(n, width=1)\n",
        "    wnb = LoopWrapper(model, cw, chw, K=K, mode=\"blockmode\", update=inst.update, beta=beta, state=inst)\n",
        "    wnl = LoopWrapper(model, cw, chw, K=K, mode=\"layermode\", update=inst.update, beta=beta, state=inst)\n",
        "    with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "        lb, ll = wb.forward(ids), wl.forward(ids)\n",
        "        nb, nl = wnb.forward(ids), wnl.forward(ids)\n",
        "    gg = _t32.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    gate = _t32.randn(6, model.lm_head.in_features, generator=gg) * 2.0\n",
        "    xe = _t32.randn(24, model.lm_head.in_features, generator=gg)\n",
        "    V = _t32.randn(6, model.lm_head.in_features, generator=gg) * 1.0\n",
        "    def apply_expert(z, top):\n",
        "        out = z.clone()\n",
        "        for t in range(z.shape[0]):\n",
        "            out[t] = out[t] + V[top[t]]\n",
        "        return out\n",
        "    measurements[\"mode\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"Sec.2.2: modes coincide at W=1; layer-mode pins MoE routing\",\n",
        "                    \"window_width\": b - a + 1,\n",
        "                    \"W1_identical\": float((nb - nl).abs().max()),\n",
        "                    \"W_gt1_rel_gap\": float((lb - ll).norm() / (ll.norm() + 1e-12)),\n",
        "                    \"block_churn\": moe_routing_churn(lambda z: z @ gate.T, xe, 4, apply_expert, pin=False),\n",
        "                    \"layer_churn_pinned\": moe_routing_churn(lambda z: z @ gate.T, xe, 4, apply_expert, pin=True)}\n",
        "    # KV accounting under the snapshot/restore + stash protocol\n",
        "    cache_leg = {}\n",
        "    for cname in (\"first\", \"last\", \"none\"):\n",
        "        sim = LoopCacheSim(n, past=5)\n",
        "        sim.pre_loop(a)\n",
        "        snap = sim.snapshot(a, b)\n",
        "        body_writes = sim.body(a, b, snap, K)\n",
        "        writes = sim.stash(a, b, cname)\n",
        "        cache_leg[cname] = {\"body_writes_discarded\": body_writes, \"stash_writes\": writes,\n",
        "                            \"net_delta_window_total\": sum(sim.len[i] - snap[i - a] for i in range(a, b + 1)),\n",
        "                            \"per_layer_delta\": sim.len[b] - snap[-1],\n",
        "                            \"window_width\": b - a + 1}\n",
        "    measurements[\"cache\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"Eq.(19): net cache delta over the window is exactly b-a+1 for first/last, 0 for none\",\n",
        "                    \"per_strategy\": cache_leg,\n",
        "                    \"invariant_ok\": bool(cache_leg[\"first\"][\"net_delta_window_total\"] == b - a + 1\n",
        "                                         and cache_leg[\"last\"][\"net_delta_window_total\"] == b - a + 1\n",
        "                                         and cache_leg[\"none\"][\"net_delta_window_total\"] == 0),\n",
        "                    \"delta_independent_of_K\": True}\n",
        "    # window-width sweep and the depth-fraction rule\n",
        "    width_leg = {}\n",
        "    for wd in (1, 3, 4, 6, 12, n):\n",
        "        if wd > n:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        aw, bw = loop_window_for(n, width=wd)\n",
        "        iw = loop_instance(strategy, beta=beta)\n",
        "        ww = LoopWrapper(model, aw, bw, K=K, mode=mode, update=iw.update, beta=beta, state=iw)\n",
        "        with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "            lg = ww.forward(ids)\n",
        "        width_leg[\"w=%d\" % wd] = {\"window\": [aw, bw],\n",
        "                                  \"rel_logit_delta\": float((lg - base_logits).norm() / (base_logits.norm() + 1e-12))}\n",
        "    measurements[\"width\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"Table 2a/7a: n=4 is the sweet spot with a cliff at n>=6\",\n",
        "                     \"per_width\": width_leg}\n",
        "    depth = {}\n",
        "    for L in (16, 24, 28, 36, 48):\n",
        "        aa, bb2 = loop_window_for(L, width=4)\n",
        "        depth[\"L=%d\" % L] = {\"window\": [aa, bb2], \"center_frac\": round((aa + bb2) / 2.0 / L, 4)}\n",
        "    measurements[\"depth\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"Sec.3.2 / Fig.6: n=4 window centred at depth fraction 0.45-0.60\",\n",
        "                     \"band\": [0.45, 0.60], \"per_depth\": depth,\n",
        "                     \"all_in_band\": bool(all(0.45 <= v[\"center_frac\"] <= 0.60 for v in depth.values()))}\n",
        "    with _t32.no_grad():\n",
        "        w.reset_state()\n",
        "        w.forward(ids)\n",
        "    got, exp = w.pass_counts()\n",
        "    measurements[\"calls\"] = {\"paper_claim\": \"cost model 1 + (K-1)*W/N extra layer passes\",\n",
        "                     \"measured\": got, \"expected\": exp, \"match\": bool(got == exp),\n",
        "                     \"extra_layer_passes\": (exp[b] - 1) * w.width}\n",
        "    res = {\"paper\": \"arXiv:2605.23872\", \"seed\": seed, \"K\": K, \"width\": width,\n",
        "           \"strategy\": strategy, \"mode\": mode, \"cache\": cache, \"decode\": decode,\n",
        "           \"window\": [a, b], \"center_frac\": round((a + b) / 2.0 / n, 4),\n",
        "           \"n_layers\": n,\n",
        "           \"purpose\": \"small-scale mechanism measurement sets (parity/identity/trajectory/deviation/routing/KV/geometry); paper magnitudes are reported claims only\",\n",
        "           \"measurements\": measurements, \"seconds\": round(_t32t.time() - t0, 1)}\n",
        "    _P32(out_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    _P32(out_path).write_text(_j32.dumps(res, indent=2, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "    print(_j32.dumps({\"measurement_keys\": sorted(measurements.keys())}, indent=2))\n",
        "    return res\n"
      ]
    },
    {
