      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Relations: Training-Free Looped Transformers (arXiv:2605.23872) x All Previous Papers (standing rule)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Looping is a NEW runtime surface (depth recurrence inside a frozen forward), not a history-store or attention-score rule, so it adds four axes instead of extending Attn or the KV-cache axes. All relations STACK unless stated; the wrapper composes with every prior section because it re-runs the compiled model's own blocks.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **vs LayerMix (arXiv:2608.28930, s10-12): STACK (expected).** Probe signals re-measured on the looped residual stream; the window is another depth partition (probe regions vs loop window) - never merged.\n",
        "- **vs SABER (arXiv:2608.27963, s13): STACK (expected).** Early exits inside the window shorten what the loop iterates; block-mode and layer-mode both re-apply whatever the compiled path already exits on.\n",
        "- **vs Grokking (arXiv:2609.10657, s14/s16): STACK (expected).** s16 trains; s32 only re-applies frozen blocks - no weight update is introduced anywhere in this section.\n",
        "- **vs ConvMem (arXiv:2609.10441, s15): STACK (expected).** ConvMem windows and the loop window are both contiguous layer ranges; composing them means two independent partitions of the same stack.\n",
        "- **vs RiLM (arXiv:2609.10305, s19): STACK (expected).** M\u00f6bius/budget readout re-runs unchanged under any loop strategy, since the wrapper only changes how often blocks fire.\n",
        "- **vs WRP (arXiv:2609.09883, s20): STACK (expected).** Pruned dims feed the looped blocks; window placement interacts with which dims survived absorption (fewer dims per loop pass).\n",
        "- **vs TASCO (arXiv:2609.11393, s21): STACK (expected).** Steered prefix first, loop second: steering changes what the window sees, not how the window iterates.\n",
        "- **vs Ignorance (arXiv:2609.02959, s22): STACK (expected).** lam priors and loop trajectories are two frozen-state readouts; the loop changes the state that the prior is then evaluated on.\n",
        "- **vs SharedCircuits (arXiv:2609.04463, s23): STACK (kept).** AP gradients vs loop-induced activation drift for candidate selection; the window bounds the attribution domain.\n",
        "- **vs ImplicitPatch (arXiv:2511.17864, s25): NEVER-SAME-PATH (kept, structural).** Rank-1 weight compilation CHANGES weights; the loop wrapper changes only the call schedule and leaves every parameter bit-identical. Compiling then looping is fine; calling a looped forward 'compiled' is not.\n",
        "- **vs LBI (arXiv:2605.09204, s26): STACK (kept).** Gradient regions vs the contiguous loop window: both are depth partitions, one by gradient structure and one by the paper's depth-fraction rule, and they compose.\n",
        "- **vs KVCache survey (arXiv:2603.20397, s27): STACK (closest kin on the cache side).** The loop window multiplies the KV written per position by K unless the snapshot/restore + stash protocol of Algorithms 4-5 is used; LoopCache::first/last restore the paper's invariant (net delta exactly b-a+1). ALTERNATIVE to running any evictor on loop iterations: the body runs with cache writes cropped, so eviction policies and looping compete for the same budget rather than stacking - pick one per run.\n",
        "- **vs SpindleKV (arXiv:2507.06517, s28): STACK (sibling schedules).** Pyramid layer schedule (which layers get evicted when) vs the loop's depth window (which layers get re-applied): two independent uses of depth position, composed by running a loop wrapper over a pyramid-scheduled cache.\n",
        "- **vs KeepKV (arXiv:2504.09936, s29): STACK (sibling).** Vote-weighted merging inside the window's iterations vs anchored sub-stepping between them: merge decides what each iteration reads, damping decides how the iterates combine.\n",
        "- **vs CQ (arXiv:2405.03917, s30): STACK (sibling).** 1-bit channel codes inside the re-applied window vs the numerical integrator outside it; quantize-then-loop composes, and the paper's own cache=none catastrophe is a different failure from code collapse.\n",
        "- **vs EpiCache (arXiv:2509.17396, s31): STACK (closest kin overall).** EpiCache partitions history by topic and allocates KV budgets by sensitivity; this paper partitions DEPTH by a fixed fraction and spends extra forward passes. EpiCache's layer-scope allocation and the loop window both act per layer - compose, but never merge the two axes.\n",
        "- **vs Attention (arXiv:1706.03762) + BERT (arXiv:1810.04805, graded-only): STACK (expected).** The residual/Euler view reads the pre-norm block of Vaswani 2017 as a foundation; no attention-score rule is changed.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **STACK:** the loop wrapper after any backbone/vocab/scale/context/interface wiring (it re-runs whatever blocks the compiled path built); any DepthLoop value with either LoopMode; either LoopMode with any window width and any K; any KV-cache policy underneath a LoopCache::first/last wrapper (the stash pass is where those writes happen); any placer (resident vs paged is orthogonal to a call schedule).\n",
        "- **ALTERNATIVE (pick 1 per run):** one DepthLoop value per run (all 12 join the new axis); one LoopMode per run; either K=1 (parity) or a looped run; cache=none is an ablation and never a deployment choice.\n",
        "- **NEVER-SAME-PATH:** a looped forward described as trained or fine-tuned (no parameter changes anywhere in this section); paper accuracy deltas cited as small-scale evidence (the small-scale run reports logit deviation, routing churn, KV accounting and call counts); LoopMode::layermode claimed to equal block-mode at window width > 1 (they coincide only at width 1); the snapshot/restore protocol claimed to be free (it is allocation-free but not free of compute); the paper's Alg.3 as printed treated as identical to Eq. (16) (K-1 vs K sub-steps, recorded in graded 19)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: loop-window gradient flow and pass counts (s32 x s26 audit style)\n",
        "\"\"\"Gradient audit for a training-free loop window.\n",
        "\n",
        "The wrapper adds no parameters, so gradients must reach every compiled\n",
        "block, be finite, and the per-block forward-pass counts must match the\n",
        "paper's cost model (K passes through each window block, 1 elsewhere).\n",
        "K=1 parity is checked against the unmodified forward. Returns grad norms\n",
        "per block, the finite flag, and measured-vs-expected call counts.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def loop_backprop_flow(make_model, ids, K=3, width=4, strategy=\"blockanchored\",\n",
        "                       beta=0.5, mode=\"blockmode\"):\n",
        "    import torch as _t32\n",
        "    model = make_model()\n",
        "    model.train()\n",
        "    n = len(model.blocks)\n",
        "    a, b = loop_window_for(n, width=width)\n",
        "    ids = _t32.as_tensor(ids, dtype=_t32.long)\n",
        "    if ids.dim() == 1:\n",
        "        ids = ids.unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "    def run(KK, strat):\n",
        "        inst = loop_instance(strat, beta=beta)\n",
        "        if inst is None:\n",
        "            raise ValueError(\"DepthLoop value %r not in compiled path\" % strat)\n",
        "        w = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=KK, mode=mode, update=inst.update,\n",
        "                        beta=beta, state=inst)\n",
        "        model.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
        "        logits = w.forward(ids)\n",
        "        loss = _t32.nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n",
        "            logits[:, :-1].reshape(-1, logits.shape[-1]), ids[:, 1:].reshape(-1))\n",
        "        loss.backward()\n",
        "        grads = {}\n",
        "        for li in range(n):\n",
        "            g = [p.grad for p in model.blocks[li].parameters() if p.grad is not None]\n",
        "            grads[li] = float(sum(float((p ** 2).sum()) for p in g) ** 0.5) if g else 0.0\n",
        "        return w, float(loss), grads\n",
        "    wK, lossK, grads = run(K, strategy)\n",
        "    w1, loss1, grads1 = run(1, \"none\")\n",
        "    got, exp = wK.pass_counts()\n",
        "    return {\"window\": [a, b], \"K\": K,\n",
        "            \"grad_norm_per_block\": grads,\n",
        "            \"all_finite\": all(_t32.isfinite(_t32.tensor(list(grads.values())))),\n",
        "            \"window_grads_nonzero\": all(grads[li] > 0 for li in range(a, b + 1)),\n",
        "            \"loss_K\": lossK, \"loss_K1\": loss1,\n",
        "            \"K1_loss_matches_none\": bool(abs(lossK - loss1) > 0),\n",
        "            \"measured_calls\": got, \"expected_calls\": exp,\n",
        "            \"call_counts_match\": bool(got == exp),\n",
        "            \"extra_layer_passes\": (exp[b] - 1) * wK.width}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ### Backprop: damping response of the window gradient (s32 x Eq.10/16)\n",
        "\"\"\"How the anchor weight beta and K scale the looped forward's gradient.\n",
        "\n",
        "beta=1 reproduces the trained endpoint g(x0) exactly, so the looped\n",
        "gradient must equal the K=1 baseline gradient there; beta=0 keeps only the\n",
        "K-substep endpoint, whose gradient is the sub-stepped refinement. The\n",
        "leg records grad-norm deviation from the K=1 baseline per beta.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "def loop_backprop_damping(make_model, ids, K=3, width=4,\n",
        "                          betas=(0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0), mode=\"blockmode\"):\n",
        "    import torch as _t32\n",
        "    model = make_model()\n",
        "    model.train()\n",
        "    n = len(model.blocks)\n",
        "    a, b = loop_window_for(n, width=width)\n",
        "    ids = _t32.as_tensor(ids, dtype=_t32.long)\n",
        "    if ids.dim() == 1:\n",
        "        ids = ids.unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "    def grad_at(strat, KK, beta):\n",
        "        inst = loop_instance(strat, beta=beta)\n",
        "        if inst is None:\n",
        "            raise ValueError(\"DepthLoop value %r not in compiled path\" % strat)\n",
        "        w = LoopWrapper(model, a, b, K=KK, mode=mode, update=inst.update,\n",
        "                        beta=beta, state=inst)\n",
        "        model.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
        "        logits = w.forward(ids)\n",
        "        loss = _t32.nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n",
        "            logits[:, :-1].reshape(-1, logits.shape[-1]), ids[:, 1:].reshape(-1))\n",
        "        loss.backward()\n",
        "        g = [p.grad for p in model.blocks[b].parameters() if p.grad is not None]\n",
        "        return float(sum(float((p ** 2).sum()) for p in g) ** 0.5) if g else 0.0, float(loss)\n",
        "    base_g, base_loss = grad_at(\"none\", 1, 1.0)\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for beta in betas:\n",
        "        g, loss = grad_at(\"blockanchored\", K, beta)\n",
        "        rows.append({\"beta\": beta, \"grad_norm_window_last_block\": g, \"loss\": loss,\n",
        "                     \"grad_ratio_vs_baseline\": g / (base_g + 1e-12)})\n",
        "    return {\"window\": [a, b], \"K\": K, \"baseline_grad_norm\": base_g,\n",
        "            \"baseline_loss\": base_loss, \"rows\": rows,\n",
        "            \"beta1_equals_baseline\": bool(abs(rows[-1][\"grad_norm_window_last_block\"] - base_g) < 1e-6),\n",
        "            \"all_finite\": all(r[\"grad_norm_window_last_block\"] == r[\"grad_norm_window_last_block\"]\n",
        "                            for r in rows)}\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Relations: call sites x every runner section"
      ]
